('chunk-192','GHBC-CHUNK-000192','GHBC-C-000192','BALANCED DOOR
A door equipped with double-pivoted hardware so designed as to cause a semicounterbalanced swing action when opening.',2,'2.1','BALANCED DOOR',NULL,129,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000448"]','822b34657a29d217759f8c6bc7dce8a287b27254160b12028870d7d95d9c8387'),
('chunk-193','GHBC-CHUNK-000193','GHBC-C-000193','BALLAST
In roofing, ballast comes in the form of large stones or paver systems or lightweight interlocking paver systems and is used to provide uplift resistance for roofing systems that are not adhered or mechanically attached to the roof deck.',2,'2.1','BALLAST',NULL,129,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000449"]','302d5ac907c771b4ae574d5cbe584adbdd384d7819e36379631898b224f4f186'),
('chunk-194','GHBC-CHUNK-000194','GHBC-C-000194','BARRICADE
A structure that consists of a combination of walls, floor and roof, which is designed to withstand the rapid release of
energy in an explosion and which is fully confined, partially vented or fully vented; or other effective method of shielding from explosive materials by a natural or artificial barrier. Artificial barricade. An artificial mound or revetment a minimum thickness of 3 feet (914 mm). Natural barricade. Natural features of the ground, such as hills, or timber of sufficient density that the surrounding exposures that require protection cannot be seen from the magazine or building containing explosives when the trees are bare of leaves. BASEMENT (for flood loads). The portion of a building having its floor subgrade (below ground level) on all sides.',2,'2.1','BARRICADE',NULL,129,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000450","GHBC-REQ-000451","GHBC-REQ-000452","GHBC-REQ-000453","GHBC-REQ-000454","GHBC-REQ-000455","GHBC-REQ-000456","GHBC-REQ-000457"]','d8ddff4daa32ae57bf5d95c5ae5780239b8dd0b0ad87d14f9e5ca22eb4ad0012'),
('chunk-195','GHBC-CHUNK-000195','GHBC-C-000195','BASEMENT
A storey that is not a storey
above grade plane',2,'2.1','BASEMENT','A storey that is not a storey',130,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000458"]','5271204c7df68c3d83fdf98447dcae2c1fd4711c7eb52f431367a7e4e6245458'),
('chunk-196','GHBC-CHUNK-000196','GHBC-C-000196','BEARING WALL STRUCTURE
A building or other structure in which vertical loads from floors and roofs are primarily supported by walls.',2,'2.1','BEARING WALL STRUCTURE',NULL,130,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000459"]','c6889272b8b8e8cc42643e3043fa4d1185fd162ea54b543fe05857ddb675d8bb'),
('chunk-197','GHBC-CHUNK-000197','GHBC-C-000197','BED JOINT
The horizontal layer of mortar on which a masonry unit is laid.',2,'2.1','BED JOINT',NULL,130,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000460"]','97b4a7834faf155c3e8aff6cc0f99faf7afbd943b61a21d57dc5878516c69a08'),
('chunk-198','GHBC-CHUNK-000198','GHBC-C-000198','BLEACHERS
Tiered seating supported on a dedicated structural system and two or more rows high and is not a building element.',2,'2.1','BLEACHERS',NULL,130,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000461"]','2ef45df922ba8ac2f1a3662d9322f342f74c46771c3e79b62ddc3e4828223397'),
('chunk-199','GHBC-CHUNK-000199','GHBC-C-000199','BOARDING HOUSE
