continuous operation to ensure safety of the structure and occupants.
CROSS-LAMINATED',2,'2.1','CRITICAL CIRCUIT','A circuit that requires',134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000615","GHBC-REQ-000616"]','011b78d9f93b06391547aea745c6d8036b083a6e1b6add4bad71c52c97b78ce4'),
('chunk-256','GHBC-CHUNK-000256','GHBC-C-000256','TIMBER
A prefabricated engineered wood product consisting of not less than three layers of solidsawn timber or structural composite timber where the adjacent layers are cross oriented and bonded with structural adhesive to form a solid wood element.',2,'2.1','TIMBER',NULL,134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000617"]','6a4719f71a0f3c44a4e52d75ee588bac9c1528e51b1d724014645b37477b3e49'),
('chunk-257','GHBC-CHUNK-000257','GHBC-C-000257','CRYOGENIC FLUID
A liquid having a boiling
point lower than -150°F (-101°C) at 14.7 pounds per square inch atmosphere (psia) (an absolute pressure of 101 kPa).',2,'2.1','CRYOGENIC FLUID','A liquid having a boiling',134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000618"]','220a0d88c1edd74d4287f1e8fa21051f7ccb1a5d6107d1c514d3dcffc3189f05'),
('chunk-258','GHBC-CHUNK-000258','GHBC-C-000258','CUSTODIAL CARE
Assistance with day-to-
day living tasks; such as assistance with cooking, taking medication, bathing, using toilet facilities and other tasks of daily living. Custodial care includes persons receiving care who have the ability to respond to emergency situations and evacuate at a slower rate and/or who have mental and psychiatric complications.',2,'2.1','CUSTODIAL CARE','Assistance with day-to-',134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000619","GHBC-REQ-000620"]','96ad8981cf748ae44eed44471b0fd3e3c0ba03b564b07ff043461a8c90e71375'),
('chunk-259','GHBC-CHUNK-000259','GHBC-C-000259','DALLE GLASS
A decorative composite
glazing material made of individual pieces of glass that are embedded in a cast matrix of concrete or epoxy.',2,'2.1','DALLE GLASS','A decorative composite',134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000621"]','17a3e932704cbf4432a354416367704a9952eaa7713d1947198c86b37df2d1d9'),
('chunk-260','GHBC-CHUNK-000260','GHBC-C-000260','DANGEROUS
Any building, structure or portion thereof that meets any of the conditions described below shall be deemed dangerous:
1. The building or structure has collapsed, has partially collapsed, has moved off its foundation or lacks the necessary support of the ground.
2. There exists a significant risk of collapse, detachment or dislodgment of any portion, member, appurtenance or ornamentation of the building or structure under service loads.',2,'2.1','DANGEROUS',NULL,134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000622","GHBC-REQ-000623","GHBC-REQ-000624","GHBC-REQ-000625","GHBC-REQ-000626"]','4ed6e8854afa1e30168c2b6dc51d203df97fd9f0a9974003e24566419da36b0b');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-261','GHBC-CHUNK-000261','GHBC-C-000261','DAY BOX
A portable magazine designed to hold explosive materials constructed in accordance with the requirements for a Type 3 magazine as defined and classified in Part 56 of the Ghana Fire Code.',2,'2.1','DAY BOX',NULL,134,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000627"]','ba41e7692e2e9ffe314198ff7f8a6a799ff2a8559420094eec82547b28cc5a22'),
('chunk-262','GHBC-CHUNK-000262','GHBC-C-000262','DEAD LOAD
The weight of materials of construction incorporated into the building, including but not limited to walls, floors, roofs, ceilings, stairways, built-in partitions, finishes, cladding and other similarly incorporated architectural and structural items, and the weight of fixed service equipment, such as cranes, plumbing stacks and risers, electrical feeders, heating, ventilating and airconditioning systems and automatic sprinkler systems.',2,'2.1','DEAD LOAD',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000628"]','be0480e502c846b5a3aaab5688bfd5e524a51bc0df02d0ac1f9bb22906f579f5'),
('chunk-263','GHBC-CHUNK-000263','GHBC-C-000263','DECORATIVE GLASS
A carved, leaded or Dalle glass or glazing material whose purpose is decorative or artistic, not functional; whose coloring, texture or other design qualities or components cannot be removed without destroying the glazing material and whose surface, or assembly into which it is incorporated, is divided into segments.
DECORATIVE',2,'2.1','DECORATIVE GLASS',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000629","GHBC-REQ-000630"]','4ee88e2927a8ae1b34f201c6f2b9650b3f384d035cacb44b18c38e02f1e1b797'),
('chunk-264','GHBC-CHUNK-000264','GHBC-C-000264','MATERIALS
All materials applied over the building interior finish for decorative, acoustical or other effect including, but not limited to, curtains, draperies, fabrics and streamers; and all other materials utilized for decorative effect including, but not limited to, bulletin boards, artwork, posters, photographs, batting, cloth, cotton, hay, stalks, straw, vines, leaves, trees, moss and similar items, foam plastics and materials containing foam plastics. Decorative materials do not include wall coverings, ceiling coverings, floor coverings, ordinary window shades, interior finish and materials 0.64 mm (0.025 inch) or less in thickness applied directly to and adhering tightly to a substrate.',2,'2.1','MATERIALS',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000631","GHBC-REQ-000632"]','01948ee2c2b4215cbd4d85e73e383ee622c382c3c9a4f8c8e1bc418ae2428454'),
('chunk-265','GHBC-CHUNK-000265','GHBC-C-000265','DEEP FOUNDATION
A deep foundation is a foundation element that does not satisfy the definition of a shallow foundation.',2,'2.1','DEEP FOUNDATION',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000633"]','3a0e7ee4ef8f762cff261240aa6a2a881e366590239b2dad37a00abad89685ee'),
('chunk-266','GHBC-CHUNK-000266','GHBC-C-000266','DEFEND-IN-PLACE
A method of emergency
response that engages building components and trained staff to provide occupant safety during an emergency. Emergency response involves remaining in place, relocating within the building, or both, without evacuating the building.',2,'2.1','DEFEND-IN-PLACE','A method of emergency',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000634","GHBC-REQ-000635"]','b85fc700f3fc8bc931b78f914d8ff1714693ec5cfb29a3a8e3e6d4e38261b5b7'),
('chunk-267','GHBC-CHUNK-000267','GHBC-C-000267','DEFERRED SUBMISSION
Those portions of the design that are not submitted at the time of the application and that are to be submitted to the Head of Works within a specified period.',2,'2.1','DEFERRED SUBMISSION',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000636"]','90d4acc00e3fab54ddbe7782ccf764f59ad8e2b99dfd4c1ed5fa4da36dbd1565'),
('chunk-268','GHBC-CHUNK-000268','GHBC-C-000268','DEFLAGRATION
An exothermic reaction,
such as the extremely rapid oxidation of a flammable dust or vapour in air, in which the reaction progresses through the unburned material at a rate less than the velocity of
sound. A deflagration can have an explosive effect.',2,'2.1','DEFLAGRATION','An exothermic reaction,',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000637","GHBC-REQ-000638","GHBC-REQ-000639"]','f235db297b144ef9ba4ec4b29ac9ad0a7daa709131f07305905ac68a0372542c'),
('chunk-269','GHBC-CHUNK-000269','GHBC-C-000269','DELAYED-ACTION CLOSER
A self-closing
device that incorporates a delay prior to the initiation of closing. Delayed-action closers are mechanical devices with an adjustable delay.
DELUGE',2,'2.1','DELAYED-ACTION CLOSER','A self-closing',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000640","GHBC-REQ-000641","GHBC-REQ-000642"]','0bd315710d0ebe9051caccacd141243573f3232554d27b0649cce9ec496d992d'),
('chunk-270','GHBC-CHUNK-000270','GHBC-C-000270','SYSTEM
A sprinkler system employing open sprinklers attached to a piping system connected to a water supply through a valve that is opened by the operation of a detection system installed in the same areas as the sprinklers. When this valve opens, water flows into the piping system and discharges from all sprinklers attached thereto.',2,'2.1','SYSTEM',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000643","GHBC-REQ-000644"]','cbe552851a6ea31c5acd2a0911061799a7c9f23b40be389b27b8b22294f89f8e');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-271','GHBC-CHUNK-000271','GHBC-C-000271','DESIGN EARTHQUAKE GROUND MOTION
The earthquake ground motion that buildings and structures are specifically proportioned to resist in this Code.',2,'2.1','DESIGN EARTHQUAKE GROUND MOTION',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000645"]','b682dc8993cc217634067ccaaf2adc46cfb838748e5d4292b5ff6bdacac952d1'),
('chunk-272','GHBC-CHUNK-000272','GHBC-C-000272','DESIGN FLOOD
The flood associated with the greater of the following two areas:
1. Area with a flood plain subject to a 1percent or greater chance of flooding in any year.
2. Area designated as a flood hazard area on a community‘s flood hazard map, or otherwise legally designated.',2,'2.1','DESIGN FLOOD',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000646","GHBC-REQ-000647","GHBC-REQ-000648","GHBC-REQ-000649","GHBC-REQ-000650"]','3cc9e5bee001921b4ee884014a19d8e247f6a938d51f9eac6230dbf8ddfe6996'),
('chunk-273','GHBC-CHUNK-000273','GHBC-C-000273','DESIGN FLOOD ELEVATION
The elevation
of the ―design flood,‖ including wave height, relative to the datum specified on the community‘s legally designated flood hazard map.',2,'2.1','DESIGN FLOOD ELEVATION','The elevation',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000651"]','a2c63b91ad4ea297ca5c9cc9577c3c15ee1797935f3f50091384c30e285029ab'),
('chunk-274','GHBC-CHUNK-000274','GHBC-C-000274','DESIGN STRENGTH
The product of the nominal strength and a resistance factor (or strength reduction factor).',2,'2.1','DESIGN STRENGTH',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000652"]','a04fa952b214386242a26c89db7c30409007ad9dedd008daf7188221dd623b37'),
('chunk-275','GHBC-CHUNK-000275','GHBC-C-000275','DETACHED BUILDING
A separate single-
storey building, without a basement or crawl space, used for the storage or use of hazardous materials and located an approved distance from all structures.',2,'2.1','DETACHED BUILDING','A separate single-',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000653"]','07672f0cec7f587c70b9a568bfa55d40d99df9209c47f240f925726cf32d7bc9'),
('chunk-276','GHBC-CHUNK-000276','GHBC-C-000276','DETECTABLE WARNING
A standardized
surface feature built in or applied to walking surfaces or other elements to warn visually impaired persons of hazards on a circulation path.',2,'2.1','DETECTABLE WARNING','A standardized',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000654"]','c873eb6bb49cbd5b9bd18f578e2c713b23a3f46a349d68a8d74d2c143907bf72'),
('chunk-277','GHBC-CHUNK-000277','GHBC-C-000277','DETECTOR, HEAT
A fire detector that senses
heat—either abnormally high temperature or rate of rise, or both.',2,'2.1','DETECTOR, HEAT','A fire detector that senses',135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000655"]','f641a8417a58d7bf19e26877f5bafa66129b5a6ef02d069b3efe01552cc549a6'),
('chunk-278','GHBC-CHUNK-000278','GHBC-C-000278','DETONATION
An exothermic reaction characterized by the presence of a shock wave
in the material which establishes and maintains the reaction. The reaction zone progresses through the material at a rate greater than the velocity of sound. The principal heating mechanism is one of shock compression. Detonations have an explosive effect.',2,'2.1','DETONATION',NULL,135,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000656","GHBC-REQ-000657","GHBC-REQ-000658","GHBC-REQ-000659","GHBC-REQ-000660"]','1d590a463017e019fd7ef358aeaa844a0ffb42aecb68657919c2f36c89134970'),
('chunk-279','GHBC-CHUNK-000279','GHBC-C-000279','DETOXIFICATION FACILITIES
Facilities that provide treatment for substance abuse, serving care recipients who are incapable of selfpreservation or who are harmful to themselves or others.',2,'2.1','DETOXIFICATION FACILITIES',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000661"]','b72f47c104b15f69b9dc20040c7308194b4b324ce6a3149fca174345db975831'),
('chunk-280','GHBC-CHUNK-000280','GHBC-C-000280','DIAPHRAGM
A horizontal or sloped system
acting to transmit lateral forces to vertical elements of the lateral force-resisting system. When the term ―diaphragm‖ is used, it shall include horizontal bracing systems.
Diaphragm, blocked. In light-frame construction, a diaphragm in which all sheathing edges not occurring on a framing member are supported on and fastened to blocking.
Diaphragm boundary. In light-frame construction, a location where shear is transferred into or out of the diaphragm sheathing. Transfer is either to a boundary element or to another force-resisting element.
Diaphragm chord. A diaphragm boundary element perpendicular to the applied load that is assumed to take axial stresses due to the diaphragm moment.
Diaphragm, unblocked. A diaphragm that has edge nailing at supporting members only. Blocking between supporting structural members at panel edges is not included. Diaphragm panels are field nailed to supporting members.',2,'2.1','DIAPHRAGM','A horizontal or sloped system',136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000662","GHBC-REQ-000663","GHBC-REQ-000664","GHBC-REQ-000665","GHBC-REQ-000666","GHBC-REQ-000667","GHBC-REQ-000668","GHBC-REQ-000669","GHBC-REQ-000670","GHBC-REQ-000671","GHBC-REQ-000672","GHBC-REQ-000673","GHBC-REQ-000674"]','343cb5ee3b7a0cab7ae659b7b7995ed5509176a54ef4db13781ae7ca58da45d5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-281','GHBC-CHUNK-000281','GHBC-C-000281','DIRECT ACCESS
A path of travel from a space to an immediately adjacent space through an opening in the common wall between the two spaces.',2,'2.1','DIRECT ACCESS',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000675"]','785d5982d82f89c2d4d4182151be7415e5e5e23fe19de7cbfca9d9e0d91460db'),
('chunk-282','GHBC-CHUNK-000282','GHBC-C-000282','DISPENSING
The pouring or transferring of any material from a container, tank or similar vessel, whereby vapours, dusts, fumes, mists or gases are liberated to the atmosphere.',2,'2.1','DISPENSING',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000676"]','b20979a8f40f68a4f390289439bebe1319dcb624ea19ffeaa68e869c953dae5d'),
('chunk-283','GHBC-CHUNK-000283','GHBC-C-000283','DORMITORY
A space in a building where
group sleeping accommodations are provided in one room, or in a series of closely associated rooms, for persons not members of the same family group, under joint occupancy and single
management, as in college dormitories or fraternity houses.',2,'2.1','DORMITORY','A space in a building where',136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000677","GHBC-REQ-000678"]','822f61a3d9432e16e2955355da2f7465b5cd4d2ca249dab44d859d112a7e979c'),
('chunk-284','GHBC-CHUNK-000284','GHBC-C-000284','DRAFTSTOP
A material, device or construction installed to restrict the movement of air within open spaces of concealed areas of building components such as crawl spaces, floor/ceiling assemblies, roof/ceiling assemblies and attics.
DRILLED',2,'2.1','DRAFTSTOP',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000679","GHBC-REQ-000680"]','b1522df94038d5c225fc21417ae45f8b7c8b2939ad4370f048b5102d358455d2'),
('chunk-285','GHBC-CHUNK-000285','GHBC-C-000285','SHAFT
A cast-in-place deep foundation element, also referred to as a caisson, drilled pier or bored pile, constructed by drilling a hole (with or without permanent casing or drilling fluid) into soil or rock and filling it with fluid concrete after the drilling equipment is removed.
Socketed drilled shaft. A drilled shaft with a permanent pipe or tube casing that extends down to bedrock and an uncased socket drilled into the bedrock.',2,'2.1','SHAFT',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000681","GHBC-REQ-000682","GHBC-REQ-000683"]','add9c4ae22cea3c8a6f53657aa7f8c4b0e7aa55f7c444b409862891c4ae28ea9'),
('chunk-286','GHBC-CHUNK-000286','GHBC-C-000286','DRY-CHEMICAL EXTINGUISHING AGENT
A powder composed of small particles, usually of sodium bicarbonate, potassium bicarbonate, urea-potassium-based bicarbonate, potassium chloride or monoammonium phosphate, with added particulate material supplemented by special treatment to provide resistance to packing, resistance to moisture absorption (caking) and the proper flow capabilities.',2,'2.1','DRY-CHEMICAL EXTINGUISHING AGENT',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000684"]','78f5d3ab2b6f04d806aef38e43a1fa7069b6378bd3a55d7a8540cbd76632284b'),
('chunk-287','GHBC-CHUNK-000287','GHBC-C-000287','DRY FLOODPROOFING
A combination of design modifications that results in a building or structure, including the attendant utilities and equipment and sanitary facilities, being water tight with walls substantially impermeable to the passage of water and with structural components having the capacity to resist loads.',2,'2.1','DRY FLOODPROOFING',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000685"]','50b4b03bb7f7d42df9bbc2bdeb164f93c7748f7ab3ad9dfcba2eed8b5aa44a18'),
('chunk-288','GHBC-CHUNK-000288','GHBC-C-000288','DWELLING
A building that contains one or two dwelling units used, intended or designed to be used, rented, leased, let or hired out to be occupied for living purposes.',2,'2.1','DWELLING',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000686"]','381c838ce78120ed6d41f36d2a8bb914bd406a391604e639bf53991a83519826'),
('chunk-289','GHBC-CHUNK-000289','GHBC-C-000289','DWELLING UNIT
A single unit providing
complete, independent living facilities for one or more persons, including permanent provisions for living, sleeping, eating, cooking and sanitation.',2,'2.1','DWELLING UNIT','A single unit providing',136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000687"]','be36beefdc33323ec7eab94b3f8addc3d4d815d04b5cff1f16ac1d0ffb446f81'),
('chunk-290','GHBC-CHUNK-000290','GHBC-C-000290','ESCAPE COURT
A court or yard which provides access to a public way for one or more exits.
ELECTRICAL CIRCUIT PROTECTIVE',2,'2.1','ESCAPE COURT',NULL,136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000688","GHBC-REQ-000689"]','30405e3fdf62fb51fe734de0ec10b95c1a19e9ec607ac2a746ac842684eeba69');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-291','GHBC-CHUNK-000291','GHBC-C-000291','SYSTEM
A specific construction of devices,
materials, or coatings installed as a fireresistive barrier system applied to electrical system components, such as cable trays,
conduits and other raceways, open run cables and conductors, cables, and conductors.',2,'2.1','SYSTEM','A specific construction of devices,',136,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000690","GHBC-REQ-000691"]','635cb33230e48ea7c7e01883e5031f9c808ccc2764884742a16497e9a61206d7'),
('chunk-292','GHBC-CHUNK-000292','GHBC-C-000292','ELEVATOR GROUP
A grouping of elevators
in a building located adjacent or directly across from one another that responds to common hall call buttons.',2,'2.1','ELEVATOR GROUP','A grouping of elevators',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000692"]','83ef9620f7c122d233fb7ac141d4daabf711e1092a857255373abe388c5d375d'),
('chunk-293','GHBC-CHUNK-000293','GHBC-C-000293','EMERGENCY ALARM SYSTEM
A system to provide indication and warning of emergency situations involving hazardous materials.
EMERGENCY CONTROL',2,'2.1','EMERGENCY ALARM SYSTEM',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000693","GHBC-REQ-000694"]','b36e3b58bcd3dab76f51af5a43814282b6989dd556ad583ab9e2798386ee0e5f'),
('chunk-294','GHBC-CHUNK-000294','GHBC-C-000294','STATION
An approved location on the premises where signals from emergency equipment are received and which is staffed by trained personnel.
EMERGENCY ESCAPE AND RESCUE',2,'2.1','STATION',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000695","GHBC-REQ-000696"]','03b6e643b1bf7b31e70e3b7fb4778ba675c16b93f025830721569c86040a1d49'),
('chunk-295','GHBC-CHUNK-000295','GHBC-C-000295','OPENING
An operable window, door or other
similar device that provides for a means of escape and access for rescue in the event of an emergency.
EMERGENCY',2,'2.1','OPENING','An operable window, door or other',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000697","GHBC-REQ-000698"]','49cfffa1531035d4bca13611adc45bd5218ee238a386f9670b51e4c631800a4d'),
('chunk-296','GHBC-CHUNK-000296','GHBC-C-000296','FACILITIES
Buildings and other structures that are intended to remain operational in the event of extreme environmental loading from flood, wind, earthquakes.',2,'2.1','FACILITIES',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000699"]','3ec96c0d0e77ebbbf0cf8f45a772eef1d0982cf52bf48fb4e544db040f2f3e1d'),
('chunk-297','GHBC-CHUNK-000297','GHBC-C-000297','EMERGENCY POWER SYSTEM
A source of automatic electric power of a required capacity and duration to operate required life safety, fire alarm, detection and ventilation systems in the event of a failure of the primary power. Emergency power systems are required for electrical loads where interruption of the primary power could result in loss of human life or serious injuries.
EMERGENCY VOICE/ALARM',2,'2.1','EMERGENCY POWER SYSTEM',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000700","GHBC-REQ-000701","GHBC-REQ-000702"]','7d1c7cb4c266403a13aac2054d0565e46e712e8329faa61028f26a780d56a2f8'),
('chunk-298','GHBC-CHUNK-000298','GHBC-C-000298','COMMUNICATIONS
Dedicated manual or automatic facilities for originating and distributing voice instructions, as well as alert and evacuation signals pertaining to a fire emergency, to the occupants of a building.',2,'2.1','COMMUNICATIONS',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000703"]','c5e78e4c2ee3137602c8026f3539dc173129db727abc5344ca3be694c446a61d'),
('chunk-299','GHBC-CHUNK-000299','GHBC-C-000299','EMPLOYEE WORK AREA
All or any portion
of a space used only by employees and only for work. Corridors, toilet rooms, kitchenettes and break rooms are not employee work areas.',2,'2.1','EMPLOYEE WORK AREA','All or any portion',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000704","GHBC-REQ-000705"]','6b25cd9aa8bef89764122f0b75873b2ba2a2a5d1443429f17a263792959ddbed'),
('chunk-300','GHBC-CHUNK-000300','GHBC-C-000300','ENGINEERED WOOD RIM BOARD
A full-
depth structural composite timber, wood structural panel, structural glued laminated timber or prefabricated wood I-joist member designed to transfer horizontal (shear) and vertical (compression) loads, provide attachment for diaphragm sheathing, siding and exterior deck ledgers, and provide lateral
support at the ends of floor or roof joists or rafters.',2,'2.1','ENGINEERED WOOD RIM BOARD','A full-',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000706","GHBC-REQ-000707"]','ad356c1b033183e29bb9061f4d1ea82a5dd0b3953cad9ab6662a5efcce3aae6d');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-301','GHBC-CHUNK-000301','GHBC-C-000301','EQUIPMENT PLATFORM
An unoccupied,
elevated platform used exclusively for mechanical systems or industrial process equipment, including the associated elevated walkways, stairways, alternating tread devices and ladders necessary to access the platform.',2,'2.1','EQUIPMENT PLATFORM','An unoccupied,',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000708"]','82e52bad296aeed2e72644dee55f3e2b1eddd03a1ecf46b32efa8090988ccd91'),
('chunk-302','GHBC-CHUNK-000302','GHBC-C-000302','EXHAUSTED ENCLOSURE
An appliance or piece of equipment that consists of a top, a back and two sides providing a means of local exhaust for capturing gases, fumes, vapours and mists. Such enclosures include laboratory hoods, exhaust fume hoods and similar appliances and equipment used to locally retain and exhaust the gases, fumes, vapours and mists that could be released. Rooms or areas provided with general ventilation, in themselves, are not exhausted enclosures.',2,'2.1','EXHAUSTED ENCLOSURE',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000709","GHBC-REQ-000710","GHBC-REQ-000711"]','fc95bdb44ab8df648cd94e8ca61d004f97fcfdc69432ae639475e06aa937542b'),
('chunk-303','GHBC-CHUNK-000303','GHBC-C-000303','EXISTING BUILDING
A building erected prior
to the date of adoption of the appropriate Code, or one for which a legal building permit has been issued.',2,'2.1','EXISTING BUILDING','A building erected prior',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000712"]','6296f355e1489899bc05e7273225b944e65af16ffabcc969806487a9bf6f6450'),
('chunk-304','GHBC-CHUNK-000304','GHBC-C-000304','EXISTING STRUCTURE
A structure erected
prior to the date of adoption of the appropriate Code, or one for which a legal building permit has been issued.',2,'2.1','EXISTING STRUCTURE','A structure erected',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000713"]','a8159b99f60c88d47f80376c8db52f4128a517832eb602f6f8ffc6b22034fa14'),
('chunk-305','GHBC-CHUNK-000305','GHBC-C-000305','EXIT
That portion of a means of escape
system between the exit access and the exit discharge or public way. Exit components include exterior exit doors at the level of exit discharge, interior exit stairways and ramps, exit passageways, exterior exit stairways and ramps and horizontal exits.',2,'2.1','EXIT','That portion of a means of escape',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000714","GHBC-REQ-000715"]','6f78de93216010ffe269a2d07204656bd953890ae40eb8a3ce6229b85f649427'),
('chunk-306','GHBC-CHUNK-000306','GHBC-C-000306','EXIT ACCESS
That portion of a means of escape system that leads from any occupied portion of a building or structure to an exit.',2,'2.1','EXIT ACCESS',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000716"]','b051565e0bf99d5934e7225979041c896e74bfc5c8fc2e75ae0531d642ae28d9'),
('chunk-307','GHBC-CHUNK-000307','GHBC-C-000307','EXIT ACCESS DOORWAY
A door or access
point along the path of escape travel from an occupied room, area or space where the path of escape enters an intervening room, corridor, exit access stairway or ramp.',2,'2.1','EXIT ACCESS DOORWAY','A door or access',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000717"]','307377e577e44e92a18a04b9da1188962556a5c5664c14a4b94cdb4bc389cc0a'),
('chunk-308','GHBC-CHUNK-000308','GHBC-C-000308','EXIT ACCESS RAMP
A ramp within the exit
access portion of the means of escape system.',2,'2.1','EXIT ACCESS RAMP','A ramp within the exit',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000718"]','11e5fe8c9cf697f8584c6468ea0eb05cbbf44e8bb13cbad7b800d61a93433f0d'),
('chunk-309','GHBC-CHUNK-000309','GHBC-C-000309','EXIT ACCESS STAIRWAY
A stairway within
the exit access portion of the means of escape system.',2,'2.1','EXIT ACCESS STAIRWAY','A stairway within',137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000719"]','c0fc805d680af4d53cf72561b8d5b1b1e61c38e24311bd40a37b7ac90e71490e'),
('chunk-310','GHBC-CHUNK-000310','GHBC-C-000310','EXIT DISCHARGE
That portion of a means of escape system between the termination of an exit and a public way.',2,'2.1','EXIT DISCHARGE',NULL,137,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000720"]','61ab70f6077eb56f214b7b797589df8f4faf115a1dd996d2f3e54fd69cdd53fb');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-311','GHBC-CHUNK-000311','GHBC-C-000311','EXIT DISCHARGE, LEVEL OF
The storey at the point at which an exit terminates and an exit discharge begins.',2,'2.1','EXIT DISCHARGE, LEVEL OF',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000721"]','98f3c2bc0594084dceef821d039efa48cf8114d8855fbd2cc82e80f9525e685c'),
('chunk-312','GHBC-CHUNK-000312','GHBC-C-000312','EXIT PASSAGEWAY
An exit component that is separated from other interior spaces of a building or structure by fire-resistance-rated construction and opening protectives, and provides for a protected path of escape travel in a horizontal direction to an exit or to the exit discharge.',2,'2.1','EXIT PASSAGEWAY',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000722"]','219bd347330ae784c304fb21405129bd44b6948a9637086a435a7ef3470d1de0'),
('chunk-313','GHBC-CHUNK-000313','GHBC-C-000313','EXPANDED VINYL WALL COVERING
Wall
covering consisting of a woven textile backing, an expanded vinyl base coat layer and a nonexpanded vinyl skin coat. The expanded base coat layer is a homogeneous vinyl layer that contains a blowing agent. During processing, the blowing agent decomposes, causing this layer to expand by forming closed cells. The total thickness of the wall covering is approximately 1.4 mm to 1.78 mm (0.055 inch to 0.070 inch).',2,'2.1','EXPANDED VINYL WALL COVERING','Wall',138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000723","GHBC-REQ-000724","GHBC-REQ-000725","GHBC-REQ-000726"]','824478b05a7654458e1d9781fdd2d5fd63a89d287652b846daf71e4a0c6059a2'),
('chunk-314','GHBC-CHUNK-000314','GHBC-C-000314','EXPLOSION
An effect produced by the sudden violent expansion of gases, which may be accompanied by a shock wave or disruption, or both, of enclosing materials or structures. An explosion could result from any of the following:
1. Chemical changes such as rapid oxidation, deflagration or detonation, decomposition of molecules and runaway polymerization (usually detonations).
2. Physical changes such as pressure tank ruptures.
3. Atomic changes (nuclear fission or fusion).',2,'2.1','EXPLOSION',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000727","GHBC-REQ-000728","GHBC-REQ-000729","GHBC-REQ-000730","GHBC-REQ-000731","GHBC-REQ-000732","GHBC-REQ-000733","GHBC-REQ-000734"]','7f0a8b869105a6e78a77074a61c12a88abe87c6b0899f539b69d9df411736cfb'),
('chunk-315','GHBC-CHUNK-000315','GHBC-C-000315','EXPLOSIVE
A chemical compound, mixture or device, the primary or common purpose of which is to function by explosion. The term includes, but is not limited to: dynamite, black powder, pellet powder, initiating explosives, detonators, safety fuses, squibs, detonating cord, igniter cord, and igniters.',2,'2.1','EXPLOSIVE',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000735","GHBC-REQ-000736"]','3eb794128500d465e1c5c7e4e374ae4fd13d0da88c7ed2041bb27f3138f260ee'),
('chunk-316','GHBC-CHUNK-000316','GHBC-C-000316','EXTERIOR EXIT RAMP
An exit component
that serves to meet one or more means of escape design requirements, such as required number of exits or exit access travel distance, and is open to yards, courts or public ways.
EXTERIOR EXIT',2,'2.1','EXTERIOR EXIT RAMP','An exit component',138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000737","GHBC-REQ-000738"]','f63c939c13824d86524e3d531f064b5e5883f882b07cbe3558b21baf39003051'),
('chunk-317','GHBC-CHUNK-000317','GHBC-C-000317','STAIRWAY
An exit component that serves to meet one or more means of escape design requirements, such as required number of exits or exit access travel
distance, and is open to yards, courts or public ways.
EXTERIOR INSULATION AND FINISH',2,'2.1','STAIRWAY',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000739","GHBC-REQ-000740","GHBC-REQ-000741"]','1ffa38883ad10640946435917ad64217de503b304d1040c382be08d9e41e088e'),
('chunk-318','GHBC-CHUNK-000318','GHBC-C-000318','SYSTEMS (EIFS)
EIFS are nonstructural,
nonload-bearing, exterior wall cladding systems that consist of an insulation board attached either adhesively or mechanically, or both, to the substrate; an integrally reinforced base coat and a textured protective finish coat.
EXTERIOR INSULATION AND FINISH',2,'2.1','SYSTEMS (EIFS)','EIFS are nonstructural,',138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000742","GHBC-REQ-000743"]','e8d4725022e881f16cc374e64cecb5c37a3a5c533f12e32b6ce9bafb57991545'),
('chunk-319','GHBC-CHUNK-000319','GHBC-C-000319','SYSTEMS (EIFS) WITH DRAINAGE
An EIFS
that incorporates a means of drainage applied over a water-resistive barrier.',2,'2.1','SYSTEMS (EIFS) WITH DRAINAGE','An EIFS',138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000744"]','85bf659cf7c14223a856d56ec9b2622636fba2543db02c46faa0f022d36451a3'),
('chunk-320','GHBC-CHUNK-000320','GHBC-C-000320','EXTERIOR SURFACES
Weather-exposed
surfaces.
EXTERIOR',2,'2.1','EXTERIOR SURFACES','Weather-exposed',138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000745","GHBC-REQ-000746"]','9df37b01619bcc2fdf433eff5a933f1e6d4da5b2a19aa874a613f962aee63b17');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-321','GHBC-CHUNK-000321','GHBC-C-000321','WALL
A wall, bearing or nonbearing, that is used as an enclosing wall for a building, other than a fire wall, and that has a slope of 60 degrees (1.05 rad) or greater with the horizontal plane.',2,'2.1','WALL',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000747"]','bb865fa3d0640fcb6f808539773edd33e3809eb63a443048761a1972ad43d866'),
('chunk-322','GHBC-CHUNK-000322','GHBC-C-000322','EXTERIOR WALL COVERING
A material or assembly of materials applied on the exterior side of exterior walls for the purpose of providing a weather-resisting barrier, insulation or for aesthetics, including but not limited to, veneers, siding, exterior insulation and finish systems, architectural trim and embellishments such as cornices, soffits, facias, gutters and leaders.',2,'2.1','EXTERIOR WALL COVERING',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000748"]','99007f2721896b958b78b43e3c7a5625bc6ac39aa278cc70a6b3cb50d10bd0f4'),
('chunk-323','GHBC-CHUNK-000323','GHBC-C-000323','EXTERIOR WALL ENVELOPE
A system or assembly of exterior wall components, including exterior wall finish materials, that provides protection of the building structural members, including framing and sheathing materials, and conditioned interior space, from the detrimental effects of the exterior environment.',2,'2.1','EXTERIOR WALL ENVELOPE',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000749"]','fc2983090af59693b8722f27fd5d8c63270f740f9dbd2bf2d61e61f933f64e75'),
('chunk-324','GHBC-CHUNK-000324','GHBC-C-000324','FABRIC PARTITION
A partition consisting of a finished surface made of fabric, without a continuous rigid backing, that is directly attached to a framing system in which the vertical framing members are spaced greater than 1219 mm (4 feet) on center.',2,'2.1','FABRIC PARTITION',NULL,138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000750"]','c6fd19e1cc491cf6eb2626af9bfa94ad5bc574cf7735ffb6df46f1e4ee9bbe3e'),
('chunk-325','GHBC-CHUNK-000325','GHBC-C-000325','FABRICATED ITEM
Structural, load-bearing
or lateral load-resisting members or assemblies consisting of materials assembled prior to installation in a building or structure, or subjected to operations such as heat treatment, thermal cutting, cold working or reforming after manufacture and prior to installation in a building or structure. Materials produced in accordance with standards referenced by this Code, such as rolled structural steel shapes,
steel reinforcing bars, masonry units and wood structural panels, or in accordance with a referenced standard that provides requirements for quality control done under the supervision of a third-party quality control agency, are not ―fabricated items.‖',2,'2.1','FABRICATED ITEM','Structural, load-bearing',138,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000751","GHBC-REQ-000752","GHBC-REQ-000753"]','9ace6ed39d1d1c6ebe3c2dec32f95489ea8744bdb501223f990a52c52617ec22'),
('chunk-326','GHBC-CHUNK-000326','GHBC-C-000326','FABRICATION AREA
An area within a semiconductor fabrication facility and related research and development areas in which there are processes using hazardous production materials. Such areas are allowed to include ancillary rooms or areas such as dressing rooms and offices that are directly related to the fabrication area processes.',2,'2.1','FABRICATION AREA',NULL,139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000754","GHBC-REQ-000755"]','b943c9652e649e3196fe24c254975e41660e6333dc7f5eb8b6f68364b73f2c4b'),
('chunk-327','GHBC-CHUNK-000327','GHBC-C-000327','FACILITY
All or any portion of buildings,
structures, site improvements, elements and pedestrian or vehicular routes located on a site.',2,'2.1','FACILITY','All or any portion of buildings,',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000756"]','0dbb51921a4754ac11b2a7257c43e1f373f26667f5bdeb5f609b6cbc63f17b9b'),
('chunk-328','GHBC-CHUNK-000328','GHBC-C-000328','FACTORED LOAD
The product of a nominal
load and a load factor.',2,'2.1','FACTORED LOAD','The product of a nominal',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000757"]','c6b5518d181cfbe20d47ef448f16d00f473f4f5779362f882e6a2267895ea1a0'),
('chunk-329','GHBC-CHUNK-000329','GHBC-C-000329','FENESTRATION
Products classified as either
vertical fenestration or skylights and sloped glazing, installed in such a manner as to preserve the weather-resistant barrier of the wall or roof in which they are installed. Fenestration includes products with glass or other transparent or translucent materials.',2,'2.1','FENESTRATION','Products classified as either',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000758","GHBC-REQ-000759"]','93a5e163451a516a07f219ee788a8f247df3d3a1b7fdcda5e194baf23333580a'),
('chunk-330','GHBC-CHUNK-000330','GHBC-C-000330','FENESTRATION, VERTICAL
Windows that are fixed or movable, opaque doors, glazed doors, glazed block and combination opaque and glazed doors installed in a wall at less than 15 degrees from the vertical.
FIBER-CEMENT (BACKER BOARD, SIDING, SOFFIT, TRIM AND UNDERLAYMENT)',2,'2.1','FENESTRATION, VERTICAL',NULL,139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000760","GHBC-REQ-000761"]','1f93b419c6c38ab5d2cdaf1549f71d1d1869b827e7b7d1df6048be746d0e792f');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-331','GHBC-CHUNK-000331','GHBC-C-000331','PRODUCTS
Manufactured thin clause
composites of hydraulic cementitious matrices and discrete nonasbestos fibers.',2,'2.1','PRODUCTS','Manufactured thin clause',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000762"]','f782f580c23bd0526d2e6fe59dd0b184dcbe212bd62a18a220c5555ac6962a87'),
('chunk-332','GHBC-CHUNK-000332','GHBC-C-000332','FIBER-REINFORCED POLYMER
A polymeric
composite material consisting of reinforcement fibers, such as glass, impregnated with a fiberbinding polymer which is then molded and hardened. Fiber-reinforced polymers are permitted to contain cores laminated between fiber-reinforced polymer facings.',2,'2.1','FIBER-REINFORCED POLYMER','A polymeric',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000763","GHBC-REQ-000764"]','5cae057e8b56c31d21e9bae5e374d9bfe7af4d3a692c75bc03203466f5f19192'),
('chunk-333','GHBC-CHUNK-000333','GHBC-C-000333','FIBERBOARD
A fibrous, homogeneous panel
made from lignocellulosic fibers (usually wood or cane) and having a density of less than 31 pounds per cubic foot (pcf) (497 kg/m3 ) but more than 10 pcf (160 kg/m3 ).',2,'2.1','FIBERBOARD','A fibrous, homogeneous panel',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000765"]','6fd3caad1e62280a7c4d760027db8e2e9955fc183d0b7c7611d5cb67dc703559'),
('chunk-334','GHBC-CHUNK-000334','GHBC-C-000334','FIRE ALARM CONTROL UNIT
A system
component that receives inputs from automatic and manual fire alarm devices and may be
capable of supplying power to detection devices and transponders or off-premises transmitters. The control unit may be capable of providing a transfer of power to the notification appliances and transfer of condition to relays or devices.',2,'2.1','FIRE ALARM CONTROL UNIT','A system',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000766","GHBC-REQ-000767","GHBC-REQ-000768"]','201fa65a10848e6249299f6b9fc0c12ff28514fc12f6ebac29b75798b936a784'),
('chunk-335','GHBC-CHUNK-000335','GHBC-C-000335','FIRE ALARM SIGNAL
A signal initiated by a fire alarm-initiating device such as a manual fire alarm box, automatic fire detector, waterflow switch or other device whose activation is indicative of the presence of a fire or fire signature.',2,'2.1','FIRE ALARM SIGNAL',NULL,139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000769"]','bcc49666eed5531ec1b7c7adba8d402b72b4e065707832714a7a6b59de7bdaea'),
('chunk-336','GHBC-CHUNK-000336','GHBC-C-000336','FIRE ALARM SYSTEM
A system or portion of a combination system consisting of components and circuits arranged to monitor and annunciate the status of fire alarm or supervisory signal-initiating devices and to initiate the appropriate response to those signals.
FIRE',2,'2.1','FIRE ALARM SYSTEM',NULL,139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000770","GHBC-REQ-000771"]','4e64b81afc195c896e16703f15fd29fa5ff4569c476f999c31da460e141fbe88'),
('chunk-337','GHBC-CHUNK-000337','GHBC-C-000337','AREA
The aggregate floor area
enclosed and bounded by fire walls, fire barriers, exterior walls or horizontal assemblies of a building. Areas of the building not provided with surrounding walls shall be included in the fire area if such areas are included within the horizontal projection of the roof or floor next above.',2,'2.1','AREA','The aggregate floor area',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000772","GHBC-REQ-000773"]','abdefb254be14b0a3d726c4799f943dcd919d18f9339a05739cd8a561d3b973d'),
('chunk-338','GHBC-CHUNK-000338','GHBC-C-000338','FIRE BARRIER
A fire-resistance-rated wall
assembly of materials designed to restrict the spread of fire in which continuity is maintained.',2,'2.1','FIRE BARRIER','A fire-resistance-rated wall',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000774"]','05a1cc0650fcdfb423bf573c0bc61df0e0671179017aa6ba4a3da2b5ea6a5fff'),
('chunk-339','GHBC-CHUNK-000339','GHBC-C-000339','FIRE COMMAND CENTER
The principal
attended or unattended location where the status of detection, alarm communications and control systems is displayed, and from which the systems can be manually controlled.',2,'2.1','FIRE COMMAND CENTER','The principal',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000775"]','e1c5a095f1c20fa5885d9762cb8741fb6a74c6801792577ff993110d3d2e7fca'),
('chunk-340','GHBC-CHUNK-000340','GHBC-C-000340','FIRE DAMPER
A listed device installed in ducts and air transfer openings designed to close automatically upon detection of heat and resist the passage of flame. Fire dampers are classified for use in either static systems that will automatically shut down in the event of a fire, or in dynamic systems that continue to operate during a fire. A dynamic fire damper is tested and rated for closure under elevated temperature airflow.',2,'2.1','FIRE DAMPER',NULL,139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000776","GHBC-REQ-000777","GHBC-REQ-000778"]','62ec722072b6ca2e2334fd25054e6c2cb68f9f685d21a188f6a896dced53ad7b');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-341','GHBC-CHUNK-000341','GHBC-C-000341','FIRE DETECTOR, AUTOMATIC
A device
designed to detect the presence of a fire signature and to initiate action.',2,'2.1','FIRE DETECTOR, AUTOMATIC','A device',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000779"]','dd4484c28d3720df4ae55c5dfa4511c6d4edb43e5b266295ea7bfbe534c46dbb'),
('chunk-342','GHBC-CHUNK-000342','GHBC-C-000342','FIRE DOOR
The door component of a fire
door assembly.',2,'2.1','FIRE DOOR','The door component of a fire',139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000780"]','ec91aaa79426e86f9e0359c32fc294b18879ce9c2c40ca38c8774f88c53457fe'),
('chunk-343','GHBC-CHUNK-000343','GHBC-C-000343','FIRE DOOR ASSEMBLY
Any combination of a fire door, frame, hardware and other
accessories that together provide a specific degree of fire protection to the opening.',2,'2.1','FIRE DOOR ASSEMBLY',NULL,139,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000781","GHBC-REQ-000782"]','d1434908148d9e3a6a987300988101e978a92c99d0c084d2078c657684d08080'),
('chunk-344','GHBC-CHUNK-000344','GHBC-C-000344','FIRE EXIT HARDWARE
Panic hardware that is listed for use on fire door assemblies.',2,'2.1','FIRE EXIT HARDWARE',NULL,140,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000783"]','223dbf69a1bc46d6291f78fd75e6bbae528485cb1b94e2cac336ee1cb3e34a69'),
('chunk-345','GHBC-CHUNK-000345','GHBC-C-000345','FIRE LANE
A road or other passageway
developed to allow the passage of fire apparatus. A fire lane is not necessarily intended for vehicular traffic other than fire apparatus.',2,'2.1','FIRE LANE','A road or other passageway',140,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000784","GHBC-REQ-000785"]','9026757be44e0d5a63bbb24c8f32c3f80756572503f5a459df2b509e3158fcb5'),
