INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-421','GHBC-CHUNK-000421','GHBC-C-000421','LABORATORY
Laboratories in Group B occupancies used for
educational purposes above the 12th grade. Storage, use and handling of chemicals in such laboratories shall be limited to purposes related to testing, analysis, teaching, research or developmental activities on a nonproduction basis.',2,'2.1','LABORATORY',NULL,144,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000929","GHBC-REQ-000930","GHBC-REQ-000931"]','65720e006624543720178c81764fec0248b22a11041000c854f68be9afc328c1'),
('chunk-422','GHBC-CHUNK-000422','GHBC-C-000422','HIGHLY TOXIC
A material which produces a lethal dose or lethal concentration that falls within any of the following categories:
1. A chemical that has a median lethal dose (LD ) of 50 milligrams or less per kilogram of body weight when50 administered orally to albino rats weighing between 200 and 300 grams each.
2. A chemical that has a median lethal dose (LD ) of 200 milligrams or less per kilogram of body weight when50 administered by continuous contact for 24 hours (or less if death occurs within 24 hours) with the bare skin of albino rabbits weighing between 2 and 3 kilograms each.
3. A chemical that has a median lethal concentration (LC ) in air of 200 parts per million by volume or less of gas or50 vapour, or 2 milligrams per liter or less of mist, fume or dust, when administered by continuous inhalation for 1 hour (or less if death occurs within 1 hour) to albino rats weighing between 200 and 300 grams each.
Mixtures of these materials with ordinary materials, such as water, might not warrant classification as highly toxic. While this system is basically simple in application, any hazard evaluation that is required for the precise categorization of this type of material shall be performed by experienced, technically competent persons.
HIGH-PRESSURE DECORATIVE EXTERIOR-GRADE COMPACT LAMINATE (HPL). Panels consisting of layers of cellulose fibrous material impregnated with thermosetting resins and bonded together by a high-pressure process to form a homogeneous nonporous core suitable for exterior use.
HIGH-PRESSURE DECORATIVE EXTERIOR-GRADE COMPACT LAMINATE (HPL) SYSTEM. An exterior wall covering fabricated using HPL in a specific assembly including joints, seams, attachments, substrate,
framing and other details as appropriate to a particular design.',2,'2.1','HIGHLY TOXIC',NULL,144,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000932","GHBC-REQ-000933","GHBC-REQ-000934","GHBC-REQ-000935","GHBC-REQ-000936","GHBC-REQ-000937","GHBC-REQ-000938","GHBC-REQ-000939","GHBC-REQ-000940","GHBC-REQ-000941","GHBC-REQ-000942","GHBC-REQ-000943","GHBC-REQ-000944","GHBC-REQ-000945"]','f8ed8fb16d662e73776d719386e091e06b6ced1cf32aab158ee6e983b1b6f406'),
('chunk-423','GHBC-CHUNK-000423','GHBC-C-000423','HIGH-RISE BUILDING
A building with an occupied floor located more than 75 feet (22 860 mm) above the lowest level of fire department vehicle access.',2,'2.1','HIGH-RISE BUILDING',NULL,145,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000946"]','4279d65294be6d19dc1f5fed210c013ff88c6f7ec6b57e1d50086d59fb4fd9b7'),
('chunk-424','GHBC-CHUNK-000424','GHBC-C-000424','HISTORIC BUILDINGS
Any building or structure that is one or more of the following:
1. Listed or certified as eligible for listing by the State Historic Preservation Officer or the Keeper of the National Register of Historic Places, in the National Register of Historic Places.
2. Designated as historic under an applicable state or local law.
3. Certified as a contributing resource within a National Register, state designated or locally designated historic district.',2,'2.1','HISTORIC BUILDINGS',NULL,145,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-000947","GHBC-REQ-000948","GHBC-REQ-000949","GHBC-REQ-000950","GHBC-REQ-000951","GHBC-REQ-000952","GHBC-REQ-000953"]','76cd80010a452533501e7d8d15d5aa4d15c6c26772ea0212e44b51261f4c4d37'),
