which is sloped less than 25 degrees from the horizontal and is located less than 3048 mm (10 feet) from operable openings above or adjacent to the level of the marquee.',2,'2.1','MARQUEE','A canopy that has a top surface',147,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001032"]','8e12ee40792c704b87303a2a6689862408b381e21286c2a9435ece888ee0e804'),
('chunk-473','GHBC-CHUNK-000473','GHBC-C-000473','MASONRY
A built-up construction or combination of building units or materials of clay, shale, concrete, glass, gypsum, stone or other approved units bonded together with or without mortar or grout or other accepted methods of joining.
Glass unit masonry. Masonry composed of glass units bonded by mortar.
Plain masonry. Masonry in which the tensile resistance of the masonry is taken into consideration and the effects of stresses in reinforcement are neglected.
Reinforced masonry. Masonry construction in which reinforcement acting in conjunction with the masonry is used to resist forces.
Solid masonry. Masonry consisting of solid masonry units laid contiguously with the joints between the units filled with mortar.
Unreinforced (plain) masonry. Masonry in which the tensile resistance of masonry is taken into consideration and the resistance of the reinforcing steel, if present, is neglected.',2,'2.1','MASONRY',NULL,147,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001033","GHBC-REQ-001034","GHBC-REQ-001035","GHBC-REQ-001036","GHBC-REQ-001037","GHBC-REQ-001038","GHBC-REQ-001039","GHBC-REQ-001040","GHBC-REQ-001041","GHBC-REQ-001042","GHBC-REQ-001043"]','95ff4371938320f7a1eb3489655e2e3b22a8f58a8e153979dc73b90395fa796c'),
('chunk-474','GHBC-CHUNK-000474','GHBC-C-000474','MASONRY UNIT
Brick, tile, stone, glass block
or concrete block conforming to the requirements specified in Clause 22.3.
Hollow. A masonry unit whose net crossclauseal area in any plane parallel to the load-bearing surface is less than 75 percent of its gross cross-clauseal area measured in the same plane.
Solid. A masonry unit whose net crossclauseal area in every plane parallel to the load-bearing surface is 75 percent or more of its gross cross-clauseal area measured in the same plane.
MASTIC FIRE-RESISTANT',2,'2.1','MASONRY UNIT','Brick, tile, stone, glass block',148,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001044","GHBC-REQ-001045","GHBC-REQ-001046","GHBC-REQ-001047","GHBC-REQ-001048","GHBC-REQ-001049"]','f0f26dbeed708f5f8bc91742ab58a3fca2ff087e75c3033df3d1a4282ffb73d3'),
('chunk-475','GHBC-CHUNK-000475','GHBC-C-000475','COATINGS
