employed or retained by an approved agency and approved by the Head of Works as having the competence necessary to inspect a particular type of construction requiring special inspection.
SPECIFIED COMPRESSIVE STRENGTH OF MASONRY, f´m. Minimum compressive strength, expressed as force per unit of net cross-clauseal area, required of the masonry used in construction by the approved construction documents, and upon which the project design is based. Whenever the quantity f´ is under the radical sign, the square root of m numerical value only is intended and the result has units of pounds per square inch (psi) (MPa).',2,'2.1','SPECIAL INSPECTOR','A qualified person',156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001297","GHBC-REQ-001298","GHBC-REQ-001299","GHBC-REQ-001300"]','019e4f6dcac88c5dbce19029ece6f3015e543cdae17494eea918ab2f8dca9789'),
