('chunk-624','GHBC-CHUNK-000624','GHBC-C-000624','ROOM
A room designed to accommodate spraying operations.',2,'2.1','ROOM',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001303"]','86e3ae2de3d8122f41f44f2eb19e64de8555574848f5ef78e9ebe5575684f705'),
('chunk-625','GHBC-CHUNK-000625','GHBC-C-000625','SPRAYED FIRE-RESISTANT MATERIALS
Cementitious or fibrous materials that are sprayed to provide fire-resistant protection of the substrates.',2,'2.1','SPRAYED FIRE-RESISTANT MATERIALS',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001304"]','cddd83492c07550ed0918e9563dac944026823902fe467b5bfbdf013e4bd54e1'),
('chunk-626','GHBC-CHUNK-000626','GHBC-C-000626','STAGE
A space within a building utilized for entertainment or presentations, which includes overhead hanging curtains, drops, scenery or stage effects other than lighting and sound.',2,'2.1','STAGE',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001305"]','922eab68d0b3d0ececf2c7074d677160f6dbe476bef36e54659a6b68948f8bc6'),
('chunk-627','GHBC-CHUNK-000627','GHBC-C-000627','STAIR
A change in elevation, consisting of one or more risers.',2,'2.1','STAIR',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001306"]','cff0188a675047ec3c1b437eb0d35c0a35f157b21074f8863c8e7245f7a7d33e'),
('chunk-628','GHBC-CHUNK-000628','GHBC-C-000628','STAIRWAY
One or more flights of stairs,
either exterior or interior, with the necessary landings and platforms connecting them, to form a continuous and uninterrupted passage from one level to another.',2,'2.1','STAIRWAY','One or more flights of stairs,',156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001307"]','c9687becde7b4c7a76d4661fb650d38e72b68f198b1ddf9bc9358817ded6cbfe'),
('chunk-629','GHBC-CHUNK-000629','GHBC-C-000629','STAIRWAY, SPIRAL
A stairway having a closed circular form in its plan view with uniform clause-shaped treads attached to and radiating from a minimum-diameter supporting column.',2,'2.1','STAIRWAY, SPIRAL',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001308"]','286f1cae5786f7010d4f37d3929669a1228b1a98aa23e98944696be1671dc88d'),
('chunk-630','GHBC-CHUNK-000630','GHBC-C-000630','STANDBY POWER SYSTEM
A source of automatic electric power of a required capacity and duration to operate required building, hazardous materials or ventilation systems in the event of a failure of the primary power. Standby power systems are required for electrical loads where interruption of the primary power could create hazards or hamper rescue or fire-fighting operations.',2,'2.1','STANDBY POWER SYSTEM',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001309","GHBC-REQ-001310"]','c7764584ecc864f9e13db252e905620b26100056a5dfdd17e3f9509888df46f3');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-631','GHBC-CHUNK-000631','GHBC-C-000631','START OF CONSTRUCTION
The date of permit issuance for new construction and substantial improvements to existing structures, provided the actual start of construction, repair, reconstruction, rehabilitation, addition, placement or other improvement is within 180 days after the date of issuance. The actual start of construction means the first placement of permanent construction of a building (including a manufactured home) on a site, such as the pouring of a slab or footings, installation of pilings or construction of columns.',2,'2.1','START OF CONSTRUCTION',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001311","GHBC-REQ-001312"]','f92395d1e2b4bfd485f51beb808f2a1f231963e1f820997b959899d34f72811e'),
('chunk-632','GHBC-CHUNK-000632','GHBC-C-000632','STEEL CONSTRUCTION, COLD-FORMED
That type of construction made up entirely or in part of steel structural members cold formed to shape from sheet or strip steel such as roof deck, floor and wall panels, studs, floor joists, roof joists and other structural elements.',2,'2.1','STEEL CONSTRUCTION, COLD-FORMED',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001313"]','812c4adf2a3af2d71ea59d94f926d0bd5bc18f0b39829346be7dafd3aa2aba3d'),
('chunk-633','GHBC-CHUNK-000633','GHBC-C-000633','STEEL ELEMENT, STRUCTURAL
Any steel
structural member of a building or structure consisting of rolled shapes, pipe, hollow structural clauses, plates, bars, sheets, rods or steel castings other than cold-formed steel or steel joist members.',2,'2.1','STEEL ELEMENT, STRUCTURAL','Any steel',156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001314"]','7d04aa60b9586384c1b19b80517370fc9f0c71a3f2c2ed109efe3424904e998e'),
('chunk-634','GHBC-CHUNK-000634','GHBC-C-000634','STEEL JOIST
Any steel structural member of a building or structure made of hot-rolled or cold-formed solid or open-web clauses, or riveted or welded bars, strip or sheet steel members, or splotted and expanded, or otherwise deformed rolled clauses.',2,'2.1','STEEL JOIST',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001315"]','39911a1e82acc331775079e6f7de4057df3d8eb8a270416b6fc43e2f4ca0c5cd'),
('chunk-635','GHBC-CHUNK-000635','GHBC-C-000635','STEEP SLOPE
A roof slope greater than two
units vertical in 12 units horizontal (17-percent slope).',2,'2.1','STEEP SLOPE','A roof slope greater than two',156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001316"]','7d102e891394ef371b3c122e30ae2dcfc61f29a5771ea283ba9180ba1622cc95'),
('chunk-636','GHBC-CHUNK-000636','GHBC-C-000636','STONE MASONRY
Masonry composed of field, quarried or cast stone units bonded by mortar.',2,'2.1','STONE MASONRY',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001317"]','baa149e7cb50dd987efd818a150e809c25c14611580308185515bcadac769da6'),
('chunk-637','GHBC-CHUNK-000637','GHBC-C-000637','STORAGE, HAZARDOUS MATERIALS
The keeping, retention or leaving of hazardous materials in closed containers, tanks, cylinders, or similar vessels; or vessels supplying operations through closed connections to the vessel.',2,'2.1','STORAGE, HAZARDOUS MATERIALS',NULL,156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001318"]','ae4a672d6248640f97429a05eb6450ac41c69ccb83819a3978111fcde077701d'),
('chunk-638','GHBC-CHUNK-000638','GHBC-C-000638','STORAGE RACKS
Cold-formed or hot-rolled
steel structural members which are formed into steel storage racks, including pallet storage racks, movable-shelf racks, rack-supported systems, automated storage and retrieval systems (stacker racks), push-back racks, pallet-flow racks, case-flow racks, pick modules and rack-supported platforms. Other types of racks, such as drive-in or drive-through racks, cantilever racks, portable racks or racks made of materials other than steel, are not
considered storage racks for the purpose of this Code.',2,'2.1','STORAGE RACKS','Cold-formed or hot-rolled',156,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001319","GHBC-REQ-001320","GHBC-REQ-001321"]','43b50ec97bbed321469883c56e8ad054d5bc15aa3464685bcd14e56d1bac2898'),
('chunk-639','GHBC-CHUNK-000639','GHBC-C-000639','STORM SHELTER
A building, structure or portions thereof, constructed in accordance with this Code and designated for use during a severe wind storm event.
Community storm shelter. A storm shelter not defined as a ―Residential storm shelter.‖
Residential storm shelter. A storm shelter serving occupants of dwelling units and having an occupant load not exceeding 16 persons.',2,'2.1','STORM SHELTER',NULL,157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001322","GHBC-REQ-001323","GHBC-REQ-001324","GHBC-REQ-001325","GHBC-REQ-001326"]','3c3d86dcf1e52360532d8cadc2ce6fdf310353ea937afeb6e7684e67b3487440'),
('chunk-640','GHBC-CHUNK-000640','GHBC-C-000640','STOREY
That portion of a building included
between the upper surface of a floor and the upper surface of the floor or roof next above (see ―Basement,‖ ―Building height,‖ ―Grade plane‖ and ―Mezzanine‖). A storey is measured as the vertical distance from top to top of two successive tiers of beams or finished floor surfaces and, for the topmost storey, from the top of the floor finish to the top of the ceiling joists or, where there is not a ceiling, to the top of the roof rafters.',2,'2.1','STOREY','That portion of a building included',157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001327","GHBC-REQ-001328"]','ae66d061372daf5aa849cb5962163da8436fa0e116ba136c65cf1a38532011e8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-641','GHBC-CHUNK-000641','GHBC-C-000641','STOREY ABOVE GRADE PLANE
Any storey
having its finished floor surface entirely above grade plane, or in which the finished surface of the floor next above is:
1. More than 1829 mm (6 feet) above grade plane; or
2. More than 3658 mm (12 feet) above the finished ground level at any point.
STRUCTURAL COMPOSITE',2,'2.1','STOREY ABOVE GRADE PLANE','Any storey',157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001329","GHBC-REQ-001330","GHBC-REQ-001331","GHBC-REQ-001332","GHBC-REQ-001333","GHBC-REQ-001334"]','55df7f67b1be955fb9bd550c4bff9f604ed59517081b6292035e83db82033c09'),
('chunk-642','GHBC-CHUNK-000642','GHBC-C-000642','TIMBER
Structural member manufactured using wood elements bonded together with exterior adhesives. Examples of structural composite timber are:
Laminated strand timber (LST). A composite of wood strand elements with wood fibers primarily oriented along the length of the member, where the least dimension of the wood strand elements is 0.10 inch (2.54 mm) or less and their average lengths not less than 150 times the least dimension of the wood strand elements.
Laminated veneer timber (LVT). A composite of wood veneer sheet elements with wood fibers primarily oriented along the length of the member, where the
veneer element thicknesses are 6.4 mm (0.25 inches) or less.
Oriented strand timber (OST). A composite of wood strand elements with wood fibers primarily oriented along the length of the member, where the least dimension of the wood strand elements is 2.54 mm (0.10 inches) or less and their average lengths not less than 75 times and less than 150 times the least dimension of the strand elements.
Parallel strand timber (PST). A composite of wood strand elements with wood fibers primarily oriented along the length of the member where the least dimension of the wood strand elements is 6.4 mm (0.25 inches) or less and their average lengths not less than 300 times the least dimension of the wood strand elements.
STRUCTURAL GLUED-LAMINATED',2,'2.1','TIMBER',NULL,157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001335","GHBC-REQ-001336","GHBC-REQ-001337","GHBC-REQ-001338","GHBC-REQ-001339","GHBC-REQ-001340","GHBC-REQ-001341","GHBC-REQ-001342","GHBC-REQ-001343","GHBC-REQ-001344","GHBC-REQ-001345","GHBC-REQ-001346"]','068fef2b3a55e6eac5b551e561bfa3ade2222a61576172e571a637819b139da6'),
('chunk-643','GHBC-CHUNK-000643','GHBC-C-000643','TIMBER
An engineered, stress-rated product
of a timber laminating plant, comprised of assemblies of specially selected and prepared wood laminations in which the grain of all laminations is approximately parallel longitudinally and the laminations are bonded with adhesives.',2,'2.1','TIMBER','An engineered, stress-rated product',157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001347"]','a628b2b2f0500f7cf687e2ca6f32d23f5c845196f3a095fbd63efcea02140912'),
('chunk-644','GHBC-CHUNK-000644','GHBC-C-000644','STRUCTURAL OBSERVATION
The visual
observation of the structural system by a registered design professional for general conformance to the approved construction documents.',2,'2.1','STRUCTURAL OBSERVATION','The visual',157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001348"]','fd294b2e511a672f0605849e28bed3b19361a3748df843801e83f2e43f026e80'),
('chunk-645','GHBC-CHUNK-000645','GHBC-C-000645','STRUCTURE
That which is built or constructed.',2,'2.1','STRUCTURE',NULL,157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001349"]','1d071275efeba53e5c1c2e1a001f66312e26009f3be069c01f820693189c93d0'),
('chunk-646','GHBC-CHUNK-000646','GHBC-C-000646','SUBSTANTIAL DAMAGE
Damage of any
origin sustained by a structure whereby the cost of restoring the structure to its beforedamaged condition would equal or exceed 50 percent of the market value of the structure before the damage occurred.',2,'2.1','SUBSTANTIAL DAMAGE','Damage of any',157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001350"]','6c058901354057ff37d587d38a231a065f3a2be22c6015387d7d8a563b71cb68'),
('chunk-647','GHBC-CHUNK-000647','GHBC-C-000647','SUBSTANTIAL IMPROVEMENT
Any repair,
reconstruction, rehabilitation, alteration, addition or other improvement of a building or structure, the cost of which equals or exceeds 50 percent of the market value of the structure before the improvement or repair is started. If the structure has sustained substantial damage, any repairs are considered substantial improvement regardless of the actual repair work performed. The term does not, however, include either:
1. Any project for improvement of a building required to correct existing
health, sanitary or safety Code violations identified by the Head of Works and that are the minimum necessary to assure safe living conditions.
2. Any alteration of a historic structure provided that the alteration will not preclude the structure‘s continued designation as a historic structure.',2,'2.1','SUBSTANTIAL IMPROVEMENT','Any repair,',157,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001351","GHBC-REQ-001352","GHBC-REQ-001353","GHBC-REQ-001354","GHBC-REQ-001355","GHBC-REQ-001356","GHBC-REQ-001357","GHBC-REQ-001358"]','7cbd7609d9279e8411914726937e95dd759138c2928c8ad42d73435dd4d9842b'),
('chunk-648','GHBC-CHUNK-000648','GHBC-C-000648','SUPERVISING STATION
A facility that receives signals and at which personnel are in attendance at all times to respond to these signals.
SUPERVISORY',2,'2.1','SUPERVISING STATION',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001359","GHBC-REQ-001360"]','dcb9f2e72f50862d71002ca3720dff59d767c85b9361ebff1b53f309add9c376'),
('chunk-649','GHBC-CHUNK-000649','GHBC-C-000649','SERVICE
The service required to monitor performance of guard tours and the operative condition of fixed suppression systems or other systems for the protection of life and property.',2,'2.1','SERVICE',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001361"]','07d476e276367c4e11f442e23e7f077657acb7dbf741399ff610ca9c06d59a72'),
('chunk-650','GHBC-CHUNK-000650','GHBC-C-000650','SUPERVISORY SIGNAL
A signal indicating
the need of action in connection with the supervision of guard tours, the fire suppression systems or equipment or the maintenance features of related systems.
SUPERVISORY SIGNAL-INITIATING',2,'2.1','SUPERVISORY SIGNAL','A signal indicating',158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001362","GHBC-REQ-001363"]','5f0ff4d3dc616ed32ddf0b1db9484b26d09b46c3ca2adc850989f2f5143bb2e5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-651','GHBC-CHUNK-000651','GHBC-C-000651','DEVICE
An initiation device, such as a valve
supervisory switch, water-level indicator or lowair pressure switch on a dry-pipe sprinkler system, whose change of state signals an offnormal condition and its restoration to normal of a fire protection or life safety system, or a need for action in connection with guard tours, fire suppression systems or equipment or maintenance features of related systems.',2,'2.1','DEVICE','An initiation device, such as a valve',158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001364"]','faaa50a2512bcfeacf0d669b8ddf28c0d84e868404021420e2b6400d6162ddaf'),
('chunk-652','GHBC-CHUNK-000652','GHBC-C-000652','SUSCEPTIBLE BAY
A roof or portion thereof
with either of the following:
1. A slope less than1 / -inch per foot (0.0208 rad).4
2. On which water is impounded, in whole or in part, and the secondary drainage system is functional but the primary drainage system is blocked.
A roof surface with a slope of1 / -inch per foot (0.0208 rad) or greater towards points of4 free drainage is not a susceptible bay.',2,'2.1','SUSCEPTIBLE BAY','A roof or portion thereof',158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001365","GHBC-REQ-001366","GHBC-REQ-001367","GHBC-REQ-001368","GHBC-REQ-001369","GHBC-REQ-001370"]','f37de387e934029762f0e242c4e2d6e69e6e64db9caecd9b9e31b5db5439b7e5'),
('chunk-653','GHBC-CHUNK-000653','GHBC-C-000653','SWIMMING POOL
Any structure intended for swimming, recreational bathing or wading that contains water over 610 mm (24 inches) deep. This includes in-ground, above-ground and on-
ground pools; hot tubs; spas and fixed-in-place wading pools.',2,'2.1','SWIMMING POOL',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001371","GHBC-REQ-001372","GHBC-REQ-001373"]','53fd0ae29e3c00b0714f3707bbbfb84fbdffe889be914f77321b90d2c331a2d1'),
('chunk-654','GHBC-CHUNK-000654','GHBC-C-000654','TECHNICAL PRODUCTION AREA
Open
elevated areas or spaces intended for entertainment technicians to walk on and occupy for servicing and operating entertainment technology systems and equipment. Galleries, including fly and lighting galleries, gridirons, catwalks, and similar areas are designed for these purposes.
TENSILE MEMBRANE',2,'2.1','TECHNICAL PRODUCTION AREA','Open',158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001374","GHBC-REQ-001375","GHBC-REQ-001376"]','dcb397225d99341b39bc61ae16f77dc6eeaeeb0947f5b6bb8af2ccc36e789669'),
('chunk-655','GHBC-CHUNK-000655','GHBC-C-000655','STRUCTURE
A membrane structure having a shape that is determined by tension in the membrane and the geometry of the support structure. Typically, the structure consists of both flexible elements (e.g., membrane and cables), nonflexible elements (e.g., struts, masts, beams and arches) and the anchorage (e.g., supports and foundations). This includes frame-supported tensile membrane structures.',2,'2.1','STRUCTURE',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001377","GHBC-REQ-001378","GHBC-REQ-001379"]','4fcd4b602435b16acc3151b810d72b06fd0c64d50a358497cd52015db15e252f'),
('chunk-656','GHBC-CHUNK-000656','GHBC-C-000656','TENT
A structure, enclosure, umbrella structure or shelter, with or without sidewalls or drops, constructed of fabric or pliable material supported in any manner except by air or the contents it protects (see ―Umbrella structure‖).
THERMAL',2,'2.1','TENT',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001380","GHBC-REQ-001381"]','efb70c1c023a442fd0443753a78ecab886fd0152317f150d6c8c5f16db0b593f'),
('chunk-657','GHBC-CHUNK-000657','GHBC-C-000657','ISOLATION
A separation of conditioned spaces, between a sunroom and a dwelling unit, consisting of existing or new walls, doors or windows.
THERMOPLASTIC',2,'2.1','ISOLATION',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001382","GHBC-REQ-001383"]','174948074357088aa934181a26fb2b9c7b92a9608f49f64b76253814cebe0411'),
('chunk-658','GHBC-CHUNK-000658','GHBC-C-000658','MATERIAL
A plastic material that is capable of being repeatedly softened by increase of temperature and hardened by decrease of temperature.
THERMOSETTING',2,'2.1','MATERIAL',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001384","GHBC-REQ-001385"]','b79660f4b682c8bfd2364b70dd123630d6f78773c68c1ccb8fdf42a5b17610a0'),
('chunk-659','GHBC-CHUNK-000659','GHBC-C-000659','MATERIAL
A plastic material that is capable of being changed into a substantially nonreformable product when cured.',2,'2.1','MATERIAL',NULL,158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001386"]','bd6fee4a6b2fc99b3804a3e8889ecb26fea51fe3e9cda37a2e300670c837638c'),
('chunk-660','GHBC-CHUNK-000660','GHBC-C-000660','THROUGH PENETRATION
A breach in both
sides of a floor, floor-ceiling or wall assembly to accommodate an item passing through the breaches.
THROUGH-PENETRATION FIRESTOP',2,'2.1','THROUGH PENETRATION','A breach in both',158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001387","GHBC-REQ-001388"]','f4581a6fff25fd0b9c7cbda5258a8aed8e79b4cd252312a9f83d55d403b8ff10');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-661','GHBC-CHUNK-000661','GHBC-C-000661','SYSTEM
An assemblage consisting of a fire-
resistance-rated floor, floor-ceiling, or wall assembly, one or more penetrating items passing through the breaches in both sides of the assembly and the materials or devices, or both, installed to resist the spread of fire through the assembly for a prescribed period of time.',2,'2.1','SYSTEM','An assemblage consisting of a fire-',158,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001389"]','a46d4af490de4b354d01c525100a5b4136b7ba547a976af90543deca6d4cdbbd'),
('chunk-662','GHBC-CHUNK-000662','GHBC-C-000662','TIE, WALL
Metal connector that connects
Wythes of masonry walls together.',2,'2.1','TIE, WALL','Metal connector that connects',159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001390"]','3adc01d7d469c44dca6f66e67ab6a7ef4f3d6a9c7d27a77368d8b9d38ac251a5'),
('chunk-663','GHBC-CHUNK-000663','GHBC-C-000663','TIE-DOWN (HOLD-DOWN)
A device used to resist uplift of the chords of shear walls.',2,'2.1','TIE-DOWN (HOLD-DOWN)',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001391"]','cb8617047404c03d7e73ee621efc89a527c506d7e5990d97fccc11e31125f5a6'),
('chunk-664','GHBC-CHUNK-000664','GHBC-C-000664','TILE, STRUCTURAL CLAY
A hollow masonry
unit composed of burned clay, shale, fire clay or mixture thereof, and having parallel cells.',2,'2.1','TILE, STRUCTURAL CLAY','A hollow masonry',159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001392"]','762cfcff0aea54639d5308c0546a8e44c544b1cd8325ce65027b057b23facdf2'),
('chunk-665','GHBC-CHUNK-000665','GHBC-C-000665','TIRES, BULK STORAGE OF
Storage of tires
where the area available for storage exceeds 20,000 cubic feet (566 m3 ).',2,'2.1','TIRES, BULK STORAGE OF','Storage of tires',159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001393"]','4bc29aafcca7e09f3d3b98e56cc90eff8a5034c103b33304739087f5b469db5c'),
('chunk-666','GHBC-CHUNK-000666','GHBC-C-000666','TOWNHOUSE
A single-family dwelling unit
constructed in a group of three or more attached units in which each unit extends from the foundation to roof and with open space on at least two sides.',2,'2.1','TOWNHOUSE','A single-family dwelling unit',159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001394"]','0c4a94249ec3bd58c6337ca66c21a8db6b8cdce552b63ca943a1f94a6ad85b93'),
('chunk-667','GHBC-CHUNK-000667','GHBC-C-000667','TOXIC
A chemical falling within any of the following categories:
1. A chemical that has a median lethal dose (LD ) of more than 50 milligrams per kilogram, but not more50 than 500 milligrams per kilogram of body weight when administered orally to albino rats weighing between 200 and 300 grams each.
2. A chemical that has a median lethal dose (LD ) of more than 200 milligrams per kilogram, but not more50 than 1,000 milligrams per kilogram of body weight when administered by continuous contact for 24 hours (or less if death occurs within 24 hours) with the bare skin of albino rabbits weighing between 2 and 3 kilograms each.
3. A chemical that has a median lethal concentration (LC ) in air of more than 200 parts per million, but not more50 than 2,000 parts per million by volume of gas or vapour, or more than 2 milligrams per liter but not more than 20 milligrams per liter of mist, fume or dust, when administered by continuous inhalation for 1 hour (or less if death occurs within 1 hour) to albino rats weighing between 200 and 300 grams each.',2,'2.1','TOXIC',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001395","GHBC-REQ-001396","GHBC-REQ-001397","GHBC-REQ-001398","GHBC-REQ-001399","GHBC-REQ-001400","GHBC-REQ-001401"]','12d79c77d38f719026ae9f68c8a3b6aed6a5ae147f8204bd839f98eb8087e083'),
('chunk-668','GHBC-CHUNK-000668','GHBC-C-000668','TRANSIENT
Occupancy of a dwelling unit or sleeping unit for not more than 30 days.',2,'2.1','TRANSIENT',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001402"]','7741ccc2094000741cea6bf4877b0a06ca3050775803aedb0049fc631e94e56b'),
('chunk-669','GHBC-CHUNK-000669','GHBC-C-000669','TRANSIENT AIRCRAFT
