('chunk-673','GHBC-CHUNK-000673','GHBC-C-000673','TUBULAR DAYLIGHTING DEVICE (TDD)
A non-operable fenestration unit primarily designed to transmit daylight from a roof surface to an interior ceiling via a tubular conduit. The basic unit consists of an exterior glazed weathering surface, a light-transmitting tube with a reflective interior surface, and an interior-sealing device such as a translucent ceiling panel. The unit can be factory assembled, or field-assembled from a manufactured kit.
UMBRELLA',2,'2.1','TUBULAR DAYLIGHTING DEVICE (TDD)',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001411","GHBC-REQ-001412","GHBC-REQ-001413","GHBC-REQ-001414"]','c099442fa91852df0c223f8572707b2a980f5b7d9785005a42e000422fa25dfd'),
('chunk-674','GHBC-CHUNK-000674','GHBC-C-000674','STRUCTURE
A structure, enclosure or shelter with or without sidewalls or drops, constructed of fabric or pliable material supported by a central pole or poles (see ―Tent‖).',2,'2.1','STRUCTURE',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001415"]','08a5bba982d9482e1a0dbd5850b9c7929ef1d3109a3f18baf0eea973508dfb32'),
('chunk-675','GHBC-CHUNK-000675','GHBC-C-000675','UNDERLAYMENT
One or more layers of a material that is applied to a steep-slope roof covering deck under the roof covering and resists liquid water that penetrates the roof covering.
UNSTABLE (REACTIVE)',2,'2.1','UNDERLAYMENT',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001416","GHBC-REQ-001417"]','e94943b76af07ac2e5fe7845ed7e13b7017520140b10049005b2a69fe28ea9cc'),
('chunk-676','GHBC-CHUNK-000676','GHBC-C-000676','MATERIAL
A material, other than an explosive, which in the pure state or as commercially produced, will vigorously polymerize, decompose, condense or become self-reactive and undergo other violent chemical changes, including explosion, when exposed to heat, friction or shock, or in
the absence of an inhibitor, or in the presence of contaminants, or in contact with incompatible materials. Unstable (reactive) materials are subdivided as follows:
Class 4. Materials that in themselves are readily capable of detonation or explosive decomposition or explosive reaction at normal temperatures and pressures. This class includes materials that are sensitive to mechanical or localized thermal shock at normal temperatures and pressures.
Class 3. Materials that in themselves are capable of detonation or of explosive decomposition or explosive reaction but which require a strong initiating source or which must be heated under confinement before initiation. This class includes materials that are sensitive to thermal or mechanical shock at elevated temperatures and pressures.
Class 2. Materials that in themselves are normally unstable and readily undergo violent chemical change but do not detonate. This class includes materials that can undergo chemical change with rapid release of energy at normal temperatures and pressures, and that can undergo violent chemical change at elevated temperatures and pressures.
Class 1. Materials that in themselves are normally stable but which can become unstable at elevated temperatures and pressure.',2,'2.1','MATERIAL',NULL,159,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001418","GHBC-REQ-001419","GHBC-REQ-001420","GHBC-REQ-001421","GHBC-REQ-001422","GHBC-REQ-001423","GHBC-REQ-001424","GHBC-REQ-001425","GHBC-REQ-001426","GHBC-REQ-001427","GHBC-REQ-001428","GHBC-REQ-001429","GHBC-REQ-001430","GHBC-REQ-001431"]','6471412521d4b75c9ee1fc4c29b2c2ac12b70bd3a96d29dc840773e834e6a1cc'),
('chunk-677','GHBC-CHUNK-000677','GHBC-C-000677','VAPOUR PERMEABLE
The property of having a moisture vapour permeance rating of 10 5 perms (2.9 × 10-2 kg/Pa × s × m ) or greater, when tested in accordance with the desiccant method using Procedure A of ASTM E96. A vapour permeable material permits the passage of moisture vapour.',2,'2.1','VAPOUR PERMEABLE',NULL,160,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001432","GHBC-REQ-001433"]','8c3891701857fa8dcaff799484cf18b98411a6902ef53ef6dae3c1c2f8ed177a'),
('chunk-678','GHBC-CHUNK-000678','GHBC-C-000678','VAPOUR RETARDER CLASS
A measure of a material or assembly‘s ability to limit the amount of moisture that passes through that material or assembly. Vapour retarder class shall be defined using the desiccant method with Procedure A of ASTM E96 as follows:
Class I: 0.1 perm or less.
Class II: 0.1 < perm  1.0 perm.
Class III: 1.0 < perm  10 perm.
VEGETATIVE',2,'2.1','VAPOUR RETARDER CLASS',NULL,160,'["Table 601, which may or may not be of fire-"]','["GHBC-REQ-001434","GHBC-REQ-001435","GHBC-REQ-001436","GHBC-REQ-001437","GHBC-REQ-001438","GHBC-REQ-001439"]','84a244b55d97c3ac6e106458973c8ffa72b125f52229504cd5ddfe85d0b35f79'),
