('chunk-1942','GHBC-CHUNK-001942','GHBC-C-001942','8.16.1.1
Alternative methods for determining
fire protection ratings. The application of any of the alternative methods listed in this clause shall be based on the fire exposure and acceptance criteria specified in the Ghana Fire Code. The required fire resistance of an opening protective shall be permitted to be established by any of the following methods or procedures:
1. Designs documented in approved sources.
2. Calculations performed in an approved manner.
3. Engineering analysis based on a comparison of opening protective designs having fire protection ratings as determined by the test procedures set forth in the Ghana Fire Code.
4. Alternative protection methods as allowed by Clause 11.4.11.',8,NULL,'8.16.1.1','Alternative methods for determining',355,'["TABLE 8.22.2.1.2(2)","Table 8.22.2.1.2(2).","TABLE 8.22.2.1.4(1) MULTIPLYING FACTOR FOR FINISHES ON NON FIREEXPOSED SIDE OF","TABLE 8.22.2.1.4(2) TIME ASSIGNED TO FINISH MATERIALS ON FIRE-EXPOSED SIDE OF WALL","TABLE 8.22.2.2.1","TABLE 8.22.2.3(1)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(2)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3) MINIMUM COVER FOR MAIN REINFORCING BARS OF REINFORCED","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(4)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(5) MINIMUM COVER FOR PRESTRESSED CONCRETE BEAMS OF ALL WIDTHS","TABLE 8.22.2.4 MINIMUM DIMENSION OF","TABLE 8.22.3.2 MINIMUM EQUIVALENT THICKNESS (inches) OF BEARING OR NONBEARING","TABLE 8.22.3.4 MINIMUM COVER OF","TABLE 8.22.3.5 MINIMUM DIMENSION OF","TABLE 8.22.4.1(1)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(1)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(3)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(4)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(5)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(6) REINFORCED CLAY","Table 8.22.4.1(4) based on the actual thickness","Table 8.22.3.2 for concrete masonry units or","Table 8.22.4.1(1) or 8.22.4.1(2) for clay and tile","TABLE 8.22.5.1(1) W/D RATIOS FOR STEEL COLUMNS","TABLE 8.22.5.1(2) PROPERTIES OF CONCRETE","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4) WEIGHT-TO-HEATED-PERIMETER RATIOS (W/D) FOR TYPICAL WIDE","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(5) FIRE RESISTANCE OF CONCRETE MASONRY PROTECTED STEEL","TABLE 8.22.5.1(5)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(6)","TABLE 8.22.5.1(7) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS ENCASED IN","TABLE 8.22.5.1(9) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS IN NORMAL WEIGHT","TABLE 8.22.5.1(10) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS IN STRUCTURAL","Table 8.22.5.1(1) contains weight-to-heated-","TABLE 8.22.6.2(1)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(2)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(3)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(4)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(5)","Table 8.22.6.2(1) indicates the time assigned to","Table 8.22.6.2(5) indicates the time increme