('chunk-2080','GHBC-CHUNK-002080','GHBC-C-002080','8.21.1.4
Plaster application
The finish coat is not required for plaster protective coatings where those coatings comply with the design mix and thickness requirements of Tables 8.21.1(1), 8.21.1(2) and 8.21.1(3). 8.21.1.5 Bonded prestressed concrete tendons. For members having a single tendon or more than one tendon installed with equal concrete cover measured from the nearest surface, the cover shall be not less than that set forth in
tendons installed with variable concrete cover, the average tendon cover shall be not less than that set forth in Table 8.21.1(1), provided that:
1. The clearance from each tendon to the nearest exposed surface is used to determine the average cover. 2. The clear cover for individual tendons shall not be less than one-half of that set forth in Table 8.21.1(1). A minimum cover of 19.1 mm (3/4 inch) for slabs and 25 mm (1 inch) for beams is required for any aggregate concrete 3. For the purpose of establishing a fireresistance rating, tendons having a clear covering less than that set forth in Table 8.21.1(1) shall not contribute more than 50 percent of the required ultimate moment capacity for members less than 0.226 m2 (350 square inches) in cross-clauseal area and 65 percent for larger members. For structural design purposes, however, of concrete, concrete masonry and clay masonry assemblies shall be permitted in accordance with this Code. The calculated fire resistance of steel assemblies shall be permitted in accordance with Part 5 of ASCE 29. The calculated fire resistance of exposed
wood members and wood decking shall be permitted in accordance with this Code.',8,NULL,'8.21.1.4','Plaster application',397,'["TABLE 8.22.2.1.2(2)","Table 8.22.2.1.2(2).","TABLE 8.22.2.1.4(1) MULTIPLYING FACTOR FOR FINISHES ON NON FIREEXPOSED SIDE OF","TABLE 8.22.2.1.4(2) TIME ASSIGNED TO FINISH MATERIALS ON FIRE-EXPOSED SIDE OF WALL","TABLE 8.22.2.2.1","TABLE 8.22.2.3(1)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(2)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3) MINIMUM COVER FOR MAIN REINFORCING BARS OF REINFORCED","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(4)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(5) MINIMUM COVER FOR PRESTRESSED CONCRETE BEAMS OF ALL WIDTHS","TABLE 8.22.2.4 MINIMUM DIMENSION OF","TABLE 8.22.3.2 MINIMUM EQUIVALENT THICKNESS (inches) OF BEARING OR NONBEARING","TABLE 8.22.3.4 MINIMUM COVER OF","TABLE 8.22.3.5 MINIMUM DIMENSION OF","TABLE 8.22.4.1(1)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(1)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(3)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(4)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(5)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(6) REINFORCED CLAY","Table 8.22.4.1(4) based on the actual thickness","Table 8.22.3.2 for concrete masonry units or","Table 8.22.4.1(1) or 8.22.4.1(2) for clay and tile","TABLE 8.22.5.1(1) W/D RATIOS FOR STEEL COLUMNS","TABLE 8.22.5.1(2) PROPERTIES OF CONCRETE","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4) WEIGHT-TO-HEATED-PERIMETER RATIOS (W/D) FOR TYPICAL WIDE","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(5) FIRE RESISTANCE OF CONCRETE MASONRY PROTECTED STEEL","TABLE 8.22.5.1(5)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(6)","TABLE 8.22.5.1(7) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS ENCASED IN","TABLE 8.22.5.1(9) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS IN NORMAL WEIGHT","TABLE 8.22.5.1(10) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS IN STRUCTURAL","Table 8.22.5.1(1) contains weight-to-heated-","TABLE 8.22.6.2(1)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(2)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(3)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(4)","TABLE 8.22.6.2(5)","Table 8.22.6.2(1) indicates the time assigned to","Table 8.22.6.2(5) indicates the time incremen