('chunk-2103','GHBC-CHUNK-002103','GHBC-C-002103','8.22.2.2.1.3
Slabs with ribbed soffits
The thickness of slabs with ribbed or undulating soffits (see Figure 8.22.2.2.1.3) shall be determined by one of the following expressions, whichever is applicable:
For s > 4t, the thickness to be used shall be t
For s ≤ 2t, the thickness to be used shall be te
For 4t > s > 2t, the thickness to be used shall be
(Equation 8-5) Where: S = Spacing of ribs or undulations. T = Minimum thickness. Equivalent thickness of the slab te = calculated as the net area of the slab divided by the width, in which the maximum thickness used in the calculation shall not exceed 2t.
Note: For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm
