These procedures establish a basis for determining the fire resistance of column assemblies as a function of the thickness of fire-resistant material and, the weight, W, and heated perimeter, D, of structural steel columns. As used in these clauses, W is the average weight of a structural steel column in pounds per linear foot. The heated perimeter, D, is the inside perimeter of the fire-resistant material in inches as illustrated in Figure 8.22.5.1(1)',8,NULL,'8.22.5.1.1','General',427,'["TABLE 8.22.2.1.2(2)","Table 8.22.2.1.2(2).","TABLE 8.22.2.1.4(1) MULTIPLYING FACTOR FOR FINISHES ON NON FIREEXPOSED SIDE OF","TABLE 8.22.2.1.4(2) TIME ASSIGNED TO FINISH MATERIALS ON FIRE-EXPOSED SIDE OF WALL","TABLE 8.22.2.2.1","TABLE 8.22.2.3(1)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(2)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3) MINIMUM COVER FOR MAIN REINFORCING BARS OF REINFORCED","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(3)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(4)","TABLE 8.22.2.3(5) MINIMUM COVER FOR PRESTRESSED CONCRETE BEAMS OF ALL WIDTHS","TABLE 8.22.2.4 MINIMUM DIMENSION OF","TABLE 8.22.3.2 MINIMUM EQUIVALENT THICKNESS (inches) OF BEARING OR NONBEARING","TABLE 8.22.3.4 MINIMUM COVER OF","TABLE 8.22.3.5 MINIMUM DIMENSION OF","TABLE 8.22.4.1(1)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(1)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(3)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(4)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(5)","TABLE 8.22.4.1(6) REINFORCED CLAY","Table 8.22.4.1(4) based on the actual thickness","Table 8.22.3.2 for concrete masonry units or","Table 8.22.4.1(1) or 8.22.4.1(2) for clay and tile","TABLE 8.22.5.1(1) W/D RATIOS FOR STEEL COLUMNS","TABLE 8.22.5.1(2) PROPERTIES OF CONCRETE","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4) WEIGHT-TO-HEATED-PERIMETER RATIOS (W/D) FOR TYPICAL WIDE","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(4)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(5) FIRE RESISTANCE OF CONCRETE MASONRY PROTECTED STEEL","TABLE 8.22.5.1(5)—continued","TABLE 8.22.5.1(6)","TABLE 8.22.5.1(7) MINIMUM COVER (inch) FOR STEEL COLUMNS ENCASED IN","TABLE 8.22.5.1(9) MINIMUM