Scope
Roof coverings shall be applied in accordance with the applicable provisions of this clause and the manufacturer‘s installation instructions.',16,'16.7','16.7.1','Scope',625,'["TABLE 16.7.1.1(1) UNDERLAYMENT TYPES","TABLE 16.7.1.1(2) UNDERLAYMENT APPLICATION","TABLE 16.7.1.1(3): UNDERLAYMENT ATTACHMENT","TABLE 16.7.2.8.2: VALLEY LINING","TABLE 16.7.3.7: CLAY AND CONCRETE TILE ATTACHMENTa, b, c","TABLE 16.7.4.3(1): METAL ROOF","TABLE 16.7.4.3(2): MINIMUM CORROSION","Table 16.7.4.3(1). The valley flashing shall","TABLE 16.7.7.6: SLATE SHINGLE HEADLAP","TABLE 16.7.8: WOOD SHINGLE AND SHAKE INSTALLATION","Table 16.7.8.5.","TABLE 16.7.8.5: WOOD SHINGLE","TABLE 16.7.8.7: WOOD SHINGLE WEATHER EXPOSURE AND ROOF SLOPE","TABLE 16.7.10.2: BUILT-UP ROOFING","TABLE 16.7.14.3: PROTECTIVE COATING"]','["GHBC-REQ-012095"]','d621c283773f3d50631602e8930d3b15ed0716adefd325ed35ca86d368afb6fd'),
('chunk-3428','GHBC-CHUNK-003428','GHBC-C-003428','16.7.1.1
Underlayment
Underlayment for asphalt shingles, clay and concrete tile, metal roof shingles, mineralsurfaced roll roofing, slate and slate-type shingles, wood shingles, wood shakes, metal roof panels and photovoltaic shingles shall conform to the applicable standards listed in this part. Underlayment materials required to comply with ASTM D226, D1970, D4869 and D6757 shall bear a label indicating compliance with the standard designation and, if applicable, type classification indicated in Table 16.7.1.1(1). Underlayment shall be applied in accordance with Table 16.7.1.1(2). Underlayment shall be attached in accordance with Table 16.7.1.1(3).
Exceptions:
1. As an alternative, self-adhering polymer modified bitumen underlayment complying with ASTM D1970 and installed in accordance with the manufacturer‘s installation instructions for the deck material, roof ventilation configuration and climate exposure for the roof covering to be installed shall be permitted.
2. As an alternative, a minimum 102 mmwide (4-inch) strip of self-adhering polymer modified bitumen membrane complying with ASTM D1970 and installed in accordance with the manufacturer‘s installation instructions for the deck material shall be applied over all joints in the roof decking. An
approved underlayment for the applicable roof covering for design wind speeds less than 54 m/s (120 mph) shall be applied over the 102 mm -wide (4-inch) membrane strips.
3. As an alternative, two layers of underlayment complying with ASTM D226 Type I or ASTM D4869 Type III shall be permitted to be installed as follows: Apply a 19-inch (483 mm) strip of underlayment parallel with the eave. Starting at the eave, apply 36-inch-wide (914 mm) strips of underlayment felt, overlapping successive 483 mm sheets (19 inches). The underlayment shall be attached with corrosion-resistant fasteners in a grid pattern of 305 mm (12 inches) between side laps with a 6inch (152 mm) spacing at side and end laps. End laps shall be 102 mm (4 inches) and shall be offset by 1829 mm (6 feet). Underlayment shall be attached using metal or plastic cap nails with a nominal cap diameter of not less than 25.4 mm (1 inch). Metal caps shall have a thickness of not less than 32-gage sheet metal. Power-driven metal caps shall have a thickness of not less than 0.010 inch (mm). Thickness of the outside edge of plastic caps shall be not less than 0.035 inch (mm). The cap nail shank shall be not less than 0.083 inch for ring shank cap nails and 0.091 inch (mm) for smooth shank cap nails. The cap nail shank shall have a length sufficient to penetrate through the roof sheathing or (3 not less than 19.1 mm / inch) into the roof sheathing.4
4. Structural metal panels that do not require a substrate or underlayment.
Note: For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 foot = 304.8 mm; 1 mile per hour = 0.447 m/s.
Note: For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm; 1 mile per hour = 0.447 m/s.
Exception: Detached accessory structures that do not contain conditioned floor area.',16,'16.7','16.7.1.1','Underlayment',625,'["TABLE 16.7.1.1(1) UNDERLAYMENT TYPES","TABLE 16.7.1.1(2) UNDERLAYMENT APPLICATION","TABLE 16.7.1.1(3): UNDERLAYMENT ATTACHMENT","TABLE 16.7.2.8.2: VALLEY LINING","TABLE 16.7.3.7: CLAY AND CONCRETE TILE ATTACHMENTa, b, c","TABLE 16.7.4.3(1): METAL ROOF","TABLE 16.7.4.3(2): MINIMUM CORROSION","Table 16.7.4.3(1). The valley flashing shall","TABLE 16.7.7.6: SLATE SHINGLE HEADLAP","TABLE 16.7.8: WOOD SHINGLE AND SHAKE INSTALLATION","Table 16.7.8.5.","TABLE 16.7.8.5: WOOD SHINGLE","TABLE 16.7.8.7: WOOD SHINGLE WEATHER EXPOSURE AND ROOF SLOPE","TABLE 16.7.10.2: BUILT-UP ROOFING","TABLE 16.7.14.3: PROTECTIVE COATING"]','["GHBC-REQ-012096","GHBC-REQ-012097","GHBC-REQ-012098","GHBC-REQ-012099","GHBC-REQ-012100","GHBC-REQ-012101","GHBC-REQ-012102","GHBC-REQ-012103","GHBC-REQ-012104","GHBC-REQ-012105","GHBC-REQ-012106","GHBC-REQ-012107","GHBC-REQ-012108","GHBC-REQ-012109","GHBC-REQ-012110","GHBC-REQ-012111","GHBC-REQ-012112","GHBC-REQ-012113","GHBC-REQ-012114","GHBC-REQ-012115","GHBC-REQ-012116","GHBC-REQ-012117","GHBC-REQ-012118","GHBC-REQ-012119","GHBC-REQ-012120","GHBC-REQ-012121","GHBC-REQ-012122"]','786dfd7df56a9e433fffc104597a57ff09c71a496fb27889d8c201ff9ae8f73c'),
