A drip edge shall be provided at eaves and rake edges of shingle roofs. Adjacent segments of the drip edge shall be lapped not less than 51 mm (2 inches). The vertical leg of drip edges shall be not less than 38 mm (11 / inches) in width and shall extend not less than 6.4 mm2 (1 / inch) below sheathing. The drip edge shall extend back on the roof not less than 51 mm (24 inches). Underlayment shall be installed over drip edges along eaves. Drip edges shall be installed over underlayment along rake edges. Drip edges shall be mechanically fastened at intervals not greater than 305 mm (12 inches) on center.',16,'16.7','16.7.2.8.3','Drip edge',630,'["TABLE 16.7.1.1(1) UNDERLAYMENT TYPES","TABLE 16.7.1.1(2) UNDERLAYMENT APPLICATION","TABLE 16.7.1.1(3): UNDERLAYMENT ATTACHMENT","TABLE 16.7.2.8.2: VALLEY LINING","TABLE 16.7.3.7: CLAY AND CONCRETE TILE ATTACHMENTa, b, c","TABLE 16.7.4.3(1): METAL ROOF","TABLE 16.7.4.3(2): MINIMUM CORROSION","Table 16.7.4.3(1). The valley flashing shall","TABLE 16.7.7.6: SLATE SHINGLE HEADLAP","TABLE 16.7.8: WOOD SHINGLE AND SHAKE INSTALLATION","Table 16.7.8.5.","TABLE 16.7.8.5: WOOD SHINGLE","TABLE 16.7.8.7: WOOD SHINGLE WEATHER EXPOSURE AND ROOF SLOPE","TABLE 16.7.10.2: BUILT-UP ROOFING","TABLE 16.7.14.3: PROTECTIVE COATING"]','["GHBC-REQ-012149","GHBC-REQ-012150","GHBC-REQ-012151","GHBC-REQ-012152","GHBC-REQ-012153","GHBC-REQ-012154","GHBC-REQ-012155"]','c059750392cad89550e7d630e9a5164f040302682805d5aeeda0ae666c1d9279'),
