('chunk-3475','GHBC-CHUNK-003475','GHBC-C-003475','16.7.7.7
Flashing
Flashing and counterflashing shall be made with sheet metal. Valley flashing shall be not less than 381 mm (15 inches) wide. Valley and flashing metal shall be a minimum uncoated thickness of 0.455 mm (0.0179-inch) zinccoated G90. Chimneys, stucco or brick walls shall have not fewer than two plies of felt for a cap flashing consisting of a 102 mm -wide (4inch) strip of felt set in plastic cement and extending 25 mm (1 inch) above the first felt and a top coating of plastic cement. The felt shall extend over the base flashing 51 mm (2 inches).',16,'16.7','16.7.7.7','Flashing',634,'["TABLE 16.7.1.1(1) UNDERLAYMENT TYPES","TABLE 16.7.1.1(2) UNDERLAYMENT APPLICATION","TABLE 16.7.1.1(3): UNDERLAYMENT ATTACHMENT","TABLE 16.7.2.8.2: VALLEY LINING","TABLE 16.7.3.7: CLAY AND CONCRETE TILE ATTACHMENTa, b, c","TABLE 16.7.4.3(1): METAL ROOF","TABLE 16.7.4.3(2): MINIMUM CORROSION","Table 16.7.4.3(1). The valley flashing shall","TABLE 16.7.7.6: SLATE SHINGLE HEADLAP","TABLE 16.7.8: WOOD SHINGLE AND SHAKE INSTALLATION","Table 16.7.8.5.","TABLE 16.7.8.5: WOOD SHINGLE","TABLE 16.7.8.7: WOOD SHINGLE WEATHER EXPOSURE AND ROOF SLOPE","TABLE 16.7.10.2: BUILT-UP ROOFING","TABLE 16.7.14.3: PROTECTIVE COATING"]','["GHBC-REQ-012262","GHBC-REQ-012263","GHBC-REQ-012264","GHBC-REQ-012265","GHBC-REQ-012266"]','57131a4e148a77f8984eb376d87ef1f373a36ab807bb4cd7294de15ecca074d1'),
