Underlayment shall be applied shingle fashion, parallel to and starting from the eave, lapped 51 mm (2 inches) and fastened sufficiently to hold in place.',16,'16.7','16.7.18.4','Underlayment application',639,'["TABLE 16.7.1.1(1) UNDERLAYMENT TYPES","TABLE 16.7.1.1(2) UNDERLAYMENT APPLICATION","TABLE 16.7.1.1(3): UNDERLAYMENT ATTACHMENT","TABLE 16.7.2.8.2: VALLEY LINING","TABLE 16.7.3.7: CLAY AND CONCRETE TILE ATTACHMENTa, b, c","TABLE 16.7.4.3(1): METAL ROOF","TABLE 16.7.4.3(2): MINIMUM CORROSION","Table 16.7.4.3(1). The valley flashing shall","TABLE 16.7.7.6: SLATE SHINGLE HEADLAP","TABLE 16.7.8: WOOD SHINGLE AND SHAKE INSTALLATION","Table 16.7.8.5.","TABLE 16.7.8.5: WOOD SHINGLE","TABLE 16.7.8.7: WOOD SHINGLE WEATHER EXPOSURE AND ROOF SLOPE","TABLE 16.7.10.2: BUILT-UP ROOFING","TABLE 16.7.14.3: PROTECTIVE COATING"]','["GHBC-REQ-012333"]','962ef6cfb5afc29a1043d42e0b2983748e6ef6cc9f2d3bb33b5458db05962688'),
('chunk-3517','GHBC-CHUNK-003517','GHBC-C-003517','16.7.18.4.1
High-wind attachment
Underlayment applied in areas subject to high winds [Vasd greater than 110 mph (49 m/s) as determined in accordance with Clause 1609.3.1 shall be applied in accordance with the manufacturer‘s instructions. Fasteners shall be
applied along the overlap at not more than 914 mm (36 inches) on center. Underlayment installed where Vasd is not less than 120 mph (54 m/s) shall comply with ASTM D226, Type II, ASTM D4869, Type III or ASTM D6757. The underlayment shall be attached in a grid pattern of 305 mm (12 inches) between side laps with a 152 mm (6-inch) spacing at the side laps. The underlayment shall be applied in accordance with Clause 16.7.2.8 except all laps shall be not less than 102 mm (4 inches). Underlayment shall be attached using cap nails or cap staples. Caps shall be metal or plastic with a nominal head diameter of not less than 25.4 mm (1 inch). Metal caps shall have a thickness of not less than 0.25 mm (0.010 inch). Power-driven metal caps shall have a thickness of not less than 0.25 mm (0.010 inch). Thickness of the outside edge of plastic caps shall be not less than 0.89 mm (0.035 inch). The cap nail shank shall be not less than 2.11 mm (0.083 inch) for ring shank cap nails and 2.31 mm (0.091 inch) for smooth shank cap nails. Staple gage shall be not less than 21 gage [0.81 mm (0.0.2 inch)]. Cap nail shank and cap staple legs shall have a length',16,'16.7','16.7.18.4.1','High-wind attachment',639,'["TABLE 16.7.1.1(1) UNDERLAYMENT TYPES","TABLE 16.7.1.1(2) UNDERLAYMENT APPLICATION","TABLE 16.7.1.1(3): UNDERLAYMENT ATTACHMENT","TABLE 16.7.2.8.2: VALLEY LINING","TABLE 16.7.3.7: CLAY AND CONCRETE TILE ATTACHMENTa, b, c","TABLE 16.7.4.3(1): METAL ROOF","TABLE 16.7.4.3(2): MINIMUM CORROSION","Table 16.7.4.3(1). The valley flashing shall","TABLE 16.7.7.6: SLATE SHINGLE HEADLAP","TABLE 16.7.8: WOOD SHINGLE AND SHAKE INSTALLATION","Table 16.7.8.5.","TABLE 16.7.8.5: WOOD SHINGLE","TABLE 16.7.8.7: WOOD SHINGLE WEATHER EXPOSURE AND ROOF SLOPE","TABLE 16.7.10.2: BUILT-UP ROOFING","TABLE 16.7.14.3: PROTECTIVE COATING"]','["GHBC-REQ-012334","GHBC-REQ-012335","GHBC-REQ-012336","GHBC-REQ-012337","GHBC-REQ-012338","GHBC-REQ-012339","GHBC-REQ-012340","GHBC-REQ-012341","GHBC-REQ-012342","GHBC-REQ-012343","GHBC-REQ-012344","GHBC-REQ-012345","GHBC-REQ-012346","GHBC-REQ-012347"]','36bca539124a58d6e7db4b45d2951402c661a7e7166ad2214790aa1232dfda1a'),
