('chunk-3616','GHBC-CHUNK-003616','GHBC-C-003616','For the purpose of calculating the wind forces that act in a way as to deform a cylindrical structure the values of Cpe in Table 17.22 may be used. They apply only in supercritical flow (i.e. they should only be used where D > 0.3m). They may be used for wind blowing normal to the axis of cylinders having their axis normal to the ground plane (i.e. chimneys, silos) and to cylinders having their axis parallel with the ground plane (i.e. horizontal tanks) provided the clearance between the tank and the ground is not less than D. h is the height of a vertical cylinder or length of a horizontal cylinder. Where there is a free flow of air around both ends, h is to be taken as half the length when calculating h/D. Interpolation may be used for intermediate values of h/D. In the calculation of the load
on the periphery of the cylinder, the value Cpi shall be taken into account. For open ended cylinders where h/D 0.3;     Cpi may be taken as -0.8. For open ended cylinders where h/D 0.3;    Cpi may be taken as -0.5
