DL II and DL III Structures Unless special proofs for exemption are given, the following dimensional limitations shall be satisfied (i) The width shall not be less than 200mm or more than the width of the supporting column, plus lengths, on each side of this member not exceeding one fourth of the depth of the column cross clause. (ii) The ratio b/h shall not be less than 0.25
(iii) The ratio l/h shall not be less than 4 (This requirement does not apply to coupling beams in wall structures, Clause 5.10.7.3(3).(Fig 17.10.8.1) (iv) The eccentricity of any beam relative to the columns into which if frames as measured by the distance between geometrical centre lines of the two members shall not exceed 1/4 bc   (Fig 17.10.8.2)
