Distance between supports, inches = s (mm). S
Thickness of the test specimen = t measured parallel to the direction of load, inches (mm). The applied load at failure, pounds P = (N).',22,'22.9','22.9.2.1.2.4','Modulus of rupture',826,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015651","GHBC-REQ-015652","GHBC-REQ-015653","GHBC-REQ-015654","GHBC-REQ-015655","GHBC-REQ-015656","GHBC-REQ-015657","GHBC-REQ-015658","GHBC-REQ-015659","GHBC-REQ-015660"]','a042a4761743f382d4ac0c4d69e98f1bc875391b3366a031ddaa43aa11e2e680'),
('chunk-4102','GHBC-CHUNK-004102','GHBC-C-004102','22.9.2.1.3
Moisture content requirements
Adobe units shall have a moisture content not exceeding 4 percent by weight.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.1.3','Moisture content requirements',826,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015661"]','4d52da4175d486efafb9c87886899246da630a8b42a322754e8a5851f65dae52'),
('chunk-4103','GHBC-CHUNK-004103','GHBC-C-004103','22.9.2.1.4
Shrinkage cracks
Adobe units shall not contain more than three shrinkage cracks and any single shrinkage crack shall not exceed 76 mm (3 inches) in length or 3.2 mm (1 / inch) in width.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.1.4','Shrinkage cracks',826,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015662"]','12399639baaed43cc197827e014abbc5adb48ec40967312433ddc9719165ee04'),
('chunk-4104','GHBC-CHUNK-004104','GHBC-C-004104','22.9.2.2
Stabilized adobe.8
Stabilized adobe shall comply with Clause 22.9.2.1 for unstabilized adobe in addition to Clauses 22.9.2.2.1 and 22.9.2.2.2.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.2','Stabilized adobe.8',826,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015663"]','d1807b4f6917c24819a5b010817ec978b5163bf824c70b5e4ef6d74f135646ad'),
('chunk-4105','GHBC-CHUNK-004105','GHBC-C-004105','22.9.2.2.1
Soil requirements
Soil used for stabilized adobe units shall be chemically compatible with the stabilizing material.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.2.1','Soil requirements',826,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015664"]','0eaf40d358fdd8158fcc23a00b6e98fb47b93feea4f1e9bb309b90f1cc058256'),
('chunk-4106','GHBC-CHUNK-004106','GHBC-C-004106','22.9.2.2.2
Absorption requirements
A 102 mm (4-inch) cube, cut from a stabilized adobe unit dried to a constant weight in a ventilated oven at 212°F to 239°F (100°C to 115°C), shall not absorb more than 21 / percent moisture by weight when placed on a constantly2 water-saturated, porous surface for seven days. Not fewer than five specimens shall be tested
and each specimen shall be cut from a separate unit.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.2.2','Absorption requirements',826,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015665","GHBC-REQ-015666","GHBC-REQ-015667"]','2bb3aa3789f63b2337e107d77b55383112d2b04dee785536b91853972aef2a68'),
('chunk-4107','GHBC-CHUNK-004107','GHBC-C-004107','22.9.2.3
Allowable stress
The allowable compressive stress based on gross cross-clauseal area of adobe shall not exceed 207 kPa (30 psi).',22,'22.9','22.9.2.3','Allowable stress',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015668"]','a814110e0261c4a3273bac69e120c75cfc6bc5af1558599b34476fbc0ea1b8e5'),
('chunk-4108','GHBC-CHUNK-004108','GHBC-C-004108','22.9.2.3.1
Bolts
Bolt values shall not exceed those set forth in
BOLTS IN ADOBE MASONRY For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 pound = 4.448 N.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.3.1','Bolts',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015669","GHBC-REQ-015670"]','06e8ad878b049996c5e0f31c8acb5b9ac4b2f9ff596ba020c2ee717082fc2096'),
('chunk-4109','GHBC-CHUNK-004109','GHBC-C-004109','22.9.2.4
Detailed requirements
Adobe construction shall comply with Clauses 22.9.2.4.1 through 22.9.2.4.9.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4','Detailed requirements',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015671"]','c24eedbd74f08ac6dba190868519008dbf248893b5eac8ffe34ad1d1dde045e8'),
('chunk-4110','GHBC-CHUNK-004110','GHBC-C-004110','22.9.2.4.1
Number of stories
Adobe construction shall be limited to buildings not exceeding one storey, except that twostorey construction is allowed where designed by a registered design professional.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.1','Number of stories',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015672"]','8ae6b41d0d21233acbd07bad15545a3d81b9b8529611364289f5a084f66b481b');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4111','GHBC-CHUNK-004111','GHBC-C-004111','22.9.2.4.2
Mortar
Mortar for adobe construction shall comply with Clauses 22.9.2.4.2.1 and 22.9.2.4.2.2.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.2','Mortar',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015673"]','aab3d879a1c179a2c5c1c5dcae8f4938bc63365303e4589096037dd55cc58940'),
('chunk-4112','GHBC-CHUNK-004112','GHBC-C-004112','22.9.2.4.2.1
General
Mortar for adobe units shall be in accordance with Clause 22.3.2.1, or be composed of adobe soil of the same composition and stabilization as the adobe brick units. Unstabilized adobe soil mortar is permitted in conjunction with unstabilized adobe brick units.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.2.1','General',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015674","GHBC-REQ-015675"]','6c8c2cc6625c81182347997cd59a87c49303defc33a75478670ec159d0bda8c2'),
('chunk-4113','GHBC-CHUNK-004113','GHBC-C-004113','22.9.2.4.2.2
Mortar joints
Adobe units shall be laid with full head and bed joints and in full running bond.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.2.2','Mortar joints',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015676"]','7e6f734ba25b27142bf21a31525e24801af857fd4f743e68f3d07d7661178ac5'),
('chunk-4114','GHBC-CHUNK-004114','GHBC-C-004114','22.9.2.4.3
Parapet walls
Parapet walls constructed of adobe units shall be waterproofed.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.3','Parapet walls',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015677"]','e6170cc9cd064f817017304486286628d10a428f313c7faee145efed27fab107'),
('chunk-4115','GHBC-CHUNK-004115','GHBC-C-004115','22.9.2.4.5.1
Foundation support
Walls and partitions constructed of adobe units shall be supported by foundations or footings that extend not less than 152 mm (6 inches) above adjacent ground surfaces and are constructed of solid masonry (excluding adobe) or concrete. Footings and foundations shall comply with Part 18.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.5.1','Foundation support',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015678","GHBC-REQ-015679"]','6daaba7746a3ec4f79fb280192497a2fd00bf73c216a8a0bab084cd51382bebb'),
('chunk-4116','GHBC-CHUNK-004116','GHBC-C-004116','22.9.2.4.5.2
Lower course requirements
Stabilized adobe units shall be used in adobe walls for the first 102 mm (4 inches) above the finished first-floor elevation.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.5.2','Lower course requirements',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015680"]','c40ed9ee8a64789c086d3642dc8561f7c07716925d0925b2c24c408de75bfe4c'),
('chunk-4117','GHBC-CHUNK-004117','GHBC-C-004117','22.9.2.4.6
Isolated piers or columns
Adobe units shall not be used for isolated piers or columns in a load-bearing capacity. Walls
less than 24 inches (610 mm) in length shall be considered to be isolated piers or columns.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.6','Isolated piers or columns',827,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015681","GHBC-REQ-015682","GHBC-REQ-015683"]','3eaffe476ff413f741bb06ace646bc88d72f256b420cd4759377efd9a8ed7501'),
('chunk-4118','GHBC-CHUNK-004118','GHBC-C-004118','22.9.2.4.7
Tie beams
Exterior walls and interior load-bearing walls constructed of adobe units shall have a continuous tie beam at the level of the floor or roof bearing and meeting the following requirements.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.7','Tie beams',828,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015684"]','2c2f66c335f36ee98b49573c9e6d14c25a6a1a07274197591c245045d0131c44'),
('chunk-4119','GHBC-CHUNK-004119','GHBC-C-004119','22.9.2.4.7.1
Concrete tie beams
Concrete tie beams shall be 152 mm (6 inches) or more in depth and 254 mm (10 inches) or more in width. Concrete tie beams shall be continuously reinforced with not fewer than two No. 4 reinforcing bars. The specified compressive strength of concrete shall be not less than 17.2 MPa (2,500 psi).',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.7.1','Concrete tie beams',828,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015685","GHBC-REQ-015686","GHBC-REQ-015687"]','2ee35b5b8473b18d789205b9a8e5c11dc3f1d61d84ce28addc5b0aad42fd2a83'),
('chunk-4120','GHBC-CHUNK-004120','GHBC-C-004120','22.9.2.4.7.2
Wood tie beams
Wood tie beams shall be solid or built up of timber having a nominal thickness of not less than 25 mm (1 inch), and shall have a depth of not less than 152 mm (6 inches) and a width of not less than 254 mm (10 inches). Joints in wood tie beams shall be spliced not less than 152 mm (6 inches). Splices shall not be allowed within 305 mm (12 inches) of an opening. Wood used in tie beams shall be approved naturally decay-resistant or preservative-treated wood.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.7.2','Wood tie beams',828,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015688","GHBC-REQ-015689","GHBC-REQ-015690","GHBC-REQ-015691"]','80a47f261c5b678c1301ead770ee4736b08896a435ae967dddb932777ea6fb65');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4121','GHBC-CHUNK-004121','GHBC-C-004121','22.9.2.4.8
Exterior finish
Exterior walls constructed of unstabilized adobe units shall have their exterior surface covered with not fewer than two coats of Portland cement plaster having a minimum thickness of 19.1 mm (3 / inch) and conforming to ASTM C926. Lathing shall comply4 with ASTM C1063. Fasteners shall be spaced at 406 mm (16 inches) on center maximum. Exposed wood surfaces shall be treated with an approved wood preservative or other protective coating prior to lath application.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.8','Exterior finish',828,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015692","GHBC-REQ-015693","GHBC-REQ-015694","GHBC-REQ-015695"]','edb895ab41bb190b2f58a3fa1003f9ebbd3d13a3a0873f6296d27d8a287cb87f'),
('chunk-4122','GHBC-CHUNK-004122','GHBC-C-004122','22.9.2.4.9
Lintels
Lintels shall be considered to be structural
members and shall be designed in accordance with the applicable provisions of Part 17.',22,'22.9','22.9.2.4.9','Lintels',828,'["Table 22.9.2.3.1.","TABLE 22.9.2.3.1 ALLOWABLE SHEAR ON"]','["GHBC-REQ-015696","GHBC-REQ-015697"]','57daf4e01b290dfca2e5ac0a6b55b0b814b7027eb5ab5211fab6ed88e7fc5cf9'),
('chunk-4123','GHBC-CHUNK-004123','GHBC-C-004123','22.10.1
General
Glass unit masonry construction shall comply with Part 13 of TMS 402 and this clause.',22,'22.10','22.10.1','General',828,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015698"]','70b08947496979d51f034e3b119939c4dc930ae7c5b74bd65c39f12d7351bf04'),
('chunk-4124','GHBC-CHUNK-004124','GHBC-C-004124','22.10.1.1
Limitations
Solid or hollow approved glass block shall not be used in fire walls, party walls, fire barriers, fire partitions or smoke barriers, or for load-bearing construction. Such blocks shall be erected with mortar and reinforcement in metal channel-type frames, structural frames, masonry or concrete recesses, embedded panel anchors as provided for both exterior and interior walls or other approved joint materials. Wood strip framing shall not be used in walls required to have a fireresistance rating by other provisions of this Code.
Exceptions:
1. Glass-block assemblies having a fire protection rating of not less than3 / hour shall be permitted4 as opening protectives in accordance with Clause 716 in fire barriers, fire partitions and smoke barriers that have a required fireresistance rating of 1 hour or less and do not enclose exit stairways and ramps or exit passageways.
3. Glass-block assemblies as permitted in Clause 4.4.6, Exception 2. 4.',22,'22.10','22.10.1.1','Limitations',828,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015699","GHBC-REQ-015700","GHBC-REQ-015701","GHBC-REQ-015702","GHBC-REQ-015703","GHBC-REQ-015704","GHBC-REQ-015705","GHBC-REQ-015706","GHBC-REQ-015707"]','55e3aefd7ac1b09420801140401bb733eb8ce102ade9e11c5d657d6b8ec89d2a'),
('chunk-4125','GHBC-CHUNK-004125','GHBC-C-004125','22.11.1
General
The construction of masonry fireplaces, consisting of concrete or masonry, shall be in accordance with this clause.',22,'22.11','22.11.1','General',828,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015708"]','c876f2cf60e991568356eecf5e4fab0a333422f694b3dcfcdc355235a1e0acb0'),
('chunk-4126','GHBC-CHUNK-004126','GHBC-C-004126','22.11.2
Fireplace drawings
The construction documents shall describe in sufficient detail the location, size and construction of masonry fireplaces. The thickness and characteristics of materials and the clearances from walls, partitions and ceilings shall be indicated.',22,'22.11','22.11.2','Fireplace drawings',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015709","GHBC-REQ-015710"]','657f7917df02ef56ed8a043727f79d02dbe73966c1df604cd517b1fef9bff5d1'),
('chunk-4127','GHBC-CHUNK-004127','GHBC-C-004127','22.11.3
Footings and foundations
Footings for masonry fireplaces and their chimneys shall be constructed of concrete or solid masonry not less than 305 mm (12 inches) thick and shall extend not less than 153 mm (6 inches) beyond the face of the fireplace or foundation wall on all sides. Footings shall be founded on natural undisturbed earth or engineered fill below frost depth. In areas not subjected to freezing, footings shall be not less than 305 mm (12 inches) below finished grade.',22,'22.11','22.11.3','Footings and foundations',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015711","GHBC-REQ-015712","GHBC-REQ-015713"]','8a2d2a68b4dce0ec4cf8d7bbc9ddb4bb3242e4591ec9e6d72f64bb8631552483'),
('chunk-4128','GHBC-CHUNK-004128','GHBC-C-004128','22.11.3.1
Ash dump cleanout
Cleanout openings, located within foundation walls below fireboxes, where provided, shall be equipped with ferrous metal or masonry doors and frames constructed to remain tightly closed, except when in use. Clean outs shall be accessible and located so that ash removal will not create a hazard to combustible materials.',22,'22.11','22.11.3.1','Ash dump cleanout',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015714","GHBC-REQ-015715"]','f5eaf0aaf57024400b91d38149b415906a2e0684eb3128c2a0e09e8665924192'),
('chunk-4129','GHBC-CHUNK-004129','GHBC-C-004129','22.11.4
Seismic reinforcement
In structures assigned to Seismic Design zone 0 or 1, seismic reinforcement is not required. In structures assigned to Seismic Design zone 2 and 3, masonry fireplaces shall be reinforced and anchored in accordance with Clauses 22.11.4.1, 22.11.4.2 and 22.11.5. In structures assigned to Seismic Design zone 3, masonry fireplaces shall be reinforced in accordance with the requirements of Clauses 22.1 through 22.8.',22,'22.11','22.11.4','Seismic reinforcement',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015716","GHBC-REQ-015717","GHBC-REQ-015718"]','9c9bec66f05598dcceccf5cbc17bbdfe902176800b9304b94ff92e67ac1334b8'),
('chunk-4130','GHBC-CHUNK-004130','GHBC-C-004130','22.11.4.1
Vertical reinforcing
For fireplaces with chimneys up to 1016 mm (40 inches) wide, four No. 4 continuous vertical bars, anchored in the foundation, shall be placed in the concrete between wythes of solid masonry
or within the cells of hollow unit masonry and grouted in accordance with Clause 22.3.3. For fireplaces with chimneys greater than 1016 mm (40 inches) wide, two additional No. 4 vertical bars shall be provided for each additional 1016 mm (40 inches) in width or fraction thereof.',22,'22.11','22.11.4.1','Vertical reinforcing',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015719","GHBC-REQ-015720","GHBC-REQ-015721"]','0783bf545eb774d016855da0e7a8044143ec140997adcc15ff085a11c6bc9d3f');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4131','GHBC-CHUNK-004131','GHBC-C-004131','22.11.4.2
Horizontal reinforcing
Vertical reinforcement shall be placed enclosed within 6.4 mm (1 / -inch) ties or other reinforcing of equivalent net cross-clauseal area, spaced4 not to exceed 457 mm (18 inches) on center in concrete; or placed in the bed joints of unit masonry at not less than every 457 mm (18 inches) of vertical height. Two such ties shall be provided at each bend in the vertical bars.',22,'22.11','22.11.4.2','Horizontal reinforcing',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015722","GHBC-REQ-015723"]','933e180b4af8457b5aa37547744a366fce3e4fb3e756efa77808867c189e0385'),
('chunk-4132','GHBC-CHUNK-004132','GHBC-C-004132','22.11.5
Seismic anchorage
Masonry fireplaces and foundations shall be anchored at each floor, ceiling or roof line more than 1829 mm (6 feet) above grade with two 4.8 mm by 25 mm (3 / -inch by 1-inch) straps embedded not less than 305 mm (12 inches)16 into the chimney. Straps shall be hooked around the outer bars and extend 152 mm (6 inches) beyond the bend. Each strap shall be fastened to not fewer than four floor joists with two 12.7 mm (1 / -inch) bolts. 2
2. Where the masonry fireplace is constructed completely within the exterior walls.
Exception: Seismic anchorage is not required for the following: 1. In structures assigned to Seismic Design Category A or B.',22,'22.11','22.11.5','Seismic anchorage',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015724","GHBC-REQ-015725","GHBC-REQ-015726","GHBC-REQ-015727","GHBC-REQ-015728","GHBC-REQ-015729","GHBC-REQ-015730"]','331153f02250708f037608bf738d8b8ec7ddfa17d14a5a2339511596614d050f'),
('chunk-4133','GHBC-CHUNK-004133','GHBC-C-004133','22.11.6
Firebox walls
Masonry fireboxes shall be constructed of solid masonry units, hollow masonry units grouted solid, stone or concrete. Where a lining of firebrick not less than 51 mm (2 inches) in
thickness or other approved lining is provided, the minimum thickness of back and sidewalls shall each be 203 mm (8 inches) of solid masonry, including the lining. The width of joints between firebricks shall be not greater than 6.4 mm (1 / inch). Where a lining is not provided, the total minimum thickness of back and4 sidewalls shall be 10 inches (254 mm) of solid masonry. Firebrick shall conform to ASTM C27 or ASTM C1261 and shall be laid with mediumduty refractory mortar conforming to ASTM C199.',22,'22.11','22.11.6','Firebox walls',829,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015731","GHBC-REQ-015732","GHBC-REQ-015733","GHBC-REQ-015734","GHBC-REQ-015735","GHBC-REQ-015736"]','0bd195ce0f152e6664d2a279cc413b09dc54a6f8e018eb7c8eea2a201d67f37e'),
('chunk-4134','GHBC-CHUNK-004134','GHBC-C-004134','22.11.6.1
Steel fireplace units
Steel fireplace units are permitted to be installed with solid masonry to form a masonry fireplace provided that they are installed according to either the requirements of their listing or the requirements of this clause. Steel fireplace units incorporating a steel firebox lining shall be constructed with steel not less than 6.4 mm (1 /
inch)4 in thickness, and an air-circulating chamber that is ducted to the interior of the building. The firebox lining shall be encased with solid masonry to provide a total thickness at the back and sides of not less than 203 mm (8 inches), of which not less than 102 mm (4 inches) shall be of solid masonry or concrete. Circulating air ducts employed with steel fireplace units shall be constructed of metal or masonry.',22,'22.11','22.11.6.1','Steel fireplace units',830,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015737","GHBC-REQ-015738","GHBC-REQ-015739","GHBC-REQ-015740","GHBC-REQ-015741"]','ca752f93124d2a7e5ef62d771b2271d395bc8dd584124c8c58a9be1e0ecc34ba'),
('chunk-4135','GHBC-CHUNK-004135','GHBC-C-004135','22.11.7
Firebox dimensions
The firebox of a concrete or masonry fireplace shall have a minimum depth of 508 mm (20 inches). The throat shall be not less than 203 mm (8 inches) above the fireplace opening. The throat opening shall be not less than 102 mm (4 inches) in depth. The cross-clauseal area of the passageway above the firebox, including the throat, damper and smoke chamber, shall be not less than the cross-clauseal area of the flue.
opening, and the throat is not less than 305 mm (12 inches) above the lintel, and not less than /1 the cross-clauseal area of the fireplace opening.20
Exception: Rumford fireplaces shall be permitted provided that the depth of the fireplace is not less than 305 mm (12 inches) and not less than one-third of the width of the fireplace',22,'22.11','22.11.7','Firebox dimensions',830,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015742","GHBC-REQ-015743","GHBC-REQ-015744","GHBC-REQ-015745","GHBC-REQ-015746","GHBC-REQ-015747"]','8fdb81d99662fec7a3bb30f18c0c5f21a5c2a30a275ea6f5c835059735919834'),
('chunk-4136','GHBC-CHUNK-004136','GHBC-C-004136','22.11.8
Lintel and throat
Masonry over a fireplace opening shall be supported by a lintel of noncombustible material. The minimum required bearing length on each end of the fireplace opening shall be 102 mm (4 inches). The fireplace throat or damper shall be located not less than 203 mm (8 inches) above the top of the fireplace opening.',22,'22.11','22.11.8','Lintel and throat',830,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015748","GHBC-REQ-015749","GHBC-REQ-015750"]','b19705ed484fcd8237c6db5552a2f12be93ba80b6fb30018042130fb73755722'),
('chunk-4137','GHBC-CHUNK-004137','GHBC-C-004137','22.11.8.1
Damper
Masonry fireplaces shall be equipped with a ferrous metal damper located not less than 203 mm (8 inches) above the top of the fireplace opening. Dampers shall be installed in the fireplace or at the top of the flue venting the fireplace, and shall be operable from the room containing the fireplace. Damper controls shall be permitted to be located in the fireplace.',22,'22.11','22.11.8.1','Damper',830,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015751","GHBC-REQ-015752","GHBC-REQ-015753"]','99c3a0be2445caaa277a455edf7f4e0f2cdd7d0e7633de6aa17b6f2b042e81a2'),
('chunk-4138','GHBC-CHUNK-004138','GHBC-C-004138','22.11.9
Smoke chamber walls
Smoke chamber walls shall be constructed of solid masonry units, hollow masonry units grouted solid, stone or concrete. The total minimum thickness of front, back and sidewalls shall be 203 mm (8 inches) of solid masonry. The inside surface shall be parged smooth with refractory mortar conforming to ASTM C199. Where a lining of firebrick not less than 2 inches (51 mm) thick, or a lining of vitrified clay not less than 15.9 mm (5 / inch) thick, is provided, the total minimum thickness of front, back and8 sidewalls shall be 152 mm (6 inches) of solid masonry, including the lining. Firebrick shall conform to ASTM C1261 and shall be laid with refractory mortar conforming to ASTM C199. Vitrified clay linings shall conform to ASTM C315.',22,'22.11','22.11.9','Smoke chamber walls',830,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015754","GHBC-REQ-015755","GHBC-REQ-015756","GHBC-REQ-015757","GHBC-REQ-015758","GHBC-REQ-015759"]','8815672468be4649dc02e3e35a4c1608abc0fa7726b5140b2e156f8dbac6a56f'),
('chunk-4139','GHBC-CHUNK-004139','GHBC-C-004139','22.11.9.1
Smoke chamber dimensions
The inside height of the smoke chamber from the fireplace throat to the beginning of the flue
shall be not greater than the inside width of the fireplace opening. The inside surface of the smoke chamber shall not be inclined more than 45 degrees (0.76 rad) from vertical where prefabricated smoke chamber linings are used or where the smoke chamber walls are rolled or sloped rather than corbeled. Where the inside surface of the smoke chamber is formed by corbeled masonry, the walls shall not be corbeled more than 30 degrees (0.52 rad) from vertical.',22,'22.11','22.11.9.1','Smoke chamber dimensions',830,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015760","GHBC-REQ-015761","GHBC-REQ-015762","GHBC-REQ-015763"]','28d54be9bb6c03b921062fb52014e81df6ee33e7e86e0739252a23e883dc0723'),
('chunk-4140','GHBC-CHUNK-004140','GHBC-C-004140','22.11.10
Hearth and hearth extension
Masonry fireplace hearths and hearth extensions shall be constructed of concrete or masonry, supported by noncombustible materials, and reinforced to carry their own weight and all imposed loads. Combustible material shall not remain against the underside of hearths or hearth extensions after construction.',22,'22.11','22.11.10','Hearth and hearth extension',831,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015764","GHBC-REQ-015765"]','9b162af3e2b12db88bd9cd934a7ff9a69a9b7733712685a5851dd1b3239538ba');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4141','GHBC-CHUNK-004141','GHBC-C-004141','22.11.10.1
Hearth thickness
The minimum thickness of fireplace hearths shall be 102 mm (4 inches).',22,'22.11','22.11.10.1','Hearth thickness',831,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015766"]','51775962c4b43a2227ea2126da98cde64b68de4beb5b307d1d771b5f915daec9'),
('chunk-4142','GHBC-CHUNK-004142','GHBC-C-004142','22.11.10.2
Hearth extension thickness
The minimum thickness of hearth extensions shall be 51 mm (2 inches).
Exception: Where the bottom of the firebox opening is raised not less than 203 mm (8 inches) above the top of the hearth extension, a hearth extension of not less than3 / -inch-thick (9.5 mm) brick, concrete, stone, tile or other8 approved noncombustible material is permitted.',22,'22.11','22.11.10.2','Hearth extension thickness',831,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015767","GHBC-REQ-015768"]','299b52e0f14e22751eb657f70be5e1ecc23514b6b326da2efc49d06cdc301726'),
('chunk-4143','GHBC-CHUNK-004143','GHBC-C-004143','22.11.11
Hearth extension dimensions
Hearth extensions shall extend not less than 406 mm (16 inches) in front of, and not less than 203 mm (8 inches) beyond, each side of the fireplace opening. Where the fireplace opening is 0.557 m2 (6 square feet) or larger, the hearth extension shall extend not less than 508 mm (20 inches) in front of, and not less than 305 mm (12 inches) beyond, each side of the fireplace opening.',22,'22.11','22.11.11','Hearth extension dimensions',831,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015769","GHBC-REQ-015770"]','4839d6983ed88615ad4103cd650b957f6e0b8a69fb4a5407d738bf2093efa603'),
('chunk-4144','GHBC-CHUNK-004144','GHBC-C-004144','22.11.12
Fireplace clearance
Any portion of a masonry fireplace located in the interior of a building or within the exterior wall of a building shall have a clearance to combustibles of not less than 51 mm (2 inches) from the front faces and sides of masonry fireplaces and not less than 102 mm (4 inches) from the back faces of masonry fireplaces. The airspace shall not be filled, except to provide fireblocking in accordance with Clause 22.11.13.
Exceptions: 1. Masonry fireplaces listed and labeled for use in contact with combustibles in accordance with this Code and installed in accordance with the manufacturer‘s instructions are permitted to have combustible material in contact with their exterior surfaces.
2. Where masonry fireplaces are constructed as part of masonry or concrete walls, combustible materials shall not be in contact with the masonry or concrete walls less than 306 mm (12 inches) from the inside surface of the nearest firebox lining.
3. Exposed combustible trim and the edges of sheathing materials, such as wood siding, flooring and drywall, are permitted to abut the masonry fireplace sidewalls and hearth extension, in accordance with
combustible trim or sheathing is not less than 306 mm (12 inches) from the inside surface of the nearest firebox lining.
4. Exposed combustible mantels or trim is permitted to be placed directly on the masonry fireplace front surrounding the fireplace opening, provided that such combustible materials shall not be placed within 153 mm (6 inches) of a fireplace opening. Combustible
material directly above and within 305 mm (12 inches) of the fireplace opening shall not project more than 3.2 mm (1 / inch) for each 25 mm (1-inch) distance from such opening.8 Combustible materials located along the sides of the fireplace opening that project more than 38 mm (11 /
inches) from the face of the fireplace2 shall have an additional clearance equal to the projection.
For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm
EXCEPTION TO FIREPLACE CLEARANCE PROVISION',22,'22.11','22.11.12','Fireplace clearance',831,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015771","GHBC-REQ-015772","GHBC-REQ-015773","GHBC-REQ-015774","GHBC-REQ-015775","GHBC-REQ-015776","GHBC-REQ-015777","GHBC-REQ-015778","GHBC-REQ-015779","GHBC-REQ-015780","GHBC-REQ-015781","GHBC-REQ-015782","GHBC-REQ-015783","GHBC-REQ-015784","GHBC-REQ-015785","GHBC-REQ-015786"]','bd5ca428c50f70af116795a557b817afc11820270109de095ca4b4a4a7892357'),
('chunk-4145','GHBC-CHUNK-004145','GHBC-C-004145','22.11.13
Fireplace fireblocking
All spaces between fireplaces and floors and ceilings through which fireplaces pass shall be fireblocked with noncombustible material securely fastened in place. The fireblocking of spaces between wood joists, beams or headers shall be to a depth of 25 mm (1 inch) and shall only be placed on strips of metal or metal lath laid across the spaces between combustible material and the chimney.',22,'22.11','22.11.13','Fireplace fireblocking',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015787","GHBC-REQ-015788"]','714a25c6c561eedcf29724a59012fda35c43a4caa176634ca3d65f1395f7e3d5'),
('chunk-4146','GHBC-CHUNK-004146','GHBC-C-004146','22.11.14
Exterior air
Factory-built or masonry fireplaces covered in this clause shall be equipped with an exterior air supply to ensure proper fuel combustion unless the room is mechanically ventilated and
controlled so that the indoor pressure is neutral or positive.',22,'22.11','22.11.14','Exterior air',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015789","GHBC-REQ-015790"]','0d0353074903a592bbe1a276287a9980a90aeb33959d6362f5ad1815afee39fb'),
('chunk-4147','GHBC-CHUNK-004147','GHBC-C-004147','22.11.14.1
Factory-built fireplaces
Exterior combustion air ducts for factory-built fireplaces shall be listed components of the fireplace, and installed according to the fireplace manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.11','22.11.14.1','Factory-built fireplaces',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015791"]','e3555c3ff6c786df5fbf439ca459b8aed562c94199845d8cbe106ecccb065555'),
('chunk-4148','GHBC-CHUNK-004148','GHBC-C-004148','22.11.14.2
Masonry fireplaces
Listed combustion air ducts for masonry fireplaces shall be installed according to the terms of their listing and manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.11','22.11.14.2','Masonry fireplaces',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015792"]','403052482f18bd2434ee0b96076c41e3295b133243bf0f2c2939a1b965faac5d'),
('chunk-4149','GHBC-CHUNK-004149','GHBC-C-004149','22.11.14.3
Exterior air intake
The exterior air intake shall be capable of providing all combustion air from the exterior of the dwelling. The exterior air intake shall not be located within a garage, attic, basement or crawl space of the dwelling nor shall the air intake be located at an elevation higher than the firebox.
The exterior air intake shall be covered with a corrosion-resistant screen of 6.4 mm (1 / -inch) mesh.4',22,'22.11','22.11.14.3','Exterior air intake',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015793","GHBC-REQ-015794","GHBC-REQ-015795"]','c0c7d3c02db9e057637f92fe319e6e9326e83b648668aa7ad3994608678ce6aa'),
('chunk-4150','GHBC-CHUNK-004150','GHBC-C-004150','21.11.14.4
Clearance
Unlisted combustion air ducts shall be installed with a minimum 25 mm (1-inch) clearance to combustibles for all parts of the duct within 1524 mm (5 feet) of the duct outlet.',22,'22.11','21.11.14.4','Clearance',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015796"]','864dd4fdd6edad0b496124d8ec143213cf3e7e43d7dacfc5385ac2382fad77ee');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4151','GHBC-CHUNK-004151','GHBC-C-004151','22.11.14.5
Passageway
The combustion air passageway shall be not less than 3870 mm2 (6 square inches) and not more than 0.035 m2 (55 square inches), except that combustion air systems for listed fireplaces or for fireplaces tested for emissions shall be constructed according to the fireplace manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.11','22.11.14.5','Passageway',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015797"]','f98fd58b476ef63beab74bbb3eea03aa26d9bd5d5fc0716265bf6c99a4e0a331'),
('chunk-4152','GHBC-CHUNK-004152','GHBC-C-004152','22.11.14.6
Outlet
The exterior air outlet is permitted to be located in the back or sides of the firebox chamber or within 610 mm (24 inches) of the firebox opening on or near the floor. The outlet shall be closable
and designed to prevent burning material from dropping into concealed combustible spaces.',22,'22.11','22.11.14.6','Outlet',832,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015798","GHBC-REQ-015799","GHBC-REQ-015800"]','de8fec967047959b0913d173cea0ed4be10b77537e87abe2311de69866387480'),
('chunk-4153','GHBC-CHUNK-004153','GHBC-C-004153','22.12.1
Definition
A masonry heater is a heating appliance constructed of concrete or solid masonry, hereinafter referred to as ―masonry,‖ which is designed to absorb and store heat from a solid fuel fire built in the firebox by routing the exhaust gases through internal heat exchange channels in which the flow path downstream of the firebox includes flow in either a horizontal or downward direction before entering the chimney and which delivers heat by radiation from the masonry surface of the heater.',22,'22.12','22.12.1','Definition',833,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015801"]','e1bf031f187ac15c7efe74e99e7da0c52b6d62f06bd0ba48ae4b113306b466bf'),
('chunk-4154','GHBC-CHUNK-004154','GHBC-C-004154','22.12.2
Installation
Masonry heaters shall be installed in accordance with this clause and comply with one of the following:
1. Masonry heaters shall comply with the requirements of ASTM E1602.
2. Masonry heaters shall be listed and labeled in accordance with EN 15250 and installed in accordance with the manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.12','22.12.2','Installation',833,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015802","GHBC-REQ-015803","GHBC-REQ-015804","GHBC-REQ-015805","GHBC-REQ-015806"]','99c746ca1fe12ec20ab244146a568bd6aab9b7be78e8d0234e36983cef1fa785'),
('chunk-4155','GHBC-CHUNK-004155','GHBC-C-004155','22.12.3
Footings and foundation
The firebox floor of a masonry heater shall be a minimum thickness of 102 mm (4 inches) of noncombustible material and be supported on a noncombustible footing and foundation in accordance with Clause 22.13.2.',22,'22.12','22.12.3','Footings and foundation',833,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015807"]','d853d934d9d7378b6f2117e5b12ba8f4303164c7ddc62c6d339bcf609305e584'),
('chunk-4156','GHBC-CHUNK-004156','GHBC-C-004156','22.12.4
Seismic reinforcing
In structures assigned to Seismic Design Category D, E or F, masonry heaters shall be anchored to the masonry foundation in accordance with Clause 22.13.3. Seismic reinforcing shall not be required within the body of a masonry heater with a height that is equal to or less than 3.5 times its body width and where the masonry chimney serving the heater is not supported by the body of the heater. Where the
masonry chimney shares a common wall with the facing of the masonry heater, the chimney portion of the structure shall be reinforced in accordance with Clause 22.13.',22,'22.12','22.12.4','Seismic reinforcing',833,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015808","GHBC-REQ-015809","GHBC-REQ-015810","GHBC-REQ-015811"]','f5a0da6a6d10cac42d864c099f2e52ff6bd069944d2df6446de0b11a2f85c6e7'),
('chunk-4157','GHBC-CHUNK-004157','GHBC-C-004157','22.12.5
Masonry heater clearance
Combustible materials shall not be placed within 914 mm (36 inches) or the distance of the allowed reduction method from the outside surface of a masonry heater in accordance with the Ghana fire Code, Clause 12.6, and the required space between the heater and combustible material shall be fully vented to permit the free flow of air around all heater surfaces.
Exceptions: 1. Where the masonry heater wall thickness is not less than 203 mm (8 inches) of solid masonry and the wall thickness of the heat exchange channels is not less than 127 mm (5 inches) of solid masonry, combustible materials shall not be placed within 102 mm (4 inches) of the outside surface of a masonry heater. A clearance of not less than 203 mm (8 inches) shall be provided between the gas-tight capping slab of the heater and a combustible ceiling.
2. Masonry heaters listed and labeled in accordance with EN 15250 and installed in accordance with the manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.12','22.12.5','Masonry heater clearance',833,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-015812","GHBC-REQ-015813","GHBC-REQ-015814","GHBC-REQ-015815","GHBC-REQ-015816","GHBC-REQ-015817"]','1a7702860edbbccf194a6e71370954a65801acaf913ad83fdac077c1daec90b3'),
('chunk-4158','GHBC-CHUNK-004158','GHBC-C-004158','22.13.1
General
The construction of masonry chimneys consisting of solid masonry units, hollow masonry units grouted solid, stone or concrete shall be in accordance with this clause.',22,'22.13','22.13.1','General',833,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015818"]','b2b073c38bd5ad049294d9c485395c2d97c5bd622dd3cc0f3cf739d6ab160be5'),
('chunk-4159','GHBC-CHUNK-004159','GHBC-C-004159','22.13.2
Footings and foundations
Footings for masonry chimneys shall be constructed of concrete or solid masonry not
less than 305 mm (12 inches) thick and shall extend not less than 152 mm (6 inches) beyond the face of the foundation or support wall on all sides. Footings shall be founded on natural undisturbed earth or engineered fill below frost depth. In areas not subjected to freezing, footings shall be not less than 305 mm (12 inches) below finished grade.',22,'22.13','22.13.2','Footings and foundations',833,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015819","GHBC-REQ-015820","GHBC-REQ-015821","GHBC-REQ-015822"]','9df8e6aaf7e70726864ea4c4ce782c03d3300786b6c8b0e0ba3463b2a5e3a0fd'),
('chunk-4160','GHBC-CHUNK-004160','GHBC-C-004160','22.13.3
Seismic reinforcement
In structures assigned to Seismic Design Category A or B, seismic reinforcement is not required. In structures assigned to Seismic Design Category C or D, masonry chimneys shall be reinforced and anchored in accordance with Clauses 22.13.3.1, 22.13.3.2 and 22.13.4. In structures assigned to Seismic Design Category E or F, masonry chimneys shall be reinforced in accordance with the requirements of Clauses 22.1 through 22.8 and anchored in accordance with Clause 22.13.4.',22,'22.13','22.13.3','Seismic reinforcement',834,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015823","GHBC-REQ-015824","GHBC-REQ-015825"]','bce3e0638eb2639e292f77124e1902e081ff74d7a8676da0af0d23bbe0edbaf0');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4161','GHBC-CHUNK-004161','GHBC-C-004161','22.13.3.1
Vertical reinforcement
For chimneys up to 1016 mm (40 inches) wide, four No. 4 continuous vertical bars anchored in the foundation shall be placed in the concrete between wythes of solid masonry or within the cells of hollow unit masonry and grouted in accordance with Clause 22.3.3. Grout shall be prevented from bonding with the flue liner so that the flue liner is free to move with thermal expansion. For chimneys greater than 1016 mm (40 inches) wide, two additional No. 4 vertical bars shall be provided for each additional 1016 mm (40 inches) in width or fraction thereof.',22,'22.13','22.13.3.1','Vertical reinforcement',834,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015826","GHBC-REQ-015827","GHBC-REQ-015828"]','3331f72576412abb1ca7242d00adacf2794fdecb2b72790fe86e2a83fa704b31'),
('chunk-4162','GHBC-CHUNK-004162','GHBC-C-004162','22.13.3.2
Horizontal reinforcement
Vertical reinforcement shall be placed enclosed within 6.4 mm (1 / -inch) ties, or other reinforcing of equivalent net cross-clauseal area, spaced4 not to exceed 457 mm (18 inches) on center in concrete, or placed in the bed joints of unit masonry, at not less than every 457 mm (18 inches) of vertical height. Two such ties shall be provided at each bend in the vertical bars.',22,'22.13','22.13.3.2','Horizontal reinforcement',834,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015829","GHBC-REQ-015830"]','ed71dae3f0c947ec223beacd89bce189361ef7609fe9b48cc6498a724d4a1926'),
('chunk-4163','GHBC-CHUNK-004163','GHBC-C-004163','22.13.4
Seismic anchorage
Masonry chimneys and foundations shall be anchored at each floor, ceiling or roof line more than 6 feet (1829 mm) above grade with two 4.8 mm by 25 mm (3 / -inch by 1-inch) straps embedded not less than 305 mm (12 inches)16 into the chimney. Straps shall be hooked around the outer bars and extend 152 mm (6 inches) beyond the bend. Each strap shall be fastened to not less than four floor joists with two 12.7 mm (1 / -inch) bolts. 2
2. Where the masonry fireplace is constructed completely within the exterior walls.
Exception: Seismic anchorage is not required for the following: 1. In structures assigned to Seismic Design Category A or B.',22,'22.13','22.13.4','Seismic anchorage',834,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015831","GHBC-REQ-015832","GHBC-REQ-015833","GHBC-REQ-015834","GHBC-REQ-015835","GHBC-REQ-015836","GHBC-REQ-015837"]','4c1119bb327769bf7dcb092e60ef6154efc7079cbe2064a65a38a36ecfff0c57'),
('chunk-4164','GHBC-CHUNK-004164','GHBC-C-004164','22.13.5
Corbeling
Masonry chimneys shall not be corbeled more than half of the chimney‘s wall thickness from a wall or foundation, nor shall a chimney be corbeled from a wall or foundation that is less than 305 mm (12 inches) in thickness unless it projects equally on each side of the wall, except that on the second storey of a two-storey dwelling, corbeling of chimneys on the exterior of the enclosing walls is permitted to equal the wall thickness. The projection of a single course shall not exceed one-half the unit height or onethird of the unit bed depth, whichever is less.',22,'22.13','22.13.5','Corbeling',834,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015838","GHBC-REQ-015839"]','3e15cf4a1f0e885af1493f7701659d3cfaf71c99411e6dee0f5ac5355da47ee2'),
('chunk-4165','GHBC-CHUNK-004165','GHBC-C-004165','22.13.6
Changes in dimension
The chimney wall or chimney flue lining shall not change in size or shape within 152 mm (6 inches) above or below where the chimney passes through floor components, ceiling components or roof components.',22,'22.13','22.13.6','Changes in dimension',834,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015840"]','02df505bb739bfe1036fb06af15f96983212d5af8f8429c811a118adb928b90a'),
('chunk-4166','GHBC-CHUNK-004166','GHBC-C-004166','22.13.7
Offsets
Where a masonry chimney is constructed with a fireclay flue liner surrounded by one wythe of masonry, the maximum offset shall be such that the centerline of the flue above the offset does not extend beyond the center of the chimney wall below the offset. Where the chimney offset is supported by masonry below the offset in an approved manner, the maximum offset limitations shall not apply. Each individual corbeled masonry course of the offset shall not exceed the projection limitations specified in Clause 22.13.5.',22,'22.13','22.13.7','Offsets',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015841","GHBC-REQ-015842","GHBC-REQ-015843"]','d7e1d66f0fba40f14e79a37dbbeb10745ddf635ffd7834a6cb56dce17a624699'),
('chunk-4167','GHBC-CHUNK-004167','GHBC-C-004167','22.13.8
Additional load
Chimneys shall not support loads other than their own weight unless they are designed and constructed to support the additional load. Masonry chimneys are permitted to be constructed as part of the masonry walls or concrete walls of the building.',22,'22.13','22.13.8','Additional load',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015844","GHBC-REQ-015845"]','b512945dd89a58e11ec74f1c53b30ebb647c2ac5124196eed1908b7e30bc5f0b'),
('chunk-4168','GHBC-CHUNK-004168','GHBC-C-004168','22.13.9
Termination
Chimneys shall extend not less than 610 mm (2 feet) higher than any portion of the building within 3048 mm (10 feet), but shall be not less than 914 mm (3 feet) above the highest point where the chimney passes through the roof.',22,'22.13','22.13.9','Termination',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015846"]','8a77e6941b352edc8e512127dac0f474647e0bbbcccd2bc1475aea9f7337fd13'),
('chunk-4169','GHBC-CHUNK-004169','GHBC-C-004169','22.13.9.1
Chimney caps
Masonry chimneys shall have a concrete, metal or stone cap, sloped to shed water, a drip edge and a caulked bond break around any flue liners in accordance with ASTM C1283.',22,'22.13','22.13.9.1','Chimney caps',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015847"]','08c3734fefa85f78f1563fdd7b9bd4812717fccc120db2e58373bc6ff15d09b1'),
('chunk-4170','GHBC-CHUNK-004170','GHBC-C-004170','22.13.9.2
Spark arrestors
Where a spark arrestor is installed on a masonry chimney, the spark arrestor shall meet all of the following requirements:
1. The net free area of the arrestor shall be not less than four times the net free area of the outlet of the chimney flue it serves.
2. The arrestor screen shall have heat and corrosion resistance equivalent
to 19-gage galvanized steel or 24gage stainless steel.
3. Openings shall not permit the passage of spheres having a diameter greater than 12.7 mm (1 /
inch) nor block the passage of2 spheres having a diameter less than 9.5 mm (3 / inch). 8
4. The spark arrestor shall be accessible for cleaning and the screen or chimney cap shall be removable to allow for cleaning of the chimney flue.',22,'22.13','22.13.9.2','Spark arrestors',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015848","GHBC-REQ-015849","GHBC-REQ-015850","GHBC-REQ-015851","GHBC-REQ-015852","GHBC-REQ-015853","GHBC-REQ-015854","GHBC-REQ-015855","GHBC-REQ-015856","GHBC-REQ-015857","GHBC-REQ-015858","GHBC-REQ-015859"]','dd4f9dc6f2a56a466d204100e8f64b98398a8aa3f07952c07f2a9516bda778d7');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4171','GHBC-CHUNK-004171','GHBC-C-004171','22.13.9.3
Rain caps
Where a masonry or metal rain cap is installed on a masonry chimney, the net free area under the cap shall be not less than four times the net free area of the outlet of the chimney flue it serves.',22,'22.13','22.13.9.3','Rain caps',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015860"]','1a288b466be2d9509ee46df085c6655a2742ec5afe831219b9fabdbc1faae62f'),
('chunk-4172','GHBC-CHUNK-004172','GHBC-C-004172','22.13.10
Wall thickness
Masonry chimney walls shall be constructed of concrete, solid masonry units or hollow masonry units grouted solid with not less than 102 mm (4 inches) nominal thickness.',22,'22.13','22.13.10','Wall thickness',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015861"]','f9169bee9bfecdc2cc059c12da12e1bd7b1f0b887a53f419420a5a7e7773d797'),
('chunk-4173','GHBC-CHUNK-004173','GHBC-C-004173','22.13.10.1
Masonry veneer chimneys
Where masonry is used as veneer for a framed chimney, through flashing and weep holes shall be provided as required by Part 15.',22,'22.13','22.13.10.1','Masonry veneer chimneys',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015862"]','bcc1abe2807d5cddfa6a46e902cc5d754c45a1cdb017891b916078c5f3046610'),
('chunk-4174','GHBC-CHUNK-004174','GHBC-C-004174','22.13.11
Flue lining (material)
Masonry chimneys shall be lined. The lining material shall be appropriate for the type of appliance connected, according to the terms of the appliance listing and the manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.13','22.13.11','Flue lining (material)',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015863","GHBC-REQ-015864"]','9df14fe92772d63df46cad0fae31312f4582fcc495cb8092169604085fd26f2d'),
('chunk-4175','GHBC-CHUNK-004175','GHBC-C-004175','22.13.11.1
Residential-type appliances
(general).
Flue lining systems shall comply with one of the following:
1. Clay flue lining complying with the requirements of ASTM C315.
2. Listed chimney lining systems complying with this Code
3. Factory-built chimneys or chimney units listed for installation within masonry chimneys.
4. Other approved materials that will resist corrosion, erosion, softening or cracking from flue gases and condensate at temperatures up to 1,800°F (982°C).
22.13.11.1.1 Flue linings for specific appliances. Flue linings other than those covered in Clause 22.13.11.1 intended for use with specific appliances shall comply with Clauses 22.13.11.1.2 through 22.13.11.1.4, 22.13.11.2 and 22.13.11.3.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.1','Residential-type appliances',835,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015865","GHBC-REQ-015866","GHBC-REQ-015867","GHBC-REQ-015868","GHBC-REQ-015869","GHBC-REQ-015870","GHBC-REQ-015871","GHBC-REQ-015872","GHBC-REQ-015873","GHBC-REQ-015874","GHBC-REQ-015875","GHBC-REQ-015876"]','2ed045343186c5a2d6f762b5b21d2607cb6c9790b7712830051aa63fd80f1637'),
('chunk-4176','GHBC-CHUNK-004176','GHBC-C-004176','22.13.11.1.2
Gas appliances
Flue lining systems for gas appliances shall be in accordance with the International Fuel Gas Code.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.1.2','Gas appliances',836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015877"]','35a0880a613afa4f76641f4f8df604e4aa613d03f72fb99e7afae0e99bc69467'),
('chunk-4177','GHBC-CHUNK-004177','GHBC-C-004177','22.13.11.1.3
Pellet fuel-burning appliances
Flue lining and vent systems for use in masonry chimneys with pellet fuel-burning appliances shall be limited to flue lining systems complying with Clause 22.13.11.1 and pellet vents listed for installation within masonry chimneys (see Clause 22.13.11.1.5 for marking).',22,'22.13','22.13.11.1.3','Pellet fuel-burning appliances',836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015878"]','1ff114c84e6ca2992f2efcfc044f6f6349edc668bb0a79fe990a5fdf3bdd7585'),
('chunk-4178','GHBC-CHUNK-004178','GHBC-C-004178','22.13.11.1.4
Oil-fired appliances approved for use with L-vent. Flue lining and vent systems for use in masonry chimneys with oil-fired appliances approved for use with Type L vent shall be limited to flue lining systems complying with Clause 22.13.11.1 and listed chimney liners complying with  this Code (see Clause 22.13.11.1.5 for marking).',22,'22.13','22.13.11.1.4',NULL,836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015879","GHBC-REQ-015880"]','ab706192fad5a19e02a1dd8259654610496365f548b3f22437e2a0a9b1857fc8'),
('chunk-4179','GHBC-CHUNK-004179','GHBC-C-004179','22.13.11.1.5
Notice of usage
When a flue is relined with a material not complying with Clause 22.13.11.1, the chimney shall be plainly and permanently identified by a label attached to a wall, ceiling or other conspicuous location adjacent to where the connector enters the chimney. The label shall include the following message or equivalent language: ―This chimney is for use only with (type or category of appliance) that burns (type of fuel). Do not connect other types of appliances.‖',22,'22.13','22.13.11.1.5','Notice of usage',836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015881","GHBC-REQ-015882","GHBC-REQ-015883"]','e19ef49910ffc4c0e2a7b1cefb8ce91c1c6895c4855f8fb913f4d545730e74f4'),
('chunk-4180','GHBC-CHUNK-004180','GHBC-C-004180','22.13.11.2
Concrete and masonry chimneys
for medium-heat appliances. Concrete and masonry chimneys for mediumheat appliances shall comply with Clauses 22.13.11.2.1 through 22.13.11.2.5.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.2','Concrete and masonry chimneys',836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015884","GHBC-REQ-015885"]','85a13911417bc9e651ce77c78c15315e221ca16d313d0e67eb392c9528f44eda');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4181','GHBC-CHUNK-004181','GHBC-C-004181','22.13.11.2.1
Construction
Chimneys for medium-heat appliances shall be constructed of solid masonry units or of concrete with walls not less than 203 mm (8 inches) thick, or with stone masonry not less than 305 mm (12 inches) thick.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.2.1','Construction',836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015886"]','520a8c4a894c4b94be914c77a64985752e9927f25ec3d6b52318c8845185e6f9'),
('chunk-4182','GHBC-CHUNK-004182','GHBC-C-004182','22.13.11.2.2
Lining
Concrete and masonry chimneys shall be lined with an approved medium-duty refractory brick not less than 114 mm (41 / inches) thick laid on 2 the 114 mm (41 / -inch bed) in an approved medium-duty refractory mortar. The lining shall2 start 610 mm (2 feet) or more below the lowest chimney connector entrance. Chimneys
terminating 7620 mm (25 feet) or less above a chimney connector entrance shall be lined to the top.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.2.2','Lining',836,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015887","GHBC-REQ-015888","GHBC-REQ-015889","GHBC-REQ-015890"]','ed9c3aba910fcd5faf0626f92102070157b647b9d581198625793b9186abaeaf'),
('chunk-4183','GHBC-CHUNK-004183','GHBC-C-004183','22.13.11.2.3
Multiple passageway
Concrete and masonry chimneys containing more than one passageway shall have the liners separated by a minimum 102 mm (4- inch-thick) concrete or solid masonry wall.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.2.3','Multiple passageway',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015891"]','422e5a9bb62c153921f6d9413d84e0895b9a12d64943cd6485ddad3346f6f069'),
('chunk-4184','GHBC-CHUNK-004184','GHBC-C-004184','22.13.11.2.4
Termination height
Concrete and masonry chimneys for mediumheat appliances shall extend not less than 3048 mm (10 feet) higher than any portion of any building within 7620 mm (25 feet).',22,'22.13','22.13.11.2.4','Termination height',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015892"]','8f142189eedd079742ef8ca98ede64b241e5d14538adffb730a98121af61c551'),
('chunk-4185','GHBC-CHUNK-004185','GHBC-C-004185','22.13.11.2.5
Clearance
A minimum clearance of 102 mm (4 inches) shall be provided between the exterior surfaces of a concrete or masonry chimney for mediumheat appliances and combustible material.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.2.5','Clearance',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015893"]','05b458d9a072c0ca8b6c0629c65be78bcfbbf708e7de71487d90213dcd7e0040'),
('chunk-4186','GHBC-CHUNK-004186','GHBC-C-004186','22.13.11.3
Concrete and masonry chimneys
for high-heat appliances. Concrete and masonry chimneys for high-heat appliances shall comply with 22.13.11.3.1 through 22.13.11.3.4.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.3','Concrete and masonry chimneys',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015894","GHBC-REQ-015895"]','ff6d374cfdba7c9405a7edd218262383e8af05551b7aabd315300847426abe4f'),
('chunk-4187','GHBC-CHUNK-004187','GHBC-C-004187','22.13.11.3.1
Construction
Chimneys for high-heat appliances shall be constructed with double walls of solid masonry units or of concrete, each wall to be not less than 203 mm (8 inches) thick with a minimum airspace of 51 mm (2 inches) between the walls.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.3.1','Construction',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015896"]','9287fa4b6cd0da5c193b6cffff0ee2e2397ab5f5275f44c22132556e26b52973'),
('chunk-4188','GHBC-CHUNK-004188','GHBC-C-004188','22.13.11.3.2
Lining
The inside of the interior wall shall be lined with an approved high-duty refractory brick, not less than 114 mm (41 / inches) thick laid on the 114 2 mm bed (41 / - inch) in an approved high-duty refractory mortar. The lining shall start at the2
base of the chimney and extend continuously to the top.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.3.2','Lining',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015897","GHBC-REQ-015898","GHBC-REQ-015899"]','526b55e922d320da8dbd5c1d4d9fbdb027c8a3ac09e708be4ec69e2b3d37649e'),
('chunk-4189','GHBC-CHUNK-004189','GHBC-C-004189','22.13.11.3.3
Termination height
Concrete and masonry chimneys for high-heat appliances shall extend not less than 6096 mm (20 feet) higher than any portion of any building within 15 240 mm (50 feet).',22,'22.13','22.13.11.3.3','Termination height',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015900"]','6b40653c15e5a8d516c6c0e4f8c4c4d25a08e34a461b483fc59df9b2df589042'),
('chunk-4190','GHBC-CHUNK-004190','GHBC-C-004190','22.13.11.3.4
Clearance
Concrete and masonry chimneys for high-heat appliances shall have approved clearance from buildings and structures to prevent overheating combustible materials, permit inspection and maintenance operations on the chimney and prevent danger of burns to persons.',22,'22.13','22.13.11.3.4','Clearance',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015901"]','9bce2d4f50bb246b3d8125921aad12ca428820e1e331d733ee827498334fcfab');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-4191','GHBC-CHUNK-004191','GHBC-C-004191','22.13.12
Clay flue lining (installation)
Clay flue liners shall be installed in accordance with ASTM C1283 and extend from a point not less than 203 mm (8 inches) below the lowest inlet or, in the case of fireplaces, from the top of the smoke chamber to a point above the enclosing walls. The lining shall be carried up vertically, with a maximum slope not greater than 30 degrees (0.52 rad) from the vertical.
Clay flue liners shall be laid in medium-duty nonwater-soluble refractory mortar conforming to ASTM C199 with tight mortar joints left smooth on the inside and installed to maintain an airspace or insulation not to exceed the thickness of the flue liner separating the flue liners from the interior face of the chimney masonry walls. Flue lining shall be supported on all sides. Only enough mortar shall be placed to make the joint and hold the liners in position.',22,'22.13','22.13.12','Clay flue lining (installation)',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015902","GHBC-REQ-015903","GHBC-REQ-015904","GHBC-REQ-015905","GHBC-REQ-015906"]','3c6e28de6858c2e822e50ffaeb1d8c023b12d9358d3df91a9e041679a5761220'),
('chunk-4192','GHBC-CHUNK-004192','GHBC-C-004192','22.13.13
Additional requirements',22,'22.13','22.13.13','Additional requirements',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','[]','5a0b89760e98bf7b3abdc6b096103761e8b65d166108a9e5a87502dc94ca6e5e'),
('chunk-4193','GHBC-CHUNK-004193','GHBC-C-004193','22.13.13.1
Listed materials
Listed materials used as flue linings shall be installed in accordance with the terms of their listings and the manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.13','22.13.13.1','Listed materials',837,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015907"]','edf1e0a21e796e6a1b7a02e1fac173190a793c44a4e545f9e39ea668b4664d9b'),
('chunk-4194','GHBC-CHUNK-004194','GHBC-C-004194','22.13.13.2
Space around lining
The space surrounding a chimney lining system or vent installed within a masonry chimney shall not be used to vent any other appliance.
Exception: This shall not prevent the installation of a separate flue lining in accordance with the manufacturer‘s instructions.',22,'22.13','22.13.13.2','Space around lining',838,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015908","GHBC-REQ-015909"]','9a027fa45809598434bfe1704ad03234e94443988f1d9b3a519c15c9fe7819cd'),
('chunk-4195','GHBC-CHUNK-004195','GHBC-C-004195','22.13.14
Multiple flues
Where two or more flues are located in the same chimney, masonry wythes shall be built between adjacent flue linings. The masonry wythes shall be not less than 102 mm (4 inches) thick and bonded into the walls of the chimney.
For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 square inch = 645 mm2 .
Exception: Where venting only one appliance, two flues are permitted to adjoin each other in the same chimney with only the flue lining separation between them. The joints of the adjacent flue linings shall be staggered not less than 102 mm (4 inches).',22,'22.13','22.13.14','Multiple flues',838,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015910","GHBC-REQ-015911","GHBC-REQ-015912","GHBC-REQ-015913"]','52fd1a1190253d28fced2ba7f93ec3931ed261a8818d3c161127dc5a3cd05868'),
('chunk-4196','GHBC-CHUNK-004196','GHBC-C-004196','22.13.15
Flue area (appliance)
Chimney flues shall not be smaller in area than the area of the connector from the appliance. Chimney flues connected to more than one appliance shall be not less than the area of the largest connector plus 50 percent of the areas of additional chimney connectors.
Exceptions: 1. Chimney flues serving oil-fired appliances sized in accordance with the Ghana Fire Code
2. Chimney flues serving gas-fired appliances sized in accordance with this Code',22,'22.13','22.13.15','Flue area (appliance)',838,'["TABLE 22.13.16(1)","TABLE 22.13.16(2) NET CROSS-CLAUSEAL"]','["GHBC-REQ-015914","GHBC-REQ-015915","GHBC-REQ-015916","GHBC-REQ-015917","GHBC-REQ-015918","GHBC-REQ-015919"]','0e3a1ddd3e177ec054bdaaeadfe0d1be9b132dd4f796bd110d22e351de044768'),
('chunk-4197','GHBC-CHUNK-004197','GHBC-C-004197','22.13.16
Flue area (masonry fireplace)
Flue sizing for chimneys serving fireplaces shall be in accordance with Clause 22.13.16.1 or 22.13.16.2.
FLUE SIZES FOR MASONRY CHIMNEYS
