('chunk-4315','GHBC-CHUNK-004315','GHBC-C-004315','24.4.9
Timber decking
Timber decking shall be designed and installed in accordance with the general provisions of this Code and Clauses 24.4.9.1 through 24.4.9.5.3.',24,'24.4','24.4.9','Timber decking',861,'["TABLE 24.4.6.1 MAXIMUM ALLOWABLE STRESS DESIGN WIND SPEED, Vasd PERMITTED FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(1) ALLOWABLE SPANS FOR TIMBER FLOOR AND ROOF SHEATHING","TABLE 24.4.8(2) SHEATHING TIMBER, MINIMUM GRADE REQUIREMENTS: BOARD GRADE","TABLE 24.4.8(3) ALLOWABLE SPANS AND LOADS FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL","TABLE 24.4.8(4) ALLOWABLE SPAN FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(5) ALLOWABLE LOAD (PSF) FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL ROOF SHEATHING","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(4)","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(5)","Table 24.4.9.3.2 shall be permitted.","TABLE 24.4.9.3.2 FASTENING SCHEDULE","TABLE 24.4.10.1"]','["GHBC-REQ-016387"]','1c61290f41e993a0e77aef4a4ae48c80d6c0389e28f54fcc33d6b7fd6f61bf93'),
('chunk-4316','GHBC-CHUNK-004316','GHBC-C-004316','24.4.9.1
General
Each piece of timber decking shall be squareend trimmed. Where random lengths are furnished, each piece shall be square end trimmed across the face so that not less than 90 percent of the pieces are within 0.5 degrees (0.00873 rad) of square. The ends of the pieces shall be permitted to be beveled up to 2 degrees (0.0349 rad) from the vertical with the exposed face of the piece slightly longer than the opposite face of the piece. Tongue-and-groove decking shall be installed with the tongues up on sloped or pitched roofs with pattern faces down.',24,'24.4','24.4.9.1','General',861,'["TABLE 24.4.6.1 MAXIMUM ALLOWABLE STRESS DESIGN WIND SPEED, Vasd PERMITTED FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(1) ALLOWABLE SPANS FOR TIMBER FLOOR AND ROOF SHEATHING","TABLE 24.4.8(2) SHEATHING TIMBER, MINIMUM GRADE REQUIREMENTS: BOARD GRADE","TABLE 24.4.8(3) ALLOWABLE SPANS AND LOADS FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL","TABLE 24.4.8(4) ALLOWABLE SPAN FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(5) ALLOWABLE LOAD (PSF) FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL ROOF SHEATHING","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(4)","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(5)","Table 24.4.9.3.2 shall be permitted.","TABLE 24.4.9.3.2 FASTENING SCHEDULE","TABLE 24.4.10.1"]','["GHBC-REQ-016388","GHBC-REQ-016389","GHBC-REQ-016390","GHBC-REQ-016391"]','e3230e9387fe18aef3f0ba9a46636a19c1493c613e1ff6a9c76415bc72abdd77'),
('chunk-4317','GHBC-CHUNK-004317','GHBC-C-004317','24.4.9.2
Layup patterns
Timber decking is permitted to be laid up following one of five standard patterns as defined in Clauses 2304.9.2.1 through 2304.9.2.5. Other patterns are permitted to be used provided that they are substantiated through engineering analysis.',24,'24.4','24.4.9.2','Layup patterns',862,'["TABLE 24.4.6.1 MAXIMUM ALLOWABLE STRESS DESIGN WIND SPEED, Vasd PERMITTED FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(1) ALLOWABLE SPANS FOR TIMBER FLOOR AND ROOF SHEATHING","TABLE 24.4.8(2) SHEATHING TIMBER, MINIMUM GRADE REQUIREMENTS: BOARD GRADE","TABLE 24.4.8(3) ALLOWABLE SPANS AND LOADS FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL","TABLE 24.4.8(4) ALLOWABLE SPAN FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(5) ALLOWABLE LOAD (PSF) FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL ROOF SHEATHING","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(4)","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(5)","Table 24.4.9.3.2 shall be permitted.","TABLE 24.4.9.3.2 FASTENING SCHEDULE","TABLE 24.4.10.1"]','["GHBC-REQ-016392","GHBC-REQ-016393"]','1404b3e72215dd07bbb482d1448b9cea6d85958de4c8ff6305a91ed4f37270d7'),
('chunk-4318','GHBC-CHUNK-004318','GHBC-C-004318','24.4.9.2.1
Simple span pattern
All pieces shall be supported on their ends (in other words, by two supports).',24,'24.4','24.4.9.2.1','Simple span pattern',862,'["TABLE 24.4.6.1 MAXIMUM ALLOWABLE STRESS DESIGN WIND SPEED, Vasd PERMITTED FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(1) ALLOWABLE SPANS FOR TIMBER FLOOR AND ROOF SHEATHING","TABLE 24.4.8(2) SHEATHING TIMBER, MINIMUM GRADE REQUIREMENTS: BOARD GRADE","TABLE 24.4.8(3) ALLOWABLE SPANS AND LOADS FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL","TABLE 24.4.8(4) ALLOWABLE SPAN FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(5) ALLOWABLE LOAD (PSF) FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL ROOF SHEATHING","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(4)","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(5)","Table 24.4.9.3.2 shall be permitted.","TABLE 24.4.9.3.2 FASTENING SCHEDULE","TABLE 24.4.10.1"]','["GHBC-REQ-016394"]','d4a01f5834b4f98a6f36963154066e37c7016a3e857cc853786da4ae5bb9797c'),
('chunk-4319','GHBC-CHUNK-004319','GHBC-C-004319','24.4.9.2.2
Two-span continuous pattern
All pieces shall be supported by three supports, and all end joints shall occur in line on alternating supports. Supporting members shall be designed to accommodate the load redistribution caused by this pattern.',24,'24.4','24.4.9.2.2','Two-span continuous pattern',862,'["TABLE 24.4.6.1 MAXIMUM ALLOWABLE STRESS DESIGN WIND SPEED, Vasd PERMITTED FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(1) ALLOWABLE SPANS FOR TIMBER FLOOR AND ROOF SHEATHING","TABLE 24.4.8(2) SHEATHING TIMBER, MINIMUM GRADE REQUIREMENTS: BOARD GRADE","TABLE 24.4.8(3) ALLOWABLE SPANS AND LOADS FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL","TABLE 24.4.8(4) ALLOWABLE SPAN FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(5) ALLOWABLE LOAD (PSF) FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL ROOF SHEATHING","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(4)","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(5)","Table 24.4.9.3.2 shall be permitted.","TABLE 24.4.9.3.2 FASTENING SCHEDULE","TABLE 24.4.10.1"]','["GHBC-REQ-016395","GHBC-REQ-016396"]','eaa5576d40a9990249bbc46d4973036962113bbaefe70902d45bf4b26f6d9f77'),
('chunk-4320','GHBC-CHUNK-004320','GHBC-C-004320','24.4.9.2.3
Combination simple and two-span
continuous pattern. Courses in end spans shall be alternating simple-span pattern and two-span continuous pattern. End joints shall be staggered in adjacent courses and shall bear on supports.',24,'24.4','24.4.9.2.3','Combination simple and two-span',862,'["TABLE 24.4.6.1 MAXIMUM ALLOWABLE STRESS DESIGN WIND SPEED, Vasd PERMITTED FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(1) ALLOWABLE SPANS FOR TIMBER FLOOR AND ROOF SHEATHING","TABLE 24.4.8(2) SHEATHING TIMBER, MINIMUM GRADE REQUIREMENTS: BOARD GRADE","TABLE 24.4.8(3) ALLOWABLE SPANS AND LOADS FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL","TABLE 24.4.8(4) ALLOWABLE SPAN FOR","TABLE 24.4.8(5) ALLOWABLE LOAD (PSF) FOR WOOD STRUCTURAL PANEL ROOF SHEATHING","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(4)","Table 24.4.8(1), 24.4.8(2), 24.4.8(3) or 24.4.8(5)","Table 24.4.9.3.2 shall be permitted.","TABLE 24.4.9.3.2 FASTENING SCHEDULE","TABLE 24.4.10.1"]','["GHBC-REQ-016397","GHBC-REQ-016398","GHBC-REQ-016399"]','4aff534f4917481d45b485095a5768bbeebf9821a2564c6188d2542c17878d1e');
