USE IN CALCULATING DIAPHRAGM
AND SHEAR WALL DEFLECTION DUE TO FASTENER SLIP (Structural I)a, c Note: For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 foot = 304.8 mm, 1 pound = 4.448 N. a. Increase e values 20 percent for plywood grades other n than Structural I. b. Load per fastener = maximum shear per foot divided by the number of fasteners per foot at interior panel edges. c. Decrease e values 50 percent for seasoned timber n (moisture content < 19 percent).',24,'24.5','24.5.2','Diaphragm deflection',875,'["TABLE 24.5.2(1) en VALUES (inches) FOR","TABLE 24.5.2(2) VALUES OF Gt FOR USE IN CALCULATING DEFLECTION OF WOOD"]','["GHBC-REQ-016593","GHBC-REQ-016594","GHBC-REQ-016595","GHBC-REQ-016596","GHBC-REQ-016597","GHBC-REQ-016598","GHBC-REQ-016599","GHBC-REQ-016600","GHBC-REQ-016601","GHBC-REQ-016602","GHBC-REQ-016603","GHBC-REQ-016604","GHBC-REQ-016605","GHBC-REQ-016606","GHBC-REQ-016607","GHBC-REQ-016608","GHBC-REQ-016609","GHBC-REQ-016610","GHBC-REQ-016611"]','75116cdf3687880510026cd6d3ce06b6e0449b10a694441a1b3429138b8741d3'),
('chunk-4380','GHBC-CHUNK-004380','GHBC-C-004380','Note: For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 pound/inch = 0.1751 N/mm. a. 5-ply applies to plywood with five or more layers. For 5-ply plywood with three layers, use values for 4-ply panels.',24,NULL,NULL,NULL,877,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-016612","GHBC-REQ-016613","GHBC-REQ-016614"]','bd717750b99b419528f6c6c157072243bbb4d3a91cbb31123f54444647b4ee60');
