The effect of the value of the contents of a structure is clears the term ‗consequential effect‘ is intended to cover not only material risks to goods and property but also such aspects as the disruption of essential services of all kinds, particularly in hospitals. The risk to life is generally very small, but if a building is struck, fire or panic can naturally result.  All possible steps should, therefore, be taken to reduce these effects, especially among children, the old, and the sick.',28,'28.13','28.13.1.2','Estimation of exposure risk',1068,'["Table 3:  Overall assessment of risk","Table 3A:  Weighting factor ‗A; - (Use of","Table 3B:Weighting factor ‗B‘ - (Type","Table 3C:   Weighting factor ‗C‘ -  (Contents","Table 3D:   Weighting factor ‗D‘ -","Table 3E:   Weighting factor ‗E‘ -","Table 4 – Examples of calculations for evaluating the need for protection"]','["GHBC-REQ-019461","GHBC-REQ-019462","GHBC-REQ-019463","GHBC-REQ-019464","GHBC-REQ-019465","GHBC-REQ-019466","GHBC-REQ-019467","GHBC-REQ-019468","GHBC-REQ-019469","GHBC-REQ-019470","GHBC-REQ-019471","GHBC-REQ-019472","GHBC-REQ-019473","GHBC-REQ-019474","GHBC-REQ-019475","GHBC-REQ-019476","GHBC-REQ-019477","GHBC-REQ-019478","GHBC-REQ-019479","GHBC-REQ-019480"]','48eb7dd9a3a8f12fd32e718780024e7a5647fb0c56a981ba895ea048cd1cec67'),
('chunk-5026','GHBC-CHUNK-005026','GHBC-C-005026','28.13.1.6
Interpretation of overall risk factor
The risk factor method put forward here is to be taken as giving guidance on what might, in some cases, be a difficult problem.  If the result assessment may lead to anomalies and those who have to decide on protection must exercise judgement.  For example, a steel-framed building may be found to have a low risk factor
A low risk factor may result for chimneys made of brick or concrete.  However, where chimneys are free standing or where they project for more than 4.5m above the adjoining structure, they will require protection regardless of the factor. Such chimneys are, therefore, not covered by the method of assessment.  Similarly, structures containing explosives or flammable substances are also not covered. Results of calculations for different structures are given in Table 8 and a specific case is worked through in 28.13.1.8.',28,'28.13','28.13.1.6','Interpretation of overall risk factor',1071,'["Table 3:  Overall assessment of risk","Table 3A:  Weighting factor ‗A; - (Use of","Table 3B:Weighting factor ‗B‘ - (Type","Table 3C:   Weighting factor ‗C‘ -  (Contents","Table 3D:   Weighting factor ‗D‘ -","Table 3E:   Weighting factor ‗E‘ -","Table 4 – Examples of calculations for evaluating the need for protection"]','["GHBC-REQ-019481","GHBC-REQ-019482","GHBC-REQ-019483","GHBC-REQ-019484","GHBC-REQ-019485","GHBC-REQ-019486","GHBC-REQ-019487","GHBC-REQ-019488"]','6c8bf2f2a7e7d41454d4404b8ff430f0fb911b97ce6e9506bcfdcfe1290c80b4'),
