APPENDIX ‗C‘ (Clause 9.4.2.22) NOISE RATING C-1 Noise rating (NR) is a graphical method of assigning a single number rating to a noise spectrum.  It can be used to specify the maximum acceptable level in each octave band of a frequency spectrum, or to assess the acceptability of a noise spectrum for a particular application. The method was originally proposed for use in assessing environmental noise, but was later also found suitable for describing noise from mechanical ventilation systems in buildings.  To make a rating, the noise spectrum is superposed on a family of NR contours; the NR of the spectrum corresponds to the value of the first NR contour that is entirely above the spectrum. The data for drawing NR contours (from NR 0 to NR 75) is given in Table 12 for the frequency range 31.5 Hz to 8 kHz. C-2 For computational methods the curves are defined by the equation: L = a + bN
