are the minimum clear plumb sizes. The architect/engineer, in conjunction with the builder, shall ensure that adequate tolerances are included in the building design so that the specified minimum clear plumb dimensions are obtained in the finished work.
Note – The words ‗clear plumb dimensions‘ should be noted particularly in case of high rise buildings.',31,NULL,'31.1.4.9.2.1','All plan dimensions of the lift well',1300,'["Table 1:  Recommended dimensions of passenger lifts and service lifts","Table 1 – Concluded","Table 1A:   Recommended dimensions of pit, overhead and machine-room","Table 1 and 1A","Table 2","Table 3","Table 1 and 1A","Table 4","Table 2:  Recommended dimensions of goods lifts for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 3: Recommended dimensions of hospital lifts (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 4:  Recommended dimensions of dumb waiter (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)"]','["GHBC-REQ-024642","GHBC-REQ-024643","GHBC-REQ-024644"]','d43aac6e58eb74e04c6c202da0e365238c557661f341598d9bd3748bffdedcf3'),
('chunk-6366','GHBC-CHUNK-006366','GHBC-C-006366','31.1.4.9.2.2
Rough opening in concrete or brick
walls to accommodate landing doors depend on the design of the architrave. It is advisable to provide sufficient allowances in rough opening width to allow for alignment errors of opening at various landings.',31,NULL,'31.1.4.9.2.2','Rough opening in concrete or brick',1300,'["Table 1:  Recommended dimensions of passenger lifts and service lifts","Table 1 – Concluded","Table 1A:   Recommended dimensions of pit, overhead and machine-room","Table 1 and 1A","Table 2","Table 3","Table 1 and 1A","Table 4","Table 2:  Recommended dimensions of goods lifts for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 3: Recommended dimensions of hospital lifts (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 4:  Recommended dimensions of dumb waiter (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)"]','["GHBC-REQ-024645","GHBC-REQ-024646"]','07e5f7ac5fc8655e0899c79c36751d010c16d1736a8fb3e0fc29808988a95e89'),
('chunk-6367','GHBC-CHUNK-006367','GHBC-C-006367','31.1.4.9.2.3
When more than one lift is located
in a common well, a minimum allowance of 100 mm for separator beams shall be made in the widths shown in Tables 1 to 4.',31,NULL,'31.1.4.9.2.3','When more than one lift is located',1300,'["Table 1:  Recommended dimensions of passenger lifts and service lifts","Table 1 – Concluded","Table 1A:   Recommended dimensions of pit, overhead and machine-room","Table 1 and 1A","Table 2","Table 3","Table 1 and 1A","Table 4","Table 2:  Recommended dimensions of goods lifts for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 3: Recommended dimensions of hospital lifts (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 4:  Recommended dimensions of dumb waiter (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)"]','["GHBC-REQ-024647"]','3ae4cf2c9b9b3db09ac4d0cedfe866c98b24e08164dafd2bf6c4fdb22da32802'),
('chunk-6368','GHBC-CHUNK-006368','GHBC-C-006368','31.1.4.9.2.4
Where the governor operated
counterweight safety is required under conditions stipulated in good practice, the tabulated values should be revised in consultation with the lift manufacturer.',31,NULL,'31.1.4.9.2.4','Where the governor operated',1301,'["Table 1:  Recommended dimensions of passenger lifts and service lifts","Table 1 – Concluded","Table 1A:   Recommended dimensions of pit, overhead and machine-room","Table 1 and 1A","Table 2","Table 3","Table 1 and 1A","Table 4","Table 2:  Recommended dimensions of goods lifts for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 3: Recommended dimensions of hospital lifts (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)","Table 4:  Recommended dimensions of dumb waiter (for speeds up to 0.5 m/s)"]','["GHBC-REQ-024648"]','8ddb2414e842d9baebe270cfb826afe98135be67b7a2113858407bced81e26fd'),
('chunk-6369','GHBC-CHUNK-006369','GHBC-C-006369','31.1.4.9.2.5
