('chunk-6823','GHBC-CHUNK-006823','GHBC-C-006823','35.7.7.1
Maximum gradient for ramps
The maximum gradient for pedestrian ramps shall be 1 in 5 for mercantile or industrial occupancies and 1 in 8 for all other occupancies.  The gradient for every exterior ramp shall be 1 in 10. Maximum gradient of ramps for disabled persons are as given in in this Code.',35,'35.7','35.7.7.1','Maximum gradient for ramps',1355,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-025760","GHBC-REQ-025761","GHBC-REQ-025762"]','830ddc5e76416665fd3f0b42511c113c2503709675155e679df4c43dcb075a82'),
('chunk-6824','GHBC-CHUNK-006824','GHBC-C-006824','35.7.7.2
Level area in ramps
Where a doorway or stairway opens onto the side of a ramp there shall be a level area extending across the full width of the ramp and for a distance of at least 300mm on either side of the opening.',35,'35.7','35.7.7.2','Level area in ramps',1355,'[]','["GHBC-REQ-025763"]','368f5d22188057242f3e7543c24e7b913f3b57b8522b1cc942eeb588ca2bd6ff'),
('chunk-6825','GHBC-CHUNK-006825','GHBC-C-006825','35.7.7.3
