Materials specifications for masonry
units Masonry units shall comply with one of the following: BS 3921: ―Clay bricks and blocks‖ BS  2028: ―Precast concrete blocks‖',35,'35.15','35.16.2.1','Materials specifications for masonry',1365,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025949"]','b2ece3f8a4de7274699bfe65b7d5f73310f03bd47be613c5744a02722b7387be'),
('chunk-6982','GHBC-CHUNK-006982','GHBC-C-006982','35.16.2.2
Used masonry
Used bricks shall be free of old mortar, soot or other surface coating and shall conform to Article 35.16.2.1',35,'35.15','35.16.2.2','Used masonry',1365,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025950"]','31440b13bb4535b44368d183b070d9d469889bfdff709350ad44ed201f369678'),
('chunk-6983','GHBC-CHUNK-006983','GHBC-C-006983','35.16.2.3
Compressive strength
Except as provided in Article 35.16.2.1, the compressive strength of masonry units in a wall of a house of one or two storeys or of a building of one or two storeys which is divided into flats, shall not be less than 2.75N/mm2 for blocks and 5.2N/mm2 for bricks.',35,'35.15','35.16.2.3','Compressive strength',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025951"]','c9b687dcbf18d550b01cecce5f44e411848f0b2b4b38b2ed4dbd3088b385f313'),
('chunk-6984','GHBC-CHUNK-006984','GHBC-C-006984','35.16.2.4
The compressive strength of bricks
and blocks for non-loadbearing partitions shall not be less than 1.4N/mm2 provided the bricks and blocks are satisfactory in other respects.',35,'35.15','35.16.2.4','The compressive strength of bricks',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025952"]','4111df1d74f277f8f455b35e4a9bf6bc52e45335c6e879c06b4e805101c6bfa0'),
('chunk-6985','GHBC-CHUNK-006985','GHBC-C-006985','35.16.3
Mortar',35,'35.15','35.16.3','Mortar',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','63ac3ddca80605b3beb05631b4b6b283fd2e74d8770608ef71d698ac0faae1e1'),
('chunk-6986','GHBC-CHUNK-006986','GHBC-C-006986','35.16.3.1
Lime
Lime used in mortar shall be hydrated.',35,'35.15','35.16.3.1','Lime',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025953"]','a56364025d81969f3bc43f96661192ff102a83fb2dbe366e5af8f767bb203c54'),
('chunk-6987','GHBC-CHUNK-006987','GHBC-C-006987','35.16.3.2
Mortar mixes
Mortar mixes shall conform to Table 35.16.3.A. Mortar containing Portland cement shall not be used later than 2½ hours after mixing.
(Forming Part of Article 35.16.3.2) Mortar mix proportions (by volume) (Refer to Dr. Lumor)',35,'35.15','35.16.3.2','Mortar mixes',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025954","GHBC-REQ-025955","GHBC-REQ-025956"]','dff60e3f673079d701141a75826af14331fb6a6d4bddc68255f715e1d6ef21cc'),
('chunk-6988','GHBC-CHUNK-006988','GHBC-C-006988','35.16.4
Mortar joints',35,'35.15','35.16.4','Mortar joints',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','16a18289ed5ee403daff214f78db3c8b107f2a1c2641337036dfebd370cf59d1'),
('chunk-6989','GHBC-CHUNK-006989','GHBC-C-006989','35.16.4.1
Mortar joint thickness
The maximum average joint thickness shall be 12mm.  Maximum thickness of an individual joint shall be 20mm.',35,'35.15','35.16.4.1','Mortar joint thickness',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025957","GHBC-REQ-025958"]','4fbd298ce7fd7fbe7e452f755c5805a1055d1b0561daadadd41f08775b9e4469'),
('chunk-6990','GHBC-CHUNK-006990','GHBC-C-006990','35.16.4.2
Solid masonry joints
Solid masonry units shall be laid with full head and bed joints.',35,'35.15','35.16.4.2','Solid masonry joints',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025959"]','e5affdf17089f26e300c5c162ea860cc8e9ea74b9a4ba2272fb0819a6b88dc9b');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-6991','GHBC-CHUNK-006991','GHBC-C-006991','35.16.4.3
Hollow masonry joints
Hollow masonry units shall be laid with mortar applied to head and bed joints of both inner and outer face shells.',35,'35.15','35.16.4.3','Hollow masonry joints',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025960"]','49d7a26b5bf319c2429f5c46bb7433b8ec0c09a467c38c23cdac7ff117bba1d9'),
('chunk-6992','GHBC-CHUNK-006992','GHBC-C-006992','35.16.5
Masonry support',35,'35.15','35.16.5','Masonry support',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','36b460dfa150a0aee42f590fe1c8e39290e23efe8c2ad62e8974b9199d4ce680'),
('chunk-6993','GHBC-CHUNK-006993','GHBC-C-006993','35.16.5.1
Masonry support
All masonry shall be supported on masonry, concrete or steel.
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.15','35.16.5.1','Masonry support',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025961","GHBC-REQ-025962"]','0b58d3007b6e2ebd2ffbf8a41e9ef66624421846a46d421b85547c15d6e2ee89'),
('chunk-6994','GHBC-CHUNK-006994','GHBC-C-006994','35.16.5.2
Lintels
Masonry over openings shall be supported by steel, reinforced concrete or masonry lintels or arches designed to support the imposed load.',35,'35.15','35.16.5.2','Lintels',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025963"]','fb651c17dae8e1e7715cfa09905088933983df2ff3cb2a563d4509727b11993b'),
('chunk-6995','GHBC-CHUNK-006995','GHBC-C-006995','35.16.5.3
Every masonry wall shall be at least as thick as the wall it supports.',35,'35.15','35.16.5.3',NULL,1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025964"]','7c98a3795b9c8eec6540edd1e4bf5336d9d252c7bc3f1a08a8b90dc6848d1190'),
('chunk-6996','GHBC-CHUNK-006996','GHBC-C-006996','35.16.6
Thickness and height',35,'35.15','35.16.6','Thickness and height',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','c9bacc4f0ff1005418a81c62bdf703c79445b3a4a203c7c37ef59deb5fc56d99'),
('chunk-6997','GHBC-CHUNK-006997','GHBC-C-006997','35.16.6.1
Thickness of solid external walls
Masonry external walls other than cavity walls in one storey buildings and the top storeys of two storey buildings shall be not less than 140mm thick provided the walls are not more than 2.75m high at the eaves and 4.60m high at the peaks of gable ends.  The external walls of the bottom storeys of two storeys buildings shall not be less than 215mm.',35,'35.15','35.16.6.1','Thickness of solid external walls',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025965","GHBC-REQ-025966"]','06d229dae792ceab329c5af99ea5df20675229c4875a9577d2a06f9dfd97e6f4'),
('chunk-6998','GHBC-CHUNK-006998','GHBC-C-006998','35.16.6.2
Thickness of interior walls
The thickness of loadbearing interior walls shall be determined on the basis of Article 35.16.9.1
Masonry finish resting on a bearing support shall be of solid units not less than 75mm thick for wall heights up to 12m.  Such finish over wood-frame walls shall have not less than a 25mm air space behind the finish.  Masonry finish less than 90mm thick shall have unraked joints.',35,'35.15','35.16.6.2','Thickness of interior walls',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025967","GHBC-REQ-025968","GHBC-REQ-025969","GHBC-REQ-025970"]','9346dd35deba765322400b91e37d4ab25223989ad99cb72c416728c4bbf4c7dc'),
('chunk-6999','GHBC-CHUNK-006999','GHBC-C-006999','35.16.6.5
Parapet walls
The height of parapet walls above the adjacent roof surface shall not be less than three times the parapet wall thickness.',35,'35.15','35.16.6.5','Parapet walls',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025971"]','251660d05e4597f43c3eb2bddea19ee6fe96e135771fe9b1270571692e3c9d00'),
('chunk-7000','GHBC-CHUNK-007000','GHBC-C-007000','35.16.7
Chases and recesses',35,'35.15','35.16.7','Chases and recesses',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','cbe48ebff36511b3001ecae640a55130c319db3b1c6c377c77cd451ca1b0f531');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7001','GHBC-CHUNK-007001','GHBC-C-007001','35.16.7.1
Size of chases and recesses
Except as permitted in Article 35.16.7.3, the depth of any chase or recess shall not exceed ⅓ the thickness of the wall and the horizontal projection of the chase or recess shall not exceed 500mm.',35,'35.15','35.16.7.1','Size of chases and recesses',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025972"]','e83cad33f4dfe6eaa34c36d3a136797206de76ff1258a500d937e111e1823e44'),
('chunk-7002','GHBC-CHUNK-007002','GHBC-C-007002','35.16.7.2
Location of chases and recesses
Chases and recesses shall be not less than four times the wall thickness apart and not less
any masonry supported above such a chase or recess shall be supported by a lintel or arch.',35,'35.15','35.16.7.2','Location of chases and recesses',1366,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025973","GHBC-REQ-025974"]','eb00b391ca800e8d5a1bf59a9f4ef93e27ac31177f86e3ad3f46d9bdee309a7e'),
('chunk-7003','GHBC-CHUNK-007003','GHBC-C-007003','35.16.8
Support of loads',35,'35.15','35.16.8','Support of loads',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','211773ffdae4751f59b77b04bf605c07a782883ebb2f5687202ee4fb52d54e30'),
('chunk-7004','GHBC-CHUNK-007004','GHBC-C-007004','35.16.8.1
Capping of walls
Loadbearing walls of hollow masonry units supporting roof or floor framing members shall be capped with not less than 50mm of solid masonry, or have the top course filled with concrete.  Capping may be omitted where the framing is supported on a wood plate not less than 50mm thick, the same width as the masonry wall.',35,'35.15','35.16.8.1','Capping of walls',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025975","GHBC-REQ-025976"]','85e0a9d3e2fd27185e54f64773d36cb5b89fff1554c4373394a9bf426bd1ad7f'),
('chunk-7005','GHBC-CHUNK-007005','GHBC-C-007005','35.16.8.2
Bearing area
The bearing area under beams and joists shall be sufficient to carry the supported load.  In no case shall the minimum length of end bearing of beams supported masonry be less than 90mm.  The length of end bearing of floor, roof or ceiling joists supported on masonry shall be not less than 40mm.',35,'35.15','35.16.8.2','Bearing area',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025977","GHBC-REQ-025978","GHBC-REQ-025979"]','02415cbfcecde7fcc1b4c584c24757142f52fd520173cb5a78946a3545a41fd3'),
('chunk-7006','GHBC-CHUNK-007006','GHBC-C-007006','35.16.9
Lateral support',35,'35.15','35.16.9','Lateral support',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','eb84c25bf65aac24eff8908bd56280788c226857716b059d74a51020138a36a3'),
('chunk-7007','GHBC-CHUNK-007007','GHBC-C-007007','35.16.9.1
Lateral support of masonry walls
Masonry walls and partitions shall be supported at right angles to the wall by floor or roof construction or by intersecting masonry walls or buttresses.  The spacing of such supports shall conform to Table 35.16.9.A
35.16.9.2 Floor and roof constructions providing required lateral support for walls as required in Article 7.16.9.1 shall be constructed to transfer lateral loads to walls or buttresses approximately at right angles to the laterally supported walls.
(Forming part of Article 7.16.9.1) Maximum Distances Between lateral wall supports
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.15','35.16.9.1','Lateral support of masonry walls',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025980","GHBC-REQ-025981","GHBC-REQ-025982","GHBC-REQ-025983","GHBC-REQ-025984"]','1c52fe0f3847b215f6350d12ceceec522b4ca2876814063f430378bcad6bd14f'),
('chunk-7008','GHBC-CHUNK-007008','GHBC-C-007008','35.16.10
Exterior finish',35,'35.15','35.16.10','Exterior finish',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','[]','59e94d8db64a050df196725eaa8cc8cca085481a6b9d9c9fdacac54913ec5dd9'),
('chunk-7009','GHBC-CHUNK-007009','GHBC-C-007009','35.16.10.1
Sandcrete Block Exterior Finish
Above-grade external walls of sandcrete block shall be stuccoed, painted or otherwise finished to provide breather-type water repellency.',35,'35.15','35.16.10.1','Sandcrete Block Exterior Finish',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025985"]','1fc88562d6ed3d2e778ab9671e07760734d372789da0a36746814bed1061c4b8'),
('chunk-7010','GHBC-CHUNK-007010','GHBC-C-007010','35.16.11
Reinforcement for earthquake
resistance',35,'35.15','35.16.11','Reinforcement for earthquake',1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025986"]','e945a09d463b5d05ba026132047371a355741a88037100c1b5f01b5793d36579');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7011','GHBC-CHUNK-007011','GHBC-C-007011','35.16.11.1
Where reinforcement is required in this clause, masonry walls shall be reinforced horizontally and vertically with steel having a total cross-clauseal area of not less than 0.002 times the cross-clauseal area of the wall, so that not less than ⅓ of the required area is installed either horizontally or vertically and the remaining in the other direction.',35,'35.15','35.16.11.1',NULL,1367,'["Table 35.16.3.A","Table 35.16.9.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025987"]','6c0c53db229992b0f1571b3551881832fe8bad9f3fe73596d4d4a93d3b9e1b9e'),
('chunk-7012','GHBC-CHUNK-007012','GHBC-C-007012','35.17.1
Scope',35,'35.17','35.17.1','Scope',1367,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','5e73aca24f45b8e7be1012e51b0f5898f3895dae49301a536531d8a55a3ea786'),
('chunk-7013','GHBC-CHUNK-007013','GHBC-C-007013','35.17.1.1
Wood-frame construction
This clause applies to conventional woodframe construction in which the framing members are spaced not more than 600mm centres.',35,'35.17','35.17.1.1','Wood-frame construction',1367,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025988"]','b2fdbea8d71b17681ee5dae42e2122436694bd99a04275019f89a83765fbd58f'),
('chunk-7014','GHBC-CHUNK-007014','GHBC-C-007014','35.17.1.2
Design live load
The requirements in this clause with regard to floor framing, sub-flooring and their fastenings apply to floors for which the design live load does not exceed 2.5KN/m2.',35,'35.17','35.17.1.2','Design live load',1367,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025989"]','e36b8a197fbd5ce9a3e2831c04132dc015659f5fa8ddd4d14a453088332f4191'),
('chunk-7015','GHBC-CHUNK-007015','GHBC-C-007015','35.17.1.3
The requirement in this clause with regard to wall framing and its fastenings apply to walls which support floors for which the design live load does not exceed 2.5KN/m2 on any floor.',35,'35.17','35.17.1.3',NULL,1367,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025990"]','3830a3c9ff198a7bef960ef2679153a04e279515d47a187cafee0faf14dae362'),
('chunk-7016','GHBC-CHUNK-007016','GHBC-C-007016','35.17.1.5
Post, beam and plank construction
and plank frame wall construction shall conform to this Code.',35,'35.17','35.17.1.5','Post, beam and plank construction',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025991"]','566b84ea6307412f7c5e21ac475d1b6b195949e18b19e3eb4b35b1e689716988'),
('chunk-7017','GHBC-CHUNK-007017','GHBC-C-007017','35.17.2
General',35,'35.17','35.17.2','General',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','6d9dede111adf0c2fff3809a938c46b9fecbec05408e8cb827f3f864e05782d7'),
('chunk-7018','GHBC-CHUNK-007018','GHBC-C-007018','35.17.2.1
Rigidity
All members shall be so framed, anchored, fastened, tied and braced to provide the necessary strength and rigidity.',35,'35.17','35.17.2.1','Rigidity',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025992"]','adc092b84e16fad8bab1dc91051b09067a2d0c43188f209a0d22a51b100cf3af'),
('chunk-7019','GHBC-CHUNK-007019','GHBC-C-007019','35.17.2.2
Treatment of end members
Ends of wood joists or beams and other members framing into masonry or concrete shall be treated to prevent decay where the bottom of the member is at or below ground level, or a 15mm air space shall be provided at the end sides of the member.',35,'35.17','35.17.2.2','Treatment of end members',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025993"]','c7bc0c31067a3e18409b84bda5a4cf77f24738880f2a94c938990da89acab2ac'),
('chunk-7020','GHBC-CHUNK-007020','GHBC-C-007020','35.17.2.3
Wood framing members that are not
pressure treated with wood preservative and which are supported on a concrete in contact with the ground or fill shall be separated from the concrete by an approved damp proofing material, except that such damp proofing is not required where the wood member is a least 150mm above the ground.',35,'35.17','35.17.2.3','Wood framing members that are not',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025994"]','9511fe9e553cf4e7a4653ec4e4198483fe0451aefacee13f61cba11ebe5e5eb7');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7021','GHBC-CHUNK-007021','GHBC-C-007021','35.17.3
Nails and staples',35,'35.17','35.17.3','Nails and staples',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','d0d8927623588f839b89e0fbb4dbf48e1f99cf5c2e19be64ba5b13f83df80ac7'),
('chunk-7022','GHBC-CHUNK-007022','GHBC-C-007022','35.17.3.1
Nails and staples specification
Nails specified in this clause shall be common steel wire nails or common spiral nails unless otherwise indicated.  Other nails providing at least equivalent performance may also be used.',35,'35.17','35.17.3.1','Nails and staples specification',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025995","GHBC-REQ-025996"]','cf2c8dd2635acdf31c5c58fa4ef148dcd77e0fab0758c3b18184dc3a79673cd0'),
('chunk-7023','GHBC-CHUNK-007023','GHBC-C-007023','35.17.3.2
Nail length
All nails shall be long enough so that not less than half their length penetrates into the second member. Splitting of wood members shall be minimized by staggering the nails in the direction of the grain and by keeping nails well in from the edges.',35,'35.17','35.17.3.2','Nail length',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025997","GHBC-REQ-025998"]','1687f9722a5eeb053eca718cf4e96d6f564abd6f5ead1e137188f726e6c9a753'),
('chunk-7024','GHBC-CHUNK-007024','GHBC-C-007024','35.17.4
Allowable spans',35,'35.17','35.17.4','Allowable spans',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','d355dd510f853bad7efd2916d77523baa7111d7bbfd3e0b64a6b4e83ba72d914'),
('chunk-7025','GHBC-CHUNK-007025','GHBC-C-007025','35.17.4.1
The spans of wood joists, rafters
and beams shall be determined in conformance with Part 5 of this Code.',35,'35.17','35.17.4.1','The spans of wood joists, rafters',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-025999"]','7e9a28497ecb93adb9a479b03cd1e3bc9d1c69d38d8b107decbbd3bc2bdcc2ff'),
('chunk-7026','GHBC-CHUNK-007026','GHBC-C-007026','35.17.5
Notching and drilling',35,'35.17','35.17.5','Notching and drilling',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','e51eb417f86c8230a798fd011ed44bb70654bbe7aa11b1caba399ee9370936fc'),
('chunk-7027','GHBC-CHUNK-007027','GHBC-C-007027','35.17.5.1
Notches and drilling
Holes drilled in roof, floor or ceiling framing members shall be not larger than ¼ the depth of the member and shall be located not less than 50mm from the edges, unless the depth
DGS 1207: 2018 of the member is increased by the size of the hole.',35,'35.17','35.17.5.1','Notches and drilling',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026000","GHBC-REQ-026001"]','4245aa2ae2ff650edb169e3d4a6a7facf0b2e794a63ab75afeb7403155b3fad2'),
('chunk-7028','GHBC-CHUNK-007028','GHBC-C-007028','35.17.5.2
Floor, roof and ceiling framing
members may be notched provided the notch is located on the top of the member within ½ the joist depth from the edge of bearing and is not deeper than ⅓ the joist depth, unless the depth of the member is increased by the size of the notch.',35,'35.17','35.17.5.2','Floor, roof and ceiling framing',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026002"]','97dd86225b6a18879cf3a79a8a27989b97404e9e869adbf094ca4b7a685fc795'),
('chunk-7029','GHBC-CHUNK-007029','GHBC-C-007029','35.17.5.3
Wall studs shall not be notched, drilled or otherwise damaged so that the undamaged portion of the stud is less than ⅔ the depth of the stud if the stud is loadbearing or 40mm if the stud is non-loadbearing, unless the weakened studs are suitably reinforced.',35,'35.17','35.17.5.3',NULL,1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026003"]','a0e14fc63c72d5fcf5724e6f873399dae2c383e4b8219d29de46b021e6844333'),
('chunk-7030','GHBC-CHUNK-007030','GHBC-C-007030','35.17.5.4
The top plates in loadbearing walls
and partitions shall not be notched, drilled or otherwise weakened to reduce the undamaged width to less than 50mm, unless the weakened plates are suitably reinforced.',35,'35.17','35.17.5.4','The top plates in loadbearing walls',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026004"]','2602220dd08345ee5483304dd7a06adf2b2f2f466ed1277f507b09ec40ef4c71');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7031','GHBC-CHUNK-007031','GHBC-C-007031','35.17.5.5
Roof truss members shall not be notched, drilled or otherwise weakened unless such notching or drilling is allowed for in the design of the truss.',35,'35.17','35.17.5.5',NULL,1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026005"]','02160eb7037fe1468055489548b62cb6fea17b10c84aede43a2e2c200b7e8f61'),
('chunk-7032','GHBC-CHUNK-007032','GHBC-C-007032','35.17.6
Anchorage',35,'35.17','35.17.6','Anchorage',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','ab2211ea56b3f9539246f59386aaf86d47893e520d0722ee1b88a7179a44c409'),
('chunk-7033','GHBC-CHUNK-007033','GHBC-C-007033','35.17.6.1
Anchorage
Building frames shall be anchored to the foundation, unless a structural analysis of the wind and earth pressures shows anchorage is not required.',35,'35.17','35.17.6.1','Anchorage',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026006"]','45a10e1d63faf869475282584ddd5701c4c0aea7ab56049bd5015168d821a2f5'),
('chunk-7034','GHBC-CHUNK-007034','GHBC-C-007034','35.17.6.2
Anchorage shall be provided by embedding the ends of the ground floor joists in concrete, or fastening the sill plate to the foundation with not less than 13mm diameter anchor bolts spaced not more than 2.5m centres. Such anchor bolts shall be embedded no less than 100mm in the foundation and so designed that they may be tightened without withdrawing them from the foundation.',35,'35.17','35.17.6.2',NULL,1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026007","GHBC-REQ-026008"]','a683d4ae8edb181b49c322b9b84640a2d842ded620070d8da977c85adb6b0221'),
('chunk-7035','GHBC-CHUNK-007035','GHBC-C-007035','35.17.6.3
Exterior columns and posts shall be anchored to resist uplift and lateral movement.',35,'35.17','35.17.6.3',NULL,1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026009"]','85fbe76293b13851064c71a11aec616d4664000033ca8f80dfee1859dfb704cf'),
('chunk-7036','GHBC-CHUNK-007036','GHBC-C-007036','35.17.7
Sill plates',35,'35.17','35.17.7','Sill plates',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','5e897facd58a5a880cbeb51b26515cb42950c0df5ce986acc9f55fb26e2ea1f1'),
('chunk-7037','GHBC-CHUNK-007037','GHBC-C-007037','35.17.7.1
Sill plates
Where sill plates provide bearing for the floor system, they shall be not less than 50mm by 100mm material.',35,'35.17','35.17.7.1','Sill plates',1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026010"]','3f7dbf9eb78fc316150532be488c2cfd876fb84b7b2cc1da23ddbcdf8fc7e3f2'),
('chunk-7038','GHBC-CHUNK-007038','GHBC-C-007038','35.17.7.2
Sill plates shall be levelled by setting them on a full bed of mortar, except that where the top of the foundation is level they may be laid directly on the foundation provided the
junction between the foundation and the sill plate is caulked.',35,'35.17','35.17.7.2',NULL,1368,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026011","GHBC-REQ-026012"]','e857be5314a0a1485d91f1c583d03abb747ada1d5a1b30da9ddbe720ebbf95e4'),
('chunk-7039','GHBC-CHUNK-007039','GHBC-C-007039','35.17.8
Beams to support floors',35,'35.17','35.17.8','Beams to support floors',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','10561c347942bdfa9a480cebe9505fbf6ee472803bc21c4e6071aee9fe1a38b3'),
('chunk-7040','GHBC-CHUNK-007040','GHBC-C-007040','35.17.8.1
Beams
Beams shall have even and level bearing to support floors.  Beams shall have not less than 90mm length of bearing at end supports.',35,'35.17','35.17.8.1','Beams',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026013","GHBC-REQ-026014"]','e753fdfbe54b6dec2d771a503932168d4b470114828dfe166235b9b8e6138b88');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7041','GHBC-CHUNK-007041','GHBC-C-007041','35.17.8.2
Built-up wood beams
Where a beam is made up of individual pieces of timber that are nailed together, the individual members shall be 50mm or greater in thickness and installed on edge.',35,'35.17','35.17.8.2','Built-up wood beams',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026015"]','f175a98ec0cee1f92a2fce62ebf04e1f67133c64c68bfa3204c5232da33338dd'),
('chunk-7042','GHBC-CHUNK-007042','GHBC-C-007042','35.17.8.3
Where the individual members of a beam described in Article 35.17.8.2 are butted together to form a joint, each such joint shall occur over a support or at or within 150mm of the end quarter points of the clear span of the beam.',35,'35.17','35.17.8.3',NULL,1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026016"]','7cbc3b6ab688ddf051f34d1d60e930c861f3068a43dffc8f562cbb646619f720'),
('chunk-7043','GHBC-CHUNK-007043','GHBC-C-007043','35.17.8.4
Joints in individual members of beams that are located at or near the end quarter points described in Article 35.17.8.3 shall not reduce the effective beam width by more than half.  Members joined at quarter points shall be continuous over the adjacent supports.',35,'35.17','35.17.8.4',NULL,1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026017","GHBC-REQ-026018"]','b75638cec71699ee074e573ee092ec77f8d982727ba44509494f55881bc8cf03'),
('chunk-7044','GHBC-CHUNK-007044','GHBC-C-007044','35.17.8.5
Except as provided in Article
35.17.8.6 where 50mm members are laid on edge to form a built-up beam, individual members shall be nailed together with a double row of nails at least 90mm in length, spaced not more than 450mm apart in each row with the end nails located 100mm to 150mm from the end of each piece.',35,'35.17','35.17.8.5','Except as provided in Article',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026019"]','04cb5fb5b7b401f08f3520864684905cea16feafe0a4f7db1bd32b820c8129aa'),
('chunk-7045','GHBC-CHUNK-007045','GHBC-C-007045','35.17.8.6
Where 50mm members in built-up
wood beams are not nailed together as provided in Article 7.17.8.5 they shall be bolted together with at least 13mm diameter bolts equipped with washers and spaced not more than 1.2m centres with the end bolts located not more than 600mm from the ends of the members.',35,'35.17','35.17.8.6','Where 50mm members in built-up',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026020"]','df0358c84da563fd719b9a846a5ae42d2eb51d584e2a91d0889f4d34a40bb229'),
('chunk-7046','GHBC-CHUNK-007046','GHBC-C-007046','35.17.9
Floor joists',35,'35.17','35.17.9','Floor joists',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','2fa984afe08e5a3b0408cc67ce54222f49c96a61935b2d9be0bf11bef364c8d5'),
('chunk-7047','GHBC-CHUNK-007047','GHBC-C-007047','35.17.9.1
Except when supported on ribbon
boards, floor joists shall have not less than 40mm length of end bearing.  Ribbon boards shall be not less than 25mm by 100mm timber let into the studs.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.1','Except when supported on ribbon',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026021","GHBC-REQ-026022"]','fcc56cfd4d474b3c347a48d8febfc92bf2b174212b709b9476fc2184d264706d'),
('chunk-7048','GHBC-CHUNK-007048','GHBC-C-007048','35.17.9.2
Floor joists may be supported on the top of beams or may be framed into the sides of beams.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.2',NULL,1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026023"]','42796eedbf74ab8797ba6ac341090b54cf229fbbde1d6ce75b70077cf89b9878'),
('chunk-7049','GHBC-CHUNK-007049','GHBC-C-007049','35.17.9.3
When framed into the sides of a wood beam, the joists shall be supported on
DGS 1207: 2018 joist hangers or other acceptable mechanical connectors or on not less than 50mm by 75mm ledger strips nailed to the side of the beam.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.3',NULL,1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026024","GHBC-REQ-026025"]','2015b99ac0593a31850b59f712e1d6d82f160b03538c7b79e9ef5878b7c19798'),
('chunk-7050','GHBC-CHUNK-007050','GHBC-C-007050','35.17.9.4
Unless ceiling furring or plywood
cladding is installed on the underside of floor joists, floor joists shall be restrained from twisting at the end supports and at intervals between supports not exceeding 2.10m. Such restraint may be provided at the end supports by toe nailing to the support, or by end nailing the joists to the header joist.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.4','Unless ceiling furring or plywood',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026026","GHBC-REQ-026027"]','2f178e493edee5f1033f6a4570d83c3047605e2861d5c90f0b06ca333ff2582a');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7051','GHBC-CHUNK-007051','GHBC-C-007051','35.17.9.5
Double joists
Header joists around floor openings shall be doubled when they exceed 1.2m in length. The size of header joists exceeding 3.15m in length shall be determined by calculations.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.5','Double joists',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026028","GHBC-REQ-026029"]','eb0266ceccfc276753ae18f5e1a322ea55abaa6cd6b62cea9439707978ed52e6'),
('chunk-7052','GHBC-CHUNK-007052','GHBC-C-007052','35.17.9.6
Trimmer joists around floor openings
shall be doubled when the length of the header joist exceeds 810mm.  When the header joist exceeds 2.03m in length the size of the trimmer joists shall be determined by calculations.
35.17.9.7 Support of non-loadbearing partitions Non-loadbearing partitions parallel to floor joists shall be supported on beams, loadbearing walls or double joists where the partition is over 1.8m in length and contains openings that are not full ceiling height. Where such partitions contain no openings or openings that are full ceiling heights, the joists need not be doubled.  Non-loadbearing partitions less than 1.8m in length need not be supported on framing but may be supported by the subfloor.  Doubled joists may be separated not more than 200mm by blocking, if the blocking is not less than 50mm by 100mm timber spaced not more than 1.2m apart.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.6','Trimmer joists around floor openings',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026030","GHBC-REQ-026031","GHBC-REQ-026032","GHBC-REQ-026033","GHBC-REQ-026034","GHBC-REQ-026035"]','61b13032e211561a36c7a6bc95dd525c007ecfb6fd5d23da08e43eed3fa5f1ea'),
('chunk-7053','GHBC-CHUNK-007053','GHBC-C-007053','35.17.9.8
Non-loadbearing partitions at right angles to the floor joists are not restricted as to location.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.8',NULL,1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026036"]','0844ae79a42bc77cc4122ca6c34afe72d246560bf3f40880093d7685e4869d6c'),
('chunk-7054','GHBC-CHUNK-007054','GHBC-C-007054','35.17.9.9
Support of loadbearing partitions
Loadbearing interior walls parallel to floor joists shall be supported by beams of walls of sufficient strength to transfer safely, the design loads to the vertical supports',35,'35.17','35.17.9.9','Support of loadbearing partitions',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026037"]','5400cad98d40175b3bfdad3d6776595a40fd16630ca5ff7696fb54783d63a352'),
('chunk-7055','GHBC-CHUNK-007055','GHBC-C-007055','35.17.9.10
Location of loadbearing interior
walls Loadbearing interior walls at right angles to floor joists shall be located not more than
900mm from the joist supports when the wall does not support a floor, and not more than 600mm from the joist support when the wall supports one floor unless the joist size is designed to support such loads.',35,'35.17','35.17.9.10','Location of loadbearing interior',1369,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026038","GHBC-REQ-026039"]','38c859e5ff82b0d1547164495717c05af646860dc54b0b88ebf2624d80d04a84'),
('chunk-7056','GHBC-CHUNK-007056','GHBC-C-007056','35.17.10
Wall studs',35,'35.17','35.17.10','Wall studs',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','78d4fec8cd38fb96151ed599d6cd5f4cd0fef6060383639f9c2baf7fcc8b5be5'),
('chunk-7057','GHBC-CHUNK-007057','GHBC-C-007057','35.17.10.1
Wall studs
Wall studs shall be continuous for the full storey height except at openings and shall not be spliced.',35,'35.17','35.17.10.1','Wall studs',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026040"]','247fed80fd574830d2586a619dca2ad3d194983a16f549f3a4d14679ce1570c2'),
('chunk-7058','GHBC-CHUNK-007058','GHBC-C-007058','35.17.10.2
Position of wall studs
Wall studs shall be placed at right angles to the wall face, except that studs on the flat may be used in gable ends of roofs that contain only unfinished space or in non-loadbearing partitions. 35.17.10.3 Design of corners and interclauses Corners and interclauses shall be designed to provide adequate support for the vertical
(Forming part of Article 7.17.10.6) Size and spacing of studs',35,'35.17','35.17.10.2','Position of wall studs',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026041","GHBC-REQ-026042","GHBC-REQ-026043"]','177eab3c66f4128beb66b5f219886558c3fc64ee214fa89654ad997f22c07d10'),
('chunk-7059','GHBC-CHUNK-007059','GHBC-C-007059','35.17.11
Wall plates',35,'35.17','35.17.11','Wall plates',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','b0d3cd014a1e101b395ff2b442caa28c39c61ec1befba138f04d98ca3db13722'),
('chunk-7060','GHBC-CHUNK-007060','GHBC-C-007060','35.17.11.1
Wall plates
Wall plates shall be not less than 50mm thick and shall be the same width as the wall studs, except that in non-loadbearing partitions and in loadbearing walls where the studs are located directly over framing members, the bottom wall plate may be 20mm thick.
DGS 1207: 2018 edges of interior and exterior cladding materials, and in no instance shall exterior corners be framed with less than the equivalent of two (2) studs.',35,'35.17','35.17.11.1','Wall plates',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026044","GHBC-REQ-026045"]','a17c80f79f4d8f62ac221ddb8af03d60a96f35d383331219bc87c70a6a71227e');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7061','GHBC-CHUNK-007061','GHBC-C-007061','35.17.10.4
Double studs
Except as provided in Article 35.17.10.5 studs shall be doubled on each side of openings so that the inner studs extend from the lintel to the bottom wall plate and the outer studs extend from the top wall plate to the bottom wall plate.',35,'35.17','35.17.10.4','Double studs',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026046"]','660e0e26865af4a45c0f035c708fa38a1cb8cc03f72757c2774413c624793cdf'),
('chunk-7062','GHBC-CHUNK-007062','GHBC-C-007062','35.17.10.5
Single studs
Single studs may be used on either side of openings in non-loadbearing partitions provided the studs extend from the top wall plate to the bottom wall plate.',35,'35.17','35.17.10.5','Single studs',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026047"]','44c179f250eee5534f31590c57a0e573801af1048c1d158c39f1ba80bbf24433'),
('chunk-7063','GHBC-CHUNK-007063','GHBC-C-007063','35.17.10.6
The size and spacing of studs
shall conform to Table 35.17.10. A
A bottom plate shall be provided in all cases. The bottom plate in exterior walls shall not project more than ⅓ the plate width over the support.',35,'35.17','35.17.10.6','The size and spacing of studs',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026048","GHBC-REQ-026049","GHBC-REQ-026050","GHBC-REQ-026051"]','8bde9ab974f20cc4635f794754dc8c80e330169e78e6a252c242a17a433d62ae'),
('chunk-7064','GHBC-CHUNK-007064','GHBC-C-007064','35.17.11.3
Top plates in loadbearing walls
Except as permitted in Articles 35.17.11.4 and 35.17.11.5 no fewer than two top plates shall be provided in loadbearing walls and partitions.',35,'35.17','35.17.11.3','Top plates in loadbearing walls',1370,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026052"]','574b88a8b80f01b06a64ba1cd668589ccab8939ef194f5dfb8089270110e664c'),
('chunk-7065','GHBC-CHUNK-007065','GHBC-C-007065','35.17.11.4
A single top plate may be used in a clause of a loadbearing wall containing a lintel provided the top plate forms a tie across the lintel.',35,'35.17','35.17.11.4',NULL,1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026053"]','1045412dd5994eff4394b03801acb9a1763302b2b217b93da77cdf22fb5f1997'),
('chunk-7066','GHBC-CHUNK-007066','GHBC-C-007066','35.17.11.5
A single top plate may be used in loadbearing wall where the concentrated loads from ceilings, floors and roofs are not more than 50mm to one side of the supporting studs and in all non-loadbearing partitions.',35,'35.17','35.17.11.5',NULL,1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026054"]','8a13dee1e1c5f1e26c96b0228af5646c05f4fa12db86e00f6cd5f522aa45ccc3'),
('chunk-7067','GHBC-CHUNK-007067','GHBC-C-007067','35.17.11.6
Joints in top plates
Joints in top plates of loadbearing walls shall be staggered at least one (1) stud spacing.',35,'35.17','35.17.11.6','Joints in top plates',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026055"]','fc626eb3cd1481a76bf5ef1d94762539c5b99606ca85b15d725bc05888388d7d'),
('chunk-7068','GHBC-CHUNK-007068','GHBC-C-007068','35.17.11.7
Tying of top plates at corners
The top plates in loadbearing walls shall be lapped or otherwise suitably tied at corners and intersecting walls.  Joints in single top plates used with loadbearing walls shall be suitably tied.',35,'35.17','35.17.11.7','Tying of top plates at corners',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026056","GHBC-REQ-026057"]','d0fbf70ee124d9e4651c583df8128b2e9c48ca8c26e94a0bb14360a18d0fdbea'),
('chunk-7069','GHBC-CHUNK-007069','GHBC-C-007069','35.17.12
Framing over openings',35,'35.17','35.17.12','Framing over openings',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','a541618200e2fef74a5b3499fd3b3341f40dc8bee86e013def0a724f3ff3a6f1'),
('chunk-7070','GHBC-CHUNK-007070','GHBC-C-007070','35.17.12.1
Except as provided in Article
35.17.12.3 openings in non-loadbearing walls shall be bridged with not less than 50mm material the same width as the studs nailed to adjacent studs.',35,'35.17','35.17.12.1','Except as provided in Article',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026058"]','08852d95e1f2a8d2e2e2317b5086d1633f015233de70d951e505a8ffb582fe24');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7071','GHBC-CHUNK-007071','GHBC-C-007071','35.17.12.2
Openings in loadbearing walls shall be bridged with lintels designed to carry the super-imposed loads to adjacent studs. Except as provided in Article 35.17.12.3 where 2 or more members are used in lintels, they shall be fastened together with not less than 85mm nails in a double row, with nails not more than 450mm apart in each row.  The lintel members may be separated by filler pieces.',35,'35.17','35.17.12.2',NULL,1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026059","GHBC-REQ-026060","GHBC-REQ-026061"]','a0b63c85cc8133de9e493b13b420a825fd5faf34451f261dcb568ce85c6fa01a'),
('chunk-7072','GHBC-CHUNK-007072','GHBC-C-007072','35.17.12.3
In loadbearing exterior and interior
walls of 50mm by 75mm framing members, lintels shall consist of solid 75mm thick members on edge or 50mm thick and 20mm thick members securely nailed together.',35,'35.17','35.17.12.3','In loadbearing exterior and interior',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026062"]','6848e47e8fdcbaf8291b45df18731579a220d4bf93dfba5ae204a2fc2b5724e9'),
('chunk-7073','GHBC-CHUNK-007073','GHBC-C-007073','35.17.13
Bracing',35,'35.17','35.17.13','Bracing',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','[]','2c41fd58d103ab4b0483341b64a5832c6f0b7b19c80ef396228f6ce851dcbba6'),
('chunk-7074','GHBC-CHUNK-007074','GHBC-C-007074','35.17.13.1
Except as provided in Article
35.17.13.2 each exterior wall in each storey shall be braced with at least one (1) diagonal brace conforming to Article 35.17.13.3',35,'35.17','35.17.13.1','Except as provided in Article',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026063"]','cf0b3965ff34e732e1b06652b35dafc2b81fa8b077e87535525829b300be774d'),
('chunk-7075','GHBC-CHUNK-007075','GHBC-C-007075','35.17.13.2
Bracing is not required where walls
are clad with panel type sheathing or panel type siding.
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.17','35.17.13.2','Bracing is not required where walls',1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026064","GHBC-REQ-026065"]','43410dfb630108388ac150f07efd52378415803b2da0db4ed94cf78b48858eff'),
('chunk-7076','GHBC-CHUNK-007076','GHBC-C-007076','35.17.13.3
Where bracing is required, it shall consist of at least 25mm by 100mm wood members applied diagonally to the studs at an angle of approximately 45 degrees to the horizontal extending the full height of the wall on each storey.  Such bracing shall be nailed to each stud and wall plate by at least two 63mm nails.',35,'35.17','35.17.13.3',NULL,1371,'["Table 7.17.10. A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026066","GHBC-REQ-026067"]','b9a7059e93f4ddcc6bfdd054445b84ad8c680220d197d66ee34dfc6023aee7b5'),
('chunk-7077','GHBC-CHUNK-007077','GHBC-C-007077','35.18.1Scope',35,'35.18',NULL,NULL,1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026068"]','72644a9404c920e0da81df968b91b91f5c7db205cf454408109c9baf4ad43d0e'),
('chunk-7078','GHBC-CHUNK-007078','GHBC-C-007078','35.18.1.1
This clause applies to wood-frame
construction with the loadbearing framing members spaced more than 600mm apart.',35,'35.18','35.18.1.1','This clause applies to wood-frame',1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026069"]','878f641490a68c4ce297413d35d581e52ed019f8262675f4d00bbde0f7272451'),
('chunk-7079','GHBC-CHUNK-007079','GHBC-C-007079','35.18.2
General',35,'35.18','35.18.2','General',1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','[]','f95fb281162ee22461a5192e2f6040c06d9279780347145c0e91ea74826954be'),
('chunk-7080','GHBC-CHUNK-007080','GHBC-C-007080','35.18.2.1
The size and spacing of posts and beams and the span and thickness of floor decking shall be calculated in conformance with Part 17 of the Code.
35.18.2.2 Requirement for nails, timber, notching and drilling anchorage and sill plates shall conform to Clause 35.17.',35,'35.18','35.18.2.1',NULL,1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026070","GHBC-REQ-026071"]','e79a6fd7a3b38a7737388dcf5210bc681d1d4f086febbbfaef12619c032f0bf0');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7081','GHBC-CHUNK-007081','GHBC-C-007081','35.18.3
Decking',35,'35.18','35.18.3','Decking',1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','[]','f43bb9912fe4d100bb3b093c8597442456b53a61c315f32c8ebfb7037d342b76'),
('chunk-7082','GHBC-CHUNK-007082','GHBC-C-007082','35.18.3.1
Specifications for floor and roof
decking Floor and roof decking shall consist of not less than 50mm timber laid on the flat or edge.',35,'35.18','35.18.3.1','Specifications for floor and roof',1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026072"]','c2b52fdf87be872d22f11548000bdcfd54942c1e1c72d394859204c6abf4cf83'),
('chunk-7083','GHBC-CHUNK-007083','GHBC-C-007083','35.18.3.2
Plank floor decking
Plank floor decking laid on the flat shall be not more than 200mm wide.  Such decking shall be tongued-and-grooved or splined unless a separate underlay is installed or the flooring consists of woodstrips laid at right angles to the decking.',35,'35.18','35.18.3.2','Plank floor decking',1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026073","GHBC-REQ-026074"]','3a74852ea47336ba2521f27387c99c8e594d24d82248a931d814e35331894ba5'),
('chunk-7084','GHBC-CHUNK-007084','GHBC-C-007084','35.18.4
Loadbearing beams',35,'35.18','35.18.4','Loadbearing beams',1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','[]','f53d05e95f497449889302d5d25dd10574301bbb3b4dc78102595491f55cadd5'),
('chunk-7085','GHBC-CHUNK-007085','GHBC-C-007085','35.18.4.1
Loadbearing beams shall be solid, built-up, glued-laminated or plywood web beams.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.1',NULL,1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026075"]','215e2a87f9edae900434b0cc60837faf2f44d9346697cd7b34c6af9f9889a682'),
('chunk-7086','GHBC-CHUNK-007086','GHBC-C-007086','35.18.4.2
Loadbearing roof beams shall be securely connected to the exterior wall framing and the centre loadbearing wall or centre beams to resist adequately the uplift forces due to wind.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.2',NULL,1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026076"]','dbbbb058e94e6e56b01a6519edcde180efde4a8171fb7c94403c95f86e365414'),
('chunk-7087','GHBC-CHUNK-007087','GHBC-C-007087','35.18.4.3
The length of end bearings for loadbearing beams shall be determined on the
basis of allowable design stress of wood but not less than 40mm.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.3',NULL,1371,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026077","GHBC-REQ-026078"]','696373b9706e8d1c0500d586689975ff2166c135fc65f24fa112e41b147e3a0b'),
('chunk-7088','GHBC-CHUNK-007088','GHBC-C-007088','35.18.4.4
When
loadbearing beams are supported by mechanical connectors, the connectors shall be capable of supporting the design loads.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.4','When',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026079"]','f269e8337e073e033e35d6c2a907fcb43745b29900dbb2ab0af5bd7f25b1308c'),
('chunk-7089','GHBC-CHUNK-007089','GHBC-C-007089','35.18.4.5
Where joints in loadbearing beams
do not occur over solid supports, joints shall be designed according to approved practice.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.5','Where joints in loadbearing beams',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026080"]','9ebd5fda312caca373b46558c68e0c6aa880774a28299d98443ab903fe624fc6'),
('chunk-7090','GHBC-CHUNK-007090','GHBC-C-007090','35.18.4.6
Opposing loadbearing beams shall be tied together at the joints by means of splices or suitable mechanical connectors.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.6',NULL,1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026081"]','fedace9ecf2a366027a7a2fb61e31aab9127fb012752841b3b6335bb254eee45');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7091','GHBC-CHUNK-007091','GHBC-C-007091','35.18.4.7
Where secondary framing members
span between floor beams, members and connections shall be designed to support the required design loads.
anchored to the wall plate by not less than 1.2mm thick steel angles or other approved anchors.',35,'35.18','35.18.4.7','Where secondary framing members',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026082","GHBC-REQ-026083"]','17ba90a5770b96be070c423b81eb4fc84a729ba306ae7de55470b10512749de2'),
('chunk-7092','GHBC-CHUNK-007092','GHBC-C-007092','35.18.5.3
Built-up posts
Solid posts and individual members in built-up posts shall extend in one piece the full height of the wall storey.  Built-up members shall be fastened together with nails spaced not more than 300mm centres and at least twice as long as the individual member thickness, or with not less than 10mm diameter bolts fitted with washers and spaced not more than 450mm centres.',35,'35.18','35.18.5.3','Built-up posts',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026084","GHBC-REQ-026085"]','a5c0702d63dfed5e631321ae28d4ffbcffbe45171f7031afdbcbb77df1614c54'),
('chunk-7093','GHBC-CHUNK-007093','GHBC-C-007093','35.18.5.4
Intermediate studs
Intermediate studs or blocking shall be provided between posts in post and beam walls for the support of exterior and interior cladding.  Intermediate studs shall conform to Clause 35.18 for non-loadbearing stud walls.
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.18','35.18.5.4','Intermediate studs',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026086","GHBC-REQ-026087","GHBC-REQ-026088"]','cfa627d4318bf838ef8d741e207804985c1d336bce4aea4569b0bd23138955fb'),
('chunk-7094','GHBC-CHUNK-007094','GHBC-C-007094','35.18.6
Plank frame wall construction',35,'35.18','35.18.6','Plank frame wall construction',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','[]','0b44754a3fb612e0c7e75bb75ac808ece1f86a3750792bd832ada799d165ad6f'),
('chunk-7095','GHBC-CHUNK-007095','GHBC-C-007095','35.18.6.1
Thickness of plank framing in plank
frame walls shall conform to Table 35.18.6A. The unsupported height of 50mm vertical plank non-loadbearing partitions shall not exceed 3.60 m.',35,'35.18','35.18.6.1','Thickness of plank framing in plank',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026089","GHBC-REQ-026090"]','dbc0876f7670dae05cb9dff71b31fc961914e9a72263a91ec60f8647b2b6525b'),
('chunk-7096','GHBC-CHUNK-007096','GHBC-C-007096','35.18.6.2
Vertical framing in plank frame walls
shall consist of not less than 250mm wide planks spaced not more than 2.40m centres.
(Forming Part of Article 35.18.6.1) Nominal thickness of plank framing',35,'35.18','35.18.6.2','Vertical framing in plank frame walls',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026091","GHBC-REQ-026092"]','2a46509b10977a8953583ee50b1ae6be9bdc3862bbf516ab069b1591e200bb79'),
('chunk-7097','GHBC-CHUNK-007097','GHBC-C-007097','35.18.6.3
Vertical framing in plank frame walls
shall not bear on wood members with the grain at right angles to the vertical framing except where bearing on sills.',35,'35.18','35.18.6.3','Vertical framing in plank frame walls',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026093"]','12c67c760e6194f1375bfd05526654d2b85423ff9efb6ac8df97ce71e89f9366'),
('chunk-7098','GHBC-CHUNK-007098','GHBC-C-007098','35.18.6.4
Corners of plank frame walls shall be formed by butting and fastening together the face and edge of two planks.',35,'35.18','35.18.6.4',NULL,1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026094"]','8c04cf50f8eded063aaed76f4c86dd291642cf597e5fc4c7c0bb1d98d127c0f1'),
('chunk-7099','GHBC-CHUNK-007099','GHBC-C-007099','35.18.6.5
Vertical framing in plank frame walls
shall be provided on each side of every opening, except that a window opening more than 750mm in width may be supported on one side only by a vertical member.  In such cases, the opposite jamb of the window or short upright to which it is attached shall bear on the filler wall plank immediately below, which in turn shall be notched into the vertical structural members on each side.',35,'35.18','35.18.6.5','Vertical framing in plank frame walls',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026095","GHBC-REQ-026096"]','a86f7407b4a644e642d71d4e8be9227fda500a3a717f91e5a163b00ab385a07f'),
('chunk-7100','GHBC-CHUNK-007100','GHBC-C-007100','35.18.6.6
Where horizontal planks act as
loadbearing lintels or headers, they shall be
framed into the vertical members by dovetailing so that not less than a 40mm length of bearing is provided.',35,'35.18','35.18.6.6','Where horizontal planks act as',1372,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026097","GHBC-REQ-026098"]','075f1164b55fd905780c73c802e4aee54079e78827a8d7f70aae11f01ea5e38e');
