Openings in loadbearing plank
frame walls shall be bridged with lintels designed to carry superimposed loads to adjacent members.
35.18.6.8 Non-loadbearing horizontal members (fillers) in plank frame walls shall be securely fastened to the vertical framing.',35,'35.18','35.18.6.7','Openings in loadbearing plank',1373,'["Table 35.18.6.A"]','["GHBC-REQ-026099","GHBC-REQ-026100"]','5e0e64d64ea9a4a8957bcc48a5b7e7980093bf9c3c446a81c7faa21c9f776a16'),
('chunk-7102','GHBC-CHUNK-007102','GHBC-C-007102','35.19.1
General',35,'35.19','35.19.1','General',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','e966482f1518310449bdf4b4338aaa8b14b7ca379eac0860adfe076a8371f9fd'),
('chunk-7103','GHBC-CHUNK-007103','GHBC-C-007103','35.19.1.1
Roof protection
Roof shall be protected with roofing, including flashing, installed to shed rain effectively.',35,'35.19','35.19.1.1','Roof protection',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026101"]','1ec411688f8efd1ed14ee3405f8923f57c5f3d237a8a5cdb0d121d52cdf1b606'),
('chunk-7104','GHBC-CHUNK-007104','GHBC-C-007104','35.19.2
Roofing materials',35,'35.19','35.19.2','Roofing materials',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','65e47ed1c8da9b9c0a7d26525969c05fc092a820946e061ac9301e8e85db75a4'),
('chunk-7105','GHBC-CHUNK-007105','GHBC-C-007105','35.19.2.1
Materials specification
Roofing materials shall conform to the
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.19','35.19.2.1','Materials specification',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026102","GHBC-REQ-026103"]','6ddb7a6f846ef46ca87ebaa883d56faf99304e4672cca3609c95e8651b04499d'),
('chunk-7106','GHBC-CHUNK-007106','GHBC-C-007106','35.19.4
Flashing at interclauses',35,'35.19','35.19.4','Flashing at interclauses',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','ee6e45a744f2faa1c719d4b6eb8a4807060872b5fe76411df4b709214af6a775'),
('chunk-7107','GHBC-CHUNK-007107','GHBC-C-007107','35.19.4.1
Sheet metal flashing shall consist of not less than 1.70mm thick sheet lead, 0.33mm galvanized steel, 0.36mm thick copper, 0.46mm thick zinc or 0.48mm thick aluminium.',35,'35.19','35.19.4.1',NULL,1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026104"]','26e7d4e877c17066d747820100873a839efd6e4cf6be69fa5fb132aee1c1888a'),
('chunk-7108','GHBC-CHUNK-007108','GHBC-C-007108','35.19.4.2
Valley flashing
Where sloping surfaces or shingled roofs intersect to form a valley, the valley shall be flashed.',35,'35.19','35.19.4.2','Valley flashing',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026105"]','0c4904a07125c87190bcb507dac30b93d3289bc8f6b7715265bb1f405e8b5db6'),
('chunk-7109','GHBC-CHUNK-007109','GHBC-C-007109','35.19.4.3
Open valley flashing
Open valleys shall be flashed with not less than one layer of sheet metal not less than 600mm wide.
(Forming part of Article 35.19.3.1) Roofing types and slope limits of roofs
top of the valley or 125mm of the bottom of the valley measured from the centerline of the valley.',35,'35.19','35.19.4.3','Open valley flashing',1373,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026106","GHBC-REQ-026107","GHBC-REQ-026108"]','2cf858d4a923447360efabbb1c22127370b26c8661e1e74aaf7cfbf1e09c4f44'),
('chunk-7110','GHBC-CHUNK-007110','GHBC-C-007110','35.19.4.5
Interclause flashing
The interclause of shingle roofs and masonry walls or chimneys shall be protected with flashing.  Counter flashing embedded not less than 25mm in the masonry shall extend not less than 150mm down the masonry and lap the lower flashing not less than 100mm. Flashing along the slopes of a roof shall be stepped so that there is not less than 75mm head lap in both the lower flashing and counter flashing.  Where the roof slopes upwards from the masonry, the flashing shall extend up the roof slope to a point equal in height to the flashing on the masonry, but not less than 1½ times the shingle exposure.',35,'35.19','35.19.4.5','Interclause flashing',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026109","GHBC-REQ-026110","GHBC-REQ-026111","GHBC-REQ-026112"]','6c525f6ac666efe0c6cb9bf6f2a91f57e9b228da5a03168ed6095eee86c31812');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7111','GHBC-CHUNK-007111','GHBC-C-007111','35.19.5
Wood roof shingles',35,'35.19','35.19.5','Wood roof shingles',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','adbfe01696f041bfdbaf25055faf1af981595f850a7d253511145f9154e04935'),
('chunk-7112','GHBC-CHUNK-007112','GHBC-C-007112','35.19.5.1
Decking
Decking for wood shingled roofs may be continuous or spaced.',35,'35.19','35.19.5.1','Decking',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026113"]','f723a39e5da60c9358361ee1168cc81a873bec1945f13ccffaca1e487141a074'),
('chunk-7113','GHBC-CHUNK-007113','GHBC-C-007113','35.19.5.2
Size
Wood shingles shall be not less than 400mm long and less than 75mm nor more than 350mm wide.',35,'35.19','35.19.5.2','Size',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026114"]','b12996b4864eaa76c44b33640ae2f46db5a051707a7c4e6add968dee1a50f358'),
('chunk-7114','GHBC-CHUNK-007114','GHBC-C-007114','35.19.5.3
Spacing
Shingles shall be spaced approximately 6mm The exposure of wood roof shingles shall conform to Table 35.19.5A
(Forming part of Articles 35.19.5.5) Exposure of wood roof shingles
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.19','35.19.5.3','Spacing',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026115","GHBC-REQ-026116","GHBC-REQ-026117"]','1bd7c8929981417cd117d3cb94dc6df8039d044dd0b243dbfcef450ac830de7d'),
('chunk-7115','GHBC-CHUNK-007115','GHBC-C-007115','35.19.5.6
Flashing
Flashing shall conform to this Code.',35,'35.19','35.19.5.6','Flashing',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026118"]','dd141e5caed552c92d53c7d36b853d3a3728c8cdcc9a9b65ceabebc46bf97edc'),
('chunk-7116','GHBC-CHUNK-007116','GHBC-C-007116','35.19.6
Handsplit roof shakes',35,'35.19','35.19.6','Handsplit roof shakes',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','83f604a6fa16b50c91f078a5eee8729c0e2c052233274d798a3116dd5a1c4fa7'),
('chunk-7117','GHBC-CHUNK-007117','GHBC-C-007117','35.19.6.1
Size of shakes
Shakes shall be not less than 450mm long and less than 100mm not more than 350mm wide with a butt thickness of not more than 30mm.',35,'35.19','35.19.6.1','Size of shakes',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026119"]','50bd87d39b970cfc5ddb6999eb75d14be6a7c4a8a048200e4a8951af7b95f4a8'),
('chunk-7118','GHBC-CHUNK-007118','GHBC-C-007118','35.19.6.2
Spacing of shakes
Shakes shall be spaced approximately 6mm apart and offset at the joints in adjacent courses not less than 40mm so that joints in alternate courses are staggered.',35,'35.19','35.19.6.2','Spacing of shakes',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026120"]','6cf07415d475565f417f718dabec8bbe87403ea89c319853e794d60c0c0079f3'),
('chunk-7119','GHBC-CHUNK-007119','GHBC-C-007119','35.19.6.3
Fastening of shakes
Shakes shall be fastened with nails located approximately 20mm from the side of the shakes and 40mm above the exposure line.',35,'35.19','35.19.6.3','Fastening of shakes',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026121"]','7b29e458d4242681b55408493f0841b605e28a3aa916ef99b2b2ab8052b707b1'),
('chunk-7120','GHBC-CHUNK-007120','GHBC-C-007120','35.19.6.4
Exposure of shakes
The exposure of wood shakes shall conform to
(Forming part of Article 35.19.6.4) Exposure of handsplit wood shakes',35,'35.19','35.19.6.4','Exposure of shakes',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026122","GHBC-REQ-026123"]','97406e749ef06d63989b3e41943147dcf4c22ea0411229fd63af8202e5c55ae3');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7121','GHBC-CHUNK-007121','GHBC-C-007121','35.19.6.5
Flashing
Flashing shall conform to Subclause 35.19.4
35.20 INTERIOR WALL AND CEILING FINISHES
assembly is required to provide a certain fireresistance, a flame-spread rating or a sound transmission class rating, the wall or ceiling finishing shall be subject to the appropriate requirements in this Code.',35,'35.19','35.19.6.5','Flashing',1374,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026124","GHBC-REQ-026125","GHBC-REQ-026126"]','dd5d27c5479a537f1a9fa0fa6918c84f1fa49608f4fcde3e7756040e3660fbff'),
('chunk-7122','GHBC-CHUNK-007122','GHBC-C-007122','35.20.2
Waterproof wall finish',35,'35.19','35.20.2','Waterproof wall finish',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','73f3e4408d7cac4e26b5da1ce5daff73a5831e57ade484461d087438442430f3'),
('chunk-7123','GHBC-CHUNK-007123','GHBC-C-007123','35.20.2.1
Waterproofing of interior finishes
Waterproof finish shall be provided to a height of not less than 1.8m above the floor in shower stalls, 1.2m above the rims of bathtubs equipped with showers and 400mm above the rims of bathtubs not equipped with showers.',35,'35.19','35.20.2.1','Waterproofing of interior finishes',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026127"]','0d78b521dcd69b569d4ba24632f2cefef1d36fb2461edf29f3869da387804aa6'),
('chunk-7124','GHBC-CHUNK-007124','GHBC-C-007124','35.20.2.2
Waterproof finish
Waterproof finish shall consist of granite, marble, ceramic, plastic or metal tile, sheet vinyl or linoleum etc.',35,'35.19','35.20.2.2','Waterproof finish',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026128"]','7141726335f6f9a0eaf8bb9122d9cfa4c26e8b76cf8db189160c07c6f9b57adb'),
('chunk-7125','GHBC-CHUNK-007125','GHBC-C-007125','35.20.3
Plywood finish',35,'35.19','35.20.3','Plywood finish',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','b2dc9c6d6ec7b58002758ee929ebf68377476eed8ad8f98d2f6063de98a5697c'),
('chunk-7126','GHBC-CHUNK-007126','GHBC-C-007126','35.20.3.1
Plywood finish thickness
The minimum thickness of plywood interior finish shall conform to Table 35.20.3A except that no minimum thickness is required when the plywood is applied over solid backing.
(Forming part of Article 35.20.3.1) Minimum thickness of plywood interior finish',35,'35.19','35.20.3.1','Plywood finish thickness',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026129","GHBC-REQ-026130"]','41634d0c02ad6fefba9531174ab543822ab34d988770dc2a5fdd4552bac01318'),
('chunk-7127','GHBC-CHUNK-007127','GHBC-C-007127','35.20.3.2
Where plywood for interior finish is
grooved, the grooves shall not extend through the face ply and into the plies below the face ply unless the groove is supported by framing or furring, or if the grain of the face ply is at right angles to supporting members, unless the thickness of the plywood exceeds the value shown in Table 35.20.3A by an amount equal to at least the depth of penetration of the grooves into the plies below the face ply.
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.19','35.20.3.2','Where plywood for interior finish is',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026131","GHBC-REQ-026132"]','9fecd44e02eff2665253bdb7d3da8ac6b44ee9304f4f509c04c62b95c55155a2'),
('chunk-7128','GHBC-CHUNK-007128','GHBC-C-007128','35.20.3.3
Nails for plywood finish
Nails for attaching plywood finishes shall be not less than 38mm casing or finishing nails spaced not more than 150mm centres along edge supports and 300mm centres along intermediate supports, except that staples providing equivalent lateral resistance may also be used.',35,'35.19','35.20.3.3','Nails for plywood finish',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026133"]','3255b3aac9e0d2617f900d32ee4352c9839a4d9829bb2e7873e6e9b6005a49ee'),
('chunk-7129','GHBC-CHUNK-007129','GHBC-C-007129','35.20.3.4
All plywood edges shall be supported by furring, blocking or framing.',35,'35.19','35.20.3.4',NULL,1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026134"]','13a3db0d5c9ad65d05bfd47856151411876581e85bcbbf0ab8fff3338b4f6bf0'),
('chunk-7130','GHBC-CHUNK-007130','GHBC-C-007130','35.20.4
Wall tile',35,'35.19','35.20.4','Wall tile',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','1513f973ce958de14946ab2a314d2255b07b47fca558dd7461da43db2fdf19fe');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7131','GHBC-CHUNK-007131','GHBC-C-007131','35.20.4.1
Wall tile base and adhesive
Ceramic tile shall be set in a mortar base or applied with adhesive. Plastic tile shall be applied with an adhesive.',35,'35.19','35.20.4.1','Wall tile base and adhesive',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026135","GHBC-REQ-026136"]','c5130c849867f5122a8b7c859f3b5134d66b7713decfdfe59c70e7c8d4f47bcf'),
('chunk-7132','GHBC-CHUNK-007132','GHBC-C-007132','35.20.4.2
Mortar for ceramic tile
When ceramic tile is applied to a mortar base the cementitious material shall consist of one part Portland cement to not more than ¼ part of lime or clay pozzolana by volume.  This shall be mixed with not less than three nor more than five parts of sand per part of cementitious material by volume. Ceramic tile applied to a mortar base shall be thoroughly soaked and pressed into place forcing the mortar into the joints while the tile is wet.',35,'35.19','35.20.4.2','Mortar for ceramic tile',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026137","GHBC-REQ-026138","GHBC-REQ-026139"]','8879217da08b9277855a2fc7c0644a55917251e3549ffef6e9d054281dc6c5f0'),
('chunk-7133','GHBC-CHUNK-007133','GHBC-C-007133','35.20.4.3
Adhesive for ceramic tile
Adhesives to attach ceramic or plastic tile shall be applied to the finish coat or brown coat of plaster that has been steel-trowelled to an even surface or to masonry provided the concrete, terrazzo, ceramic or other types of flooring providing similar degrees of water resistance.',35,'35.19','35.20.4.3','Adhesive for ceramic tile',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026140"]','0c62ee75ac89cfd35ef022230f896789bc59067d355702166ba0d577d8901998'),
('chunk-7134','GHBC-CHUNK-007134','GHBC-C-007134','35.21.1.3
Wood sleeper
Wood sleepers supporting finished flooring over a concrete base on ground shall be not less than 25mm by 50mm and shall be treated with a soaking coat of approved wood preservative.',35,'35.19','35.21.1.3','Wood sleeper',1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026141"]','fe588700caf3c3e98fc0b2d7e00a141c64318cf4ca84ed7f8a242e4e0d75cefa'),
('chunk-7135','GHBC-CHUNK-007135','GHBC-C-007135','35.21.1.4
Finished flooring shall have a surface that is smooth, even and free from roughness or open defects.
(Forming part of Articles 35.21.2.1) Wood strip flooring',35,'35.19','35.21.1.4',NULL,1375,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026142","GHBC-REQ-026143"]','8fb69690407bb39c389e859eeb48e14257c89b4f22c70efab7311cc433f9bc98'),
('chunk-7136','GHBC-CHUNK-007136','GHBC-C-007136','35.21.2.2
Underlay
Wood strip flooring shall not be laid parallel to lumber sub-flooring unless a separate underlay is provided.',35,'35.19','35.21.2.2','Underlay',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026144"]','1d974d066308c6b18c5f3c902aeba0a28dec04ca4b257f3924e40815370435c4'),
('chunk-7137','GHBC-CHUNK-007137','GHBC-C-007137','35.21.2.3
Laying of wood strip flooring
If wood strip flooring is applied without a subfloor, it shall be laid at right angles to the joists so that end joists are staggered and occur over supports or are end matched. It shall be laid so that no two adjoining strips break joints in the same space between supports and each strip bears on no fewer than two supports.',35,'35.19','35.21.2.3','Laying of wood strip flooring',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026145","GHBC-REQ-026146"]','78076105e6065b26c5089204f747318167f82ce6b770de81cbad03feaf367165'),
('chunk-7138','GHBC-CHUNK-007138','GHBC-C-007138','35.21.2.4
Nailing
Wood strip flooring shall be toe nailed or face nailed with at least 1 nail per strip at spacings shown in Table 35.21.2B except that face nailed strips of more than 25mm in width shall have no fewer than two nails per strip. Face nails shall be countersunk and the holes filled with suitable filler.
(Forming part of Article 35.21.2.4) Nailing Of Wood Strip Flooring
DGS 1207: 2018',35,'35.19','35.21.2.4','Nailing',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026147","GHBC-REQ-026148","GHBC-REQ-026149","GHBC-REQ-026150"]','f5697d69656e915fb24dde41c9021cbb070bd911021225503d8b4b44b7937f38'),
('chunk-7139','GHBC-CHUNK-007139','GHBC-C-007139','35.21.3
Parquet flooring',35,'35.19','35.21.3','Parquet flooring',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','ed6b044b7ae0677cf4e453fd8d06753de34e7705883f5af4b37e79e6aeeb682a'),
('chunk-7140','GHBC-CHUNK-007140','GHBC-C-007140','35.21.3.1
Adhesive used to attach parquet
block flooring shall be suitable for bonding',35,'35.19','35.21.3.1','Adhesive used to attach parquet',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026151"]','055c2652b9109d09aa1cc22f55ef877585de028a7aeb25c691836d5c2b838244');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "chunks" ("id", "chunk_id", "clause_id", "text", "part", "section", "clause", "title", "page", "tables_json", "requirement_ids_json", "source_hash") VALUES ('chunk-7141','GHBC-CHUNK-007141','GHBC-C-007141','35.22.1.1
This clause applies to the facilities
required in plumbing systems within dwelling units. Plumbing and plumbing systems will generally conform to this Code.',35,'35.19','35.22.1.1','This clause applies to the facilities',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026152","GHBC-REQ-026153"]','242e2a8299258ec80956044f09b1300c7b9edee776d3d6dc39b855d5759d4430'),
('chunk-7142','GHBC-CHUNK-007142','GHBC-C-007142','35.22.1.2
Facilities in plumbing systems other
than those required in dwelling units shall conform to Part 3 of this Code.',35,'35.19','35.22.1.2','Facilities in plumbing systems other',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026154"]','3f61786f4c24142f2e18ccf6e029d876f5b4e9395cac2bbd1b7ac9e48faaa305'),
('chunk-7143','GHBC-CHUNK-007143','GHBC-C-007143','35.22.2
Water supply and distribution',35,'35.19','35.22.2','Water supply and distribution',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','489b6904846371b4deb41785d234d9c03428f5eda21a83adaeac17ecb01cd0b7'),
('chunk-7144','GHBC-CHUNK-007144','GHBC-C-007144','35.22.2.1
Portable water
Every dwelling unit shall be supplied with portable water from an approved public or community system when these systems are available.',35,'35.19','35.22.2.1','Portable water',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026155"]','9591caa476b65716931e069bfeb61bf9106dd5852f30486e8e09a1c44c763ff6'),
('chunk-7145','GHBC-CHUNK-007145','GHBC-C-007145','35.22.2.2
Piping facilities
Where a piped water supply is available, piping for cold water shall be connected to every kitchen sink, bathtub, shower and laundry area.  Piping for cold water shall be run to every water closet and hose bib.',35,'35.19','35.22.2.2','Piping facilities',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026156","GHBC-REQ-026157"]','1388c211b5e486ded6cfba2fdf21c3aed71ae74aef5bf58bf4535a21bdb2407f'),
('chunk-7146','GHBC-CHUNK-007146','GHBC-C-007146','35.22.3
Required facilities',35,'35.19','35.22.3','Required facilities',1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','[]','e4a8891ba17ef9d82766bb207257b81b2104e44893a8728204f8675137dde2e3'),
('chunk-7147','GHBC-CHUNK-007147','GHBC-C-007147','35.22.3.1
A kitchen sink, lavatory bathtub and water closet shall be provided for every
supply other approved means of waste disposal shall be provided for every dwelling unit.',35,'35.19','35.22.3.1',NULL,1376,'["Table 35.19.3A","Table 35.19.5A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.19.6A","Table 35.20.3A","Table 35.21.2.1","Table 35.21.2B"]','["GHBC-REQ-026158","GHBC-REQ-026159"]','4bf184aadb92aee9f6582b8eda9574907714bcece73e7036ba6ccff94eb3f48e'),
('chunk-7148','GHBC-CHUNK-007148','GHBC-C-007148','35.22.4
